window.FWN_DIMENSIONAL_KEEPER_ALL_MY_SKILLS_ARE_AT_LEVEL_100_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_DIMENSIONAL_KEEPER_ALL_MY_SKILLS_ARE_AT_LEVEL_100_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2001,"title":"Chapter 2001: Ten Void Sealing Art!","paragraphs":["The Unholy Trinity Body had already proved its value many times.","Without it, Max doubted his body could safely hold so many bloodlines, legacies, laws, flames, domains, and divine powers at the same time.","His Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline, Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline, Voidwalker bloodline, Dimensional Keeper Legacy, Emotion Severing Path, Divine King Punishment, Devouring Flames, Primordial Flames, Dimension of Soul, Dimension of Light, and five Divine Veins should have clashed with one another long ago.","Yet somehow, his body had endured everything.","The Chaos Tree, however, remained more mysterious.","It gathered laws.","It grew branches from powers.","It produced fruits.","But Max felt there had to be something deeper behind it.","As he stared at the massive tree, a thought suddenly entered his mind.","\"Since the Chaos Tree is filled with laws, maybe its true purpose will only appear when I enter the Divine Lord Realm in the future.\"","The more he thought about it, the more reasonable it seemed.","The Law Manifestation Realm allowed laws to appear outside the body and influence reality. The Divine Lord Realm, however, was a far higher stage.","Perhaps only when Max’s control over laws reached that level would the Chaos Tree reveal its true nature. Perhaps the tree was not only meant to produce Chaos Fruits. Perhaps it was meant to become the foundation of something much larger.","A law world.","A divine domain.","Or perhaps even something connected to the true path of the Unholy Trinity Body.","Max could not be sure.","For now, all he could do was make the best use of what he already had.","He looked at the towering Chaos Tree for a long moment before slowly exhaling.","\"I hope my guess is right.\"","The Chaos Tree swayed gently in the silent dimension, its enormous branches moving as if answering him, but no clear response came.","Max did not mind.","One day, he would understand what it truly was.","For now, he still had one day before the meeting with the devils, and he intended to use every moment of that time to understand his new strength.","With that thought, Max stopped looking at the Chaos Tree and shifted his attention to something else.","\"It is time to fully digest the Primordial Bloodline and the Voidwalker Bloodline,\" Max muttered.","He had awakened both bloodlines only recently, and because one event had followed another without pause, he had not gotten enough time to properly understand their true potential.","The Voidwalker inheritance had entered his body in the inheritance chamber of the Voidwalker Clan, and the Primordial Bloodline ability had awakened inside the training facility of the Primordial Race.","Both powers were now part of him, but possessing a power and mastering it were two completely different things.","Now that he had entered the Dimension of Time, he finally had enough space and time to examine them properly.","\"First, the Voidwalker Bloodline,\" Max muttered.","The moment he said those words, blue glowing rings appeared around both of his hands.","There were five rings around each hand, making a total of ten.","The rings floated around his wrists to his shoulders with quiet precision. They were not ordinary rings made of metal or energy. Each one looked like a condensed circle of folded space, with a deep blue glow flowing along its edge. Within the center of each ring, Max could faintly see layers of darkness rotating inward, as if each ring contained a tiny sealed void.","The Voidwalker Clan, one of the original Five Sacred Clans, specialized in sealing. Their bloodline was not built for simple movement through space alone. It was also designed to lock, isolate, separate, imprison, and suppress.","Among the many arts stored inside the Voidwalker inheritance, the strongest technique was the Ten Void Sealing Art.","Ten Void Sealing Art.","According to the inheritance, a member of the Voidwalker Clan could form ten void rings and use them to seal almost anything.","A weapon, an attack, a person, a law, a domain, a space, and even a path could be sealed if the user had enough strength and understanding. However, the rings were not limited to sealing alone. Sealing was their greatest specialty, but it was not their only function.","Max willed the rings to move.","The ten void rings slipped away from his hands and floated in the air around him. They moved silently, circling his body like obedient stars. Their motion was smooth and natural, as if they were not separate tools but extensions of his bloodline.","Max then took out Dragonheart and tossed it into the air.","At the same time, he controlled one of the void rings.","The ring flew toward Dragonheart.","The moment it came close to the sword, the ring expanded slightly and released a blue transparent sphere. The sphere wrapped around Dragonheart in an instant, and the sword was sealed inside it before becoming suspended in the air.","It did not fall. It did not tremble. It simply floated there, locked inside the blue sphere as if it had been removed from normal space.","Max’s eyes lit up slightly.","\"This is interesting.\"","He could feel that his connection to Dragonheart had been cut off.","It was not a permanent severing, but it was a true isolation. The sword was still in front of him, yet for that brief moment, it felt as though it existed in a different layer of space. If someone else’s weapon, attack, or treasure were trapped inside such a seal during battle, that person’s control over it would likely be disturbed or even completely broken.","Max waved his hand, and the seal loosened.","Dragonheart returned to him.","Then Max looked at the remaining void rings.","\"Now, let us test the other uses.\"","One of the void rings floated back to his right wrist and settled there.","Max stretched his right hand through the ring.","Then he calmed his breathing and directed the power of his black flames into it.","The blue ring trembled.","Slowly, its glow changed.","The bright blue color darkened until the entire void ring became pitch black. Wisps of black flame appeared along its edges, but they did not spread outward. Instead, they were pulled inward again and again by the spatial compression of the ring.","The black flames, which were usually wild and devouring, became increasingly concentrated until their aura grew far denser than before.","Max looked at the ring with sharp interest.","The void ring was not only holding the flames.","It was compressing them."]},{"number":2002,"title":"Chapter 2002: True Use of the Ten Rings!","paragraphs":["After a few moments, Max clenched his fist and slammed it into the ground.","Boom!","A violent wave of black flames erupted from his fist and spread outward.","The flames were far more concentrated than before. Their devouring power became sharper, heavier, and more explosive. The impact caused the Dimension of Time to tremble faintly, and for a moment, the surrounding space rippled from the force of the release.","Max looked at his fist in surprise.","\"This is good.\"","The second use of the void rings was compression.","He could incorporate different elements or powers into the rings, and the rings would compress those powers to an extreme degree. Once released, the result would be far stronger than simply attacking directly with the same energy.","For someone like Max, who controlled many elements, bloodline powers, divine abilities, and pseudo cosmic paths, this function was terrifyingly useful.","He could use the void rings as amplifiers.","He could use them as seals.","He could use them as storage points for attacks.","He could even prepare different powers in different rings and release them during battle with almost no delay.","Max’s eyes became brighter.","Then he willed the black flames to disperse and began guiding the power of the seven-colored lightning into the void ring on his wrist.","The ring trembled more violently this time.","The seven-colored lightning came from Divine King Punishment, one of Max’s strongest powers. It carried judgment, destruction, punishment, and heavenly authority. The moment it entered the void ring, lightning flickered wildly in every direction, as if it refused to be restrained.","However, the void ring did not break.","It continued compressing the lightning.","Blue turned into seven colors.","The ring around Max’s wrist became a radiant circle of lightning, with arcs of seven-colored thunder snapping from its edges. The aura inside the ring grew more and more violent, and even Max felt a dangerous pressure forming around his hand.","\"This is...\"","Max stared at the ring in shock.","\"This is deadly.\"","He could clearly feel that the compressed seven-colored lightning stored inside the void ring was far more violent than the black flames had been.","The black flames were terrifying because they devoured and corroded, but this lightning was different. It did not only destroy. It judged. It punished. It descended like a sentence from a divine law that allowed no resistance.","If he released the lightning from the void ring, the devastation would far exceed the previous black flame attack.","In terms of raw explosive destruction, the black flames could not compare to this compressed Divine King Punishment lightning.","Max looked down at the white floor of the Dimension of Time.","\"This is dangerous,\" he muttered. \"But I do not think my Dimension of Time is so easy to damage.\"","With that, he clenched his fist again.","Then he slammed it into the ground.","Boom!","A surge of seven-colored lightning exploded outward in all directions.","The force was far more terrifying than Max expected. The concentrated lightning struck the white floor, spread across the ground like a divine punishment net, and released a violent roar that shook the Dimension of Time.","For a moment, the clean white tiles beneath him turned black, as if they had been scorched by a power too fierce to be endured.","Then, only a few breaths later, the black marks faded.","The tiles returned to their original white color.","Max exhaled slowly.","\"If this had been the real world, that attack would have destroyed everything around me.\"","There was excitement in his eyes.","The Ten Void Sealing Art was even more useful than he had first imagined. With this art, he could increase the strength of his existing attacks without needing to create entirely new techniques from scratch.","More importantly, the void rings gave him flexibility. He could store, compress, release, seal, and combine different powers depending on the situation.","However, in Max’s opinion, this was still not the most important use of the void rings.","He raised his hand.","All ten void rings began glowing as they floated around him.","A moment later, one void ring released the aura of his Emotion Severing Path. The space inside the ring became pale and sharp, as if an invisible blade had formed there.","Another void ring released seven-colored lightning in every direction, carrying the overwhelming aura of Divine King Punishment. A third void ring became darker and hotter as it carried the force of the Devouring Flames Domain.","These were his three pseudo cosmic paths.","Emotion Severing Path.","Divine King Punishment.","Devouring Flames Domain.","Max watched the rings carefully.","Then a smile slowly appeared on his face.","\"So it is true.\"","The smile grew slightly wider.","\"The void rings can carry pseudo cosmic paths and even cosmic paths.\"","When he first received the Voidwalker Bloodline inheritance, Max had been shocked to see this recorded inside the Ten Void Sealing Art.","According to the inheritance, the highest use of the void rings was not merely sealing objects or compressing elemental power. Their true value lay in their ability to temporarily carry a user’s cosmic path.","A true master of the Voidwalker Clan could place a cosmic path into a void ring, move it independently, use it to seal an enemy’s law, release it as an attack, or combine multiple rings to form a terrifying cosmic path formation.","At that time, Max had been skeptical.","A cosmic path was not like ordinary energy.","Even a pseudo cosmic path was the result of extreme comprehension, personal will, and the transformation of law into something far more profound. Carrying such a thing inside a ring sounded almost impossible.","But now, three of his void rings were carrying the aura of his three pseudo cosmic paths.","Only after seeing it with his own eyes did Max understand the true potential of the Ten Void Sealing Art.","His eyes became deep.","If one void ring could carry Emotion Severing Path, another could carry Divine King Punishment, and another could carry Devouring Flames Domain, then what would happen if he used all ten rings together in battle?","What if he placed black flames in one, Primordial Flames in another, seven-colored lightning in another, dimensional force in another, and a pseudo cosmic path in each of the remaining rings?","What if he formed a sealing formation with all ten?","What if he trapped an enemy inside that formation and released all the compressed powers at once?","Max’s smile became dangerous.","The Ten Void Sealing Art was not merely a defensive sealing art.","In his hands, it could become his greatest killing art."]},{"number":2003,"title":"Chapter 2003: Practice","paragraphs":["Max continued practicing the Ten Void Sealing Art for hundreds of hours inside the Dimension of Time.","At first, the ten void rings moved around him like powerful but unfamiliar tools. They obeyed his will, but the response wasn’t perfect. Sometimes a ring lagged half a breath behind what he wanted. Sometimes the energy compressed inside a ring became unstable. Sometimes the sealing sphere formed too loose, and other times it locked so tight that even Max had to put in extra effort just to release it.","But with time, that awkwardness faded away.","One hour became ten. Ten hours became a hundred. After hundreds of hours of repeated practice, Max finally pushed the Ten Void Sealing Art to its current limit.","Now the ten void rings no longer felt like separate constructs built from his bloodline. They felt like part of his own body. With a single thought, he could summon them around his wrists, shoulders, feet, or even behind him in a rotating formation. With another thought, he could scatter them across a battlefield, hide them inside space, or attach them to an enemy’s attack before sealing it away entirely.","The more he practiced, the more Max understood why the Voidwalker Clan had once stood among the Five Sacred Clans. Their sealing arts weren’t simple restraints. They controlled distance. They controlled separation. They decided whether something stayed connected to the world or got cut off from it completely. That kind of power was terrifying.","After mastering the Ten Void Sealing Art as far as he currently could, Max also discovered that awakening the Voidwalker Bloodline had given him a lot of passive benefits beyond just the ability to form void rings or use inheritance arts. His entire body had changed in a subtle but powerful way.","Seals were now far less effective against him. Not just his body, but his blood, soul, limbs, senses, and energy circulation had all become extremely hard to seal. Ordinary sealing formations could no longer lock down his movement easily. Restraining techniques built on space, law chains, bloodline pressure, or energy isolation would lose most of their bite against him too. Unless whoever used the seal belonged to the Voidwalker Clan or carried a sealing path far above his own level, most seals would struggle to actually hold him.","Even the sealing power inside the Legacy Arena of the Four Sacred Clans wouldn’t be nearly as dangerous to him anymore.","That realization made Max’s eyes deepen. The Voidwalker Clan had been known for sealing since the age of the Five Sacred Clans. It made sense that their bloodline didn’t only let them seal others. A clan specialized in sealing would naturally build up resistance to seals too. Their bodies, bloodlines, and souls had evolved to understand exactly how seals worked, and that understanding made them extremely hard to imprison.","In a way, this passive effect might turn out even more useful than some of his direct attacks. After all, Max had plenty of enemies. Some would try to kill him. Some would try to capture him. Some would try to seal him away. Now, at least that last option had gotten a lot harder for them.","Once he finished going through the Voidwalker Bloodline, Max shifted his attention to the Primordial Bloodline.","Compared to the Voidwalker Bloodline, the Primordial Bloodline felt mysterious in a different way. It wasn’t as direct as the ten void rings. It didn’t hand him a complete inheritance art with obvious use cases. It felt broader, deeper, and far more fundamental, almost like it existed beneath all his other laws rather than sitting beside them.","Max sat cross-legged and activated the Primordial Bloodline. A deep golden aura spread through his body. The eye between his brows opened slowly, and the ancient symbols inside it rotated like a circle of dawn. The moment the eye opened, the laws around Max became clearer. Flame, lightning, space, light, darkness, ice, wind, soul, and every other law he’d touched seemed to draw closer to him.","Still, Max frowned slightly.","\"Aside from feeling closer to all these different laws, I don’t notice much else changing,\" he muttered. \"Even when I activate the Primordial Bloodline, it mostly just feels like my Pseudo Cosmic Paths and elemental attacks get ten times stronger. Other than that, it doesn’t feel as extraordinary as I expected.\"","That thought left him a bit confused. The Primordial Race was the strongest race in the Divine Realm, and probably the strongest in the entire universe. Their bloodline was the origin of human strength, and among every tier of Primordial Bloodline out there, Max carried the highest one, the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline.","A bloodline at that level shouldn’t be simple. Yet to Max, its effects still felt strangely hidden. It strengthened him a lot, sure. It brought him closer to the laws and multiplied the power of his paths and elements. It also let him awaken Primordial Flames. But compared to how mysterious the Primordials were supposed to be, Max felt like he’d only scratched the surface.","\"I’ll need to ask Sarvion or one of the Primordials about this later,\" Max muttered.","He was sure there was more to the Primordial Bloodline than what he currently grasped. Maybe the problem wasn’t the bloodline. Maybe it was him. He’d only received the bloodline recently and hadn’t gotten a proper explanation of how Primordials actually used it. He was treating it like just another power stacked onto his body, but maybe the Primordial Bloodline needed to be understood as a foundation that transformed all his other powers rather than as a separate ability on its own.","Either way, thinking about it without guidance wouldn’t give him answers right away. So Max stopped dwelling on it and started practicing with the Primordial Flames instead.","The golden flame appeared above his palm the moment the eye between his brows opened. It burned quietly, pure and ancient, without the wild hunger of his black flames. Max controlled it carefully at first, shaping it into threads, blades, spheres, waves, and thin layers that wrapped his fists. The more he practiced, the more he understood its nature."]},{"number":2004,"title":"Chapter 2004: More Pseudo Cosmic Paths!","paragraphs":["Primordial Flames didn’t simply burn. They refined, purified and returned things to a more original state.","When Max used black flames, the result was violent and direct. The black flames devoured energy, corroded defenses, consumed vitality, and turned everything they touched into fuel. But the Primordial Flames worked differently.","They burned through impurities. They weakened corruption. They refined unstable energy. They even sharpened Max’s own understanding of law when he used them with restraint.","For enemies, that purity could turn terrifying. A defense built on unstable laws might get refined until it collapsed. A devil’s corrupted power might get purified until its foundation cracked.","A bloodline curse might burn away from the inside. Even a strong body could be attacked not by destroying it outright, but by burning away the hidden flaws holding its strength together.","After long practice, Max’s grasp of the Primordial Flames deepened rapidly. Eventually, he created another Pseudo Cosmic Path from them. The moment the new path took shape, the golden flame above his palm turned sharper and more profound. It no longer felt like just a bloodline ability. It became a road, a direction, a law that Max himself had started to comprehend.","Primordial Flame Path. It was still only a Pseudo Cosmic Path, but its potential ran deep.","Once that was done, Max didn’t stop. He still had time. Over the next few years inside the Dimension of Time, he focused on building Pseudo Cosmic Paths for his Ice Element and Light Element.","Before, he hadn’t been able to do this because his mastery over these two elements hadn’t gone deep enough. He could use ice and light, but using an element and walking it toward a Pseudo Cosmic Path were two completely different things. Forming a Pseudo Cosmic Path meant understanding the deeper nature, law structure, battle application, and conceptual direction of that power. Max’s mastery hadn’t reached that level before.","Now, with the Primordial Bloodline, everything had changed. The moment he focused on ice, he felt like he’d been close to it for years. He could feel the stillness inside cold, the way motion slowed down, the freezing of energy, and how ice could preserve, imprison, and destroy all at once. The element no longer felt like something he had to force himself to use. It felt natural.","The same thing happened with light. When Max studied the Light Element, he could sense its speed, purity, warmth, illumination, and judgment. It wasn’t the same as the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, but the two resonated with each other. His Primordial Bloodline made that resonance clearer, letting him understand the Light Element not just as a force of brightness, but as a law that revealed, purified, accelerated, and pierced.","Because of that, Max successfully built Pseudo Cosmic Paths for both ice and light.","\"I see,\" Max muttered once he’d finished. \"The Primordial Bloodline massively boosts my mastery over elements.\"","His eyes turned thoughtful. \"Even for elements where I haven’t unlocked a dimension yet, I still feel a lot closer to them.\"","This gave him a clearer picture of the Primordial Bloodline. Maybe its greatest strength wasn’t some single obvious ability. Maybe its real value sat in comprehension itself. It pulled him closer to the laws, made elements feel natural, strengthened his Pseudo Cosmic Paths, and let him understand powers that should have taken years of study.","To other cultivators, forming a Pseudo Cosmic Path was an enormous challenge. To Max, the Primordial Bloodline made the whole process smoother, faster, and more instinctive.","That was terrifying in its own way.","After finishing the Pseudo Cosmic Paths for Primordial Flames, Ice, and Light, Max still had a few hours left. He spent the rest of the time practicing his sword arts and thinking through the Emotion Severing Path.","Dragonheart appeared in his hand, and Max moved through the Saint Order Sword Art again and again. Each swing came out calm, precise, and controlled. He wasn’t chasing his strongest attack. Instead, he focused on feeling the edge hidden inside emotion, the line between attachment and detachment, the moment when killing intent became unnecessary because the blade itself had already cut through the heart’s disturbance.","Among all his Pseudo Cosmic Paths, the Emotion Severing Path felt closest to becoming a true Cosmic Path. Divine King Punishment was powerful, but it still needed more comprehension. The Devouring Flames Domain was terrifying, but its path leaned too heavily on destruction and hunger. The Primordial Flame Path had great potential, but it had only just come together. Ice and Light were also brand new.","Emotion Severing Path was different. It had followed Max through several dangerous battles. It had sharpened his will, changed his attacks, and let him cut through things ordinary force couldn’t touch. Every time he used it, he felt like he was standing closer to the boundary between a Pseudo Cosmic Path and a true one.","\"I feel like out of all my Pseudo Cosmic Paths, Emotion Severing is closest to becoming the real thing,\" Max muttered.","His gaze settled into calm. \"It’s only a matter of time.\"","With that, he kept practicing. Dragonheart moved through the air in smooth arcs, and the Saint Order Sword Art carried the invisible sharpness of the Emotion Severing Path with every strike. The Dimension of Time stayed silent around him, but with each swing, the space ahead of him seemed to lose something intangible.","Anger. Fear. Desire. Attachment.","For those final hours, Max forgot about the devils, the Primordials, the Five Sacred Clans, the sacred legacy, and even the warning about Anover. He focused only on his sword. He focused only on the path. And slowly, the edge of Emotion Severing grew sharper.","***","On the day of the meeting with the devils, the entire Divine Realm seemed to hold its breath.","It wasn’t that the countless worlds, planets, forces, clans, empires, and ancient forces of the Divine Realm had actually stopped moving.","Cities kept running. Merchants kept traveling. Cultivators kept training. Starships still crossed the void, and formation gates still opened from one region to another. Yet beneath all that ordinary movement, a strange tension had spread across the realm like an invisible storm."]},{"number":2005,"title":"Chapter 2005: Stage Was Set!","paragraphs":["People with ordinary status didn’t know the full truth, but even they could sense that something had changed. The sky above many major worlds felt heavier. The elders of powerful forces had suddenly withdrawn from public view. Ancient formations that hadn’t lit up in countless years began glowing quietly in hidden places.","Patrols around important star realms increased. The great families put their celebrations on hold. The forces called their wandering disciples back home. Even a few old monsters who’d been in seclusion for thousands of years opened their eyes after getting secret messages from their forces.","The Divine Realm was vast, but news traveled fast among those standing near its peak.","Devils had entered their universe. That single fact alone was enough to leave countless ancient powers on edge.","The meeting took place inside the grand council domain of the Primordial Race. This wasn’t just some hall. It was an enormous sacred meeting ground built inside the Primordial Ancestral Domain, surrounded by floating mountains, golden law rivers, and countless ancient symbols drifting slowly across the sky like living stars.","At the center stood a vast circular platform made of bronze-gold stone, and above it hovered a rotating star map showing the layout of the Divine Realm, the Mortal Realm beneath it, and the distant boundary where the Wall of Eternity stood.","The aura in the meeting place felt so heavy that even space itself seemed more solid than usual.","The Primordials sat in the highest seats. The four Primarchs sat at the front, their expressions calm, though the pressure surrounding them made it clear none of them were taking this meeting lightly. Behind them stood other powerful Primordial experts, each one carrying an ancient aura that made them look like living pillars of the universe itself.","Beyond the Primordial Race, many of the strongest first-rate forces in the Divine Realm had shown up too.","The War God Palace stood on one side, their experts dressed in battle robes and ancient armor. Their leader’s aura came off fierce and straightforward, like a weapon sharpened through countless wars. Even standing quietly, the warriors behind him carried a frightening battle intent, like they were ready to march into war the second an order came down.","Beside them stood the representatives of the Sword God Palace. Compared to the War God Palace, their group looked far quieter, but the sharpness surrounding them felt even more suffocating. Their robes moved gently without any wind, and sword intent flowed around them like an invisible river. Several of their elders looked calm on the surface, but Max could feel that each of them was like a sheathed divine sword waiting to be drawn.","The Nine Star Court had also arrived. Their experts wore dark blue robes marked with star patterns, and nine radiant stars floated behind their leading elder like a small constellation. Their presence felt mysterious and profound, carrying traces of destiny, star law, and heavenly calculation.","The Stellar Templar stood not far off, their armor shining with silver light. Unlike the War God Palace, they carried a colder, more disciplined presence. They looked like witches of a sacred order, every movement measured and every gaze filled with solemn vigilance.","The Lunarian Kingdom had sent its royal delegation as well. Their people wore moon-white robes and silver crowns, and their leader carried an elegant, unreadable aura. A faint moon shadow hovered above their group, casting a gentle glow that somehow made the surrounding space feel colder and quieter.","The Grand Void Sanctum stood in a section where space itself seemed to bend. Their experts stayed half-hidden inside layers of darkness and folded void. Some looked clear for a moment and blurred the next, as if they weren’t fully standing in the same space as everyone else.","Ascension Hall had come too. Their representatives looked solemn and dignified, with ancient scrolls, law tablets, and golden seals floating behind them. They were known for managing many of the Divine Realm’s great ascension records and ancient trials, and their presence here alone showed how serious the situation had gotten.","Then there were the Four Sacred Clans.","Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest had all come with their leaders, elders, and selected descendants. Their expressions were also solemn. Even though a lot had happened in the Four Sacred Clans due to Max and Freya, they still chose to attend the meeting. They knew not to let their personal matters change what matters the most.","Their four sacred ancestors were present too, standing above their respective clans with solemn faces. Every so often, their gazes drifted toward Max.","They weren’t the only ones watching him.","Beside the Primordials stood the ten new geniuses who’d received the Primordial Bloodline. Max stood among them with a calm expression.","Revona stood quietly not far from him, her posture relaxed, her eyes deep and unreadable. Damian’s face stayed cold as he looked over the gathered first-rate forces. Ervin looked thoughtful, like he was trying to work out the meaning behind every arrangement in the meeting ground.","Morgana glanced around with a faint sneer, though even she kept her mouth shut in a place like this. Kaiden stood beside Revona, his expression steady. Orion looked far less carefree than usual, while Rosaline, Rakan, Aurelian, and the rest all carried different shades of seriousness.","They’d only been given one week. One week to awaken their Primordial Bloodline abilities. One week to digest the truth about the devils. One week to prepare for a meeting involving forces standing at the very peak of the Divine Realm.","For Max, that week had stretched much longer thanks to the Dimension of Time, but even he could feel that today’s atmosphere was different from any battle or trial he’d faced before. This wasn’t an arena where strength alone decided everything. This was a meeting where words could decide whether the Divine Realm slid into war, compromise, delay, or disaster.","His gaze swept across the gathered forces. War God Palace. Sword God Palace. Nine Star Court. Stellar Templar. Lunarian Kingdom. Grand Void Sanctum. Ascension Hall. Four Sacred Clans. Primordial Race. Each of these forces could shake countless worlds with a single command. Yet today, all of them had gathered in one place because a small group of devils had shown up in their universe.","That alone said everything about how terrifying the devil race really was."]},{"number":2006,"title":"Chapter 2006: Arrival of the Devils!","paragraphs":["The wait for the Devil Race didn’t last long.","Only a few minutes had passed since the major forces of the Divine Realm gathered inside the grand council domain of the Primordial Race, yet the atmosphere already felt heavy enough to crush weaker cultivators.","The four Primarchs stood at the center of the meeting ground, surrounded by the leaders of the strongest first-rate forces, the Four Sacred Clans, and the newly awakened Primordial geniuses. No one spoke casually.","Even those who hated waiting understood that this meeting would decide whether the Divine Realm gained time to prepare or took another step toward a universe-shaking war.","Then the sky changed.","The golden clouds above the council domain slowly parted. A dark crack appeared between them. Black mist poured out of that crack, and the pure primordial light in the air dimmed, as if a stain had spread across the heavens.","The temperature dropped sharply. The laws around the meeting ground twisted for a moment, and a cruel pressure came down from above.","The devils had arrived.","There were only around ten of them, but their presence alone tensed up the entire council domain. Each devil stood tall and powerful, covered in ancient tattoos that resembled Infernal Demon Tattoos, only deeper and more vicious.","Their horns glowed with dark crimson light, and the markings across their bodies seemed to pulse like living symbols. They hovered above the meeting ground as if they hadn’t stepped into enemy territory, but had come to inspect a place that would soon belong to them.","At their front stood Varok.","He looked young, handsome, and cruel. His skin was pale with a faint gray tone, his eyes were dark red, and the tattoos running from his horns down to his neck and hands made him look both elegant and savage.","He was the son of Devil Emperor Abaddon, but his expression carried none of the caution an envoy should have. He looked down at the gathered forces of the Divine Realm with a faint smile, as if the Primordials, sacred clans, palace masters, kingdom rulers, and ancient leaders below weren’t worth being nervous about.","\"You’ve put together quite the grand welcome for me,\" Varok said.","His voice spread through the sky.","The four Primarchs rose from their seats at the same time and appeared in the air in front of the devils.","Arvantos stood among them, his expression calm and unreadable. Beside him stood the other three Primarchs, and their presence alone made the pressure in the sky much heavier.","The first was Primarch Eryndor, a tall man with bronze-gold skin, long dark hair, and eyes that burned like molten stars. His aura felt thick, ancient, and overwhelming, like a living mountain built from the first bones of the universe.","Among the four Primarchs, he gave off the most direct physical pressure, and every breath he took made space tremble faintly.","The second was Primarch Lysandra, a woman dressed in flowing silver-gold robes. Her hair was pale as moonlight, and countless tiny law runes moved around her like fireflies. Her aura came off calm, but it carried terrifying depth, as if she could see through energy, soul, bloodline, and fate with a single glance.","The third was Primarch Veyrion, a cold-faced man whose eyes seemed to hold a rotating starfield. His body didn’t release much pressure openly, but the space around him bent naturally, making him feel distant even while standing right there.","Compared to Eryndor’s overwhelming force and Lysandra’s profound mystery, Veyrion felt like someone who could make entire star realms disappear without changing his expression.","Arvantos stood slightly ahead of them. He’d already spoken with Max and the others before, but now, facing Varok and the Devil Race, his aura felt completely different. He no longer looked like an elder teaching younger geniuses. He looked like one of the pillars holding up the universe.","Behind the four Primarchs, the leaders of the top first-rate forces rose into the air too.","The War God Palace Master, Garron Aresvale, stood with both arms crossed, his body wrapped in dark battle armor that looked forged from the bones of ancient battlefields. His eyes were sharp and wild, and even before he said a word, his battle intent made it clear he’d rather crush the devils than negotiate with them.","Beside him stood the Sword God Palace Master, Celian Voss, a calm man in white sword robes. He carried no visible sword, yet the air around him was filled with sword intent so sharp that even the darkness released by the devils seemed to split apart before it could touch him.","The Nine Star Court was represented by High Lord Astren Vale, an old man with nine small stars rotating behind him. His eyes were deep and calculating, and his fingers moved slowly, as if he were measuring hidden changes in fate.","The Stellar Templar stood behind Grand Marshal Seraphis Kael, whose silver armor shone with cold starlight. His presence felt disciplined and solemn, carrying the air of someone who’d commanded countless wars without ever letting emotion cloud his judgment.","The Lunarian Kingdom’s delegation was led by Queen Selene Lunaris, a beautiful woman with moon-white hair and a silver crown. She stood beneath a faint lunar shadow, her expression gentle, though her eyes stayed clear and distant, like a cold moon watching worlds rise and fall.","The Grand Void Sanctum’s master, Lord Vael Noxis, appeared half-hidden inside folded darkness. His figure blurred at the edges, and sometimes he looked close while his aura felt thousands of miles away.","Ascension Hall was led by Hall Master Orin Caldus, a dignified man with ancient scrolls and golden law tablets floating behind him. His expression stayed grave, and his eyes never left Varok.","The Four Sacred Clans had also sent their leaders and ancestors. Valerius burned with sacred solar light. Ashbourne carried blood-iron battle force. Ravenhart stood in shadowed silence. Evercrest controlled the surrounding space through hidden roots and sealed domains.","Even though the recent matter involving the Voidwalker Clan hadn’t been settled, none of them dared show any internal conflict in front of the devils.","Below them, Max and the other nine geniuses stood near the Primordial side. They weren’t seated among the leaders, but their position let them hear every word clearly. The meeting hadn’t been kept from them.","Arvantos had said it was time they learned the truth, and clearly that also meant they were allowed to listen to the negotiations that would shape the direction of the coming storm.","Max looked up at Varok in silence. He’d already heard that Varok carried the Pearl of Abyss. Because of that, the Primordials couldn’t simply kill or seal him without risking consequences no one could predict. Still, watching the young devil stand above the council domain with such arrogance made Max’s eyes turn colder."]},{"number":2007,"title":"Chapter 2007: Terms and Conditions!","paragraphs":["Varok looked at the four Primarchs, then at the leaders standing behind them. A sneer crossed his face.","\"I didn’t expect this meeting to bring in so many insects,\" he said. \"But since you’ve dragged out so many ants to watch, I won’t complain.\"","The expressions of many leaders turned cold at once.","The War God Palace Master gave a low laugh, and the sound carried real violence in it. The Sword God Palace Master’s eyes narrowed slightly. Several elders of the Four Sacred Clans let out faint killing intent, but the four Primarchs stayed calm.","Varok spread his hands. \"Since you’ve gathered everyone, let’s begin.\" His smile faded, and his voice sharpened. \"I don’t enjoy wasting time. Have you decided whether you’ll accept my conditions, or would you rather have war instead?\"","The council domain fell silent.","Varok continued before anyone could answer. \"My condition is simple. I’ll establish a force of my own in the Divine Realm. This force will be independent. No Primordial, sacred clan, or any force in the Divine Realm will suppress it, monitor it openly, restrict its normal movement, or interfere with its affairs without cause.\"","His gaze moved across the leaders one by one. \"My people will be allowed to enter the Divine Realm, trade, cultivate, recruit, and build our foundation here. As long as we don’t start slaughtering your people, you won’t move against us. In exchange, I won’t push for immediate war.\"","A cold silence followed. Even though everyone had already heard the general condition from Arvantos, hearing Varok say it so openly still made the air feel suffocating.","Letting devils establish a force inside the Divine Realm wasn’t a small concession. It was like letting poison into the bloodstream and hoping it wouldn’t spread.","Arvantos looked at Varok calmly. \"We’re willing to accept a modified version of your condition.\"","Varok’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"Modified?\"","Primarch Eryndor stepped forward, his voice deep enough to shake the sky. \"You may establish a force in the Divine Realm, but it won’t be free from consequences. If any devil gets caught harming the human race, forcibly corrupting cultivators, slaughtering innocent people, devouring worlds, damaging star realms, or using devil power to secretly control the forces of the Divine Realm, all terms will be broken.\"","Primarch Lysandra continued in a calm but cold voice. \"If that happens, every protection granted to your people will disappear. Any devil involved will be killed. Any devil force connected to the crime will be destroyed. If your newly established faction shelters the offender, the entire faction will be wiped out.\"","Varok’s expression darkened. \"You dare threaten to kill devils after agreeing to negotiate?\"","Before the Primarchs could respond, Garron Aresvale, the War God Palace Master, laughed with open contempt.","\"Seems like you’ve misunderstood something, devil brat.\"","Varok turned slowly toward him.","Garron’s sneer deepened. \"This is the Divine Realm, not your devil universe. You’re not standing in your father’s court, and the people here aren’t your subjects. If any devil gets caught doing something suspicious, we’ll kill them without mercy. If you want to call that a threat, go ahead and call it a threat.\"","The devils behind Varok let their killing intent loose all at once.","Garron’s battle aura exploded in response, turning the air around him into a roaring battlefield.","\"Try it,\" he said coldly.","The atmosphere nearly broke.","Then Arvantos raised one hand. The pressure from both sides stopped before it could fully erupt.","Varok’s face had gone much darker. He stared at Garron for a long moment, then looked back at the four Primarchs.","\"You expect me to accept a condition where any random force can accuse my people and kill them?\"","Primarch Veyrion spoke for the first time. His voice was quiet, but it reached everyone clearly. \"No. We’ll set up a judgment system. If a devil gets accused, the matter will be investigated by representatives from the Primordial Race and at least three top first-rate forces. But if a devil gets caught in the act, the nearest force has full authority to kill them immediately.\"","Varok’s eyes flashed with cold light.","Lysandra added, \"There’s another condition.\"","Varok looked at her. \"Go on.\"","\"The devils are prohibited from entering the Mortal Realm.\"","The moment she said it, Max’s eyes sharpened slightly, and the other geniuses grew more serious too.","The Mortal Realm was far weaker than the Divine Realm. If devils gained access to it, the fallout would be disastrous. Countless worlds wouldn’t be able to resist even a small group of devils.","Lysandra’s voice stayed calm. \"Any attempt to open a passage toward the Mortal Realm, contact forces there, spread devil power there, establish hidden shrines there, or carry out suspicious activity connected to it will count as a violation of the agreement. If a violation happens, the devils involved will be killed.\"","Arvantos added, \"And if your force is connected to it, your force will be destroyed.\"","Varok’s expression turned colder. \"You people have a lot of rules for a side that claims it doesn’t want war.\"","Celian Voss, the Sword God Palace Master, spoke softly. \"Rules are the only reason this meeting hasn’t already turned into slaughter.\"","The air turned colder again.","High Lord Astren Vale of the Nine Star Court then said, \"There’s another matter. If our geniuses run into devils outside the universe in future battlefields, trials, ruins, or neutral spaces, your people must not target them with killing intent, assassination attempts, soul corruption, or bloodline curses.\"","Varok looked at him with a faint sneer. \"You want me to control every devil beyond this universe?\"","Astren’s eyes stayed calm. \"You’re the one asking to establish a force here. If you want privileges inside our Divine Realm, you should restrain your race elsewhere too.\"","Varok laughed coldly. \"I can control the devils who fall under my banner in this universe. I can’t control every devil in the devil universe, and I can’t control those acting outside my authority. If your geniuses run into devils beyond this universe, their survival will depend on their own strength.\"","Damian’s face turned cold hearing that.","Orion clenched his fists.","Morgana sneered softly. \"So they want safety here but won’t offer any out there.\"","Revona stayed silent, but her eyes had turned sharper.","Max watched Varok carefully. He understood exactly what Varok’s words meant. The devils wanted their people protected inside the Divine Realm, but they refused to guarantee the safety of Divine Realm geniuses outside the universe.","That wasn’t surprising. This negotiation wasn’t about fairness. It was about leverage.","Grand Marshal Seraphis Kael of the Stellar Templar said coldly, \"Then your people in the Divine Realm won’t get absolute protection either. If they stir up hatred, they’ll face the consequences.\"","Queen Selene Lunaris added in a gentle but firm voice, \"Your force can exist, but it can’t recruit any people of the Divine Realm. If any people of the Divine Realm were to join your force, they will be declared a traitor and be killed immediately\"","Lord Vael Noxis of the Grand Void Sanctum spoke from within the folded darkness. \"Your force will also be forbidden from building secret spatial passages without registering them. Any hidden passage we find will be destroyed immediately.\"","Hall Master Orin Caldus of Ascension Hall said, \"Your members will be recorded. Their identities, cultivation, aura signatures, and movements between major regions have to be registered. Call it a restriction if you want, but without it, there’s no agreement.\"","Varok’s face grew darker with every added condition. The devils behind him looked furious, but none of them moved.","They clearly understood that despite their arrogance, they stood deep inside the Primordial Ancestral Domain, surrounded by the strongest forces of the Divine Realm. If not for Varok’s identity and the Pearl of Abyss, they wouldn’t have dared stand here so boldly."]},{"number":2008,"title":"Chapter 2008: Max’s Exposing the Hole in the Agreement!","paragraphs":["Varok’s voice turned icy. \"You want to accept my condition while tying my hands and feet.\"","Arvantos replied calmly, \"You want to enter our Divine Realm while expecting us to trust the Devil Race. Neither side gets everything it wants.\"","Varok stared at him. Arvantos stared back. For a long moment, the entire council domain hung frozen between war and compromise.","Neither side was willing to fully back down. Varok refused to drop his demand to establish a devil force in the Divine Realm.","The Primordials and the leaders of the Divine Realm refused to accept any agreement that handed the devils unrestricted freedom. Both sides knew the flaws in the other’s position, and both sides knew starting a war right now would be dangerous.","The devils had too few people inside the universe to win a direct war at this point. The Divine Realm couldn’t kill Varok casually because of Abaddon and the Pearl of Abyss. That balance forced both sides to keep talking.","The argument dragged on for a long time. Conditions got added, rejected, altered, and narrowed down.","The devils demanded independence. The Divine Realm demanded restrictions. The devils demanded freedom of movement. The Divine Realm demanded registration.","The devils demanded no suppression. The Divine Realm demanded the right to retaliate if harm was done. The devils refused to take responsibility for devils beyond the universe. The Divine Realm refused to offer them complete protection inside it.","In the end, both sides compromised. The devils would be allowed to establish a force in the Divine Realm, but only within a designated star region chosen by the Primordials and approved by the major forces.","Their members would be registered. Their movements would be monitored in limited ways. They’d be forbidden from entering the Mortal Realm, building secret passages, committing slaughter, spreading forced corruption, enslaving cultivators, or interfering with existing forces through hidden means.","If they broke these conditions, the Divine Realm would have the right to kill the offenders. If the violation was severe enough, the whole agreement would be considered broken.","Varok’s expression stayed dark after the terms were settled, but a faint smile still crept onto his lips.","Max noticed it. So did Revona. So did several of the older leaders. No matter how many restrictions had been piled on them, the devils had still won something important.","They’d gained a foothold. For the first time since the ancient war, the Devil Race would be allowed to build a force inside the Divine Realm, inside another universe.","Even watched, even restricted, even surrounded by conditions from the Divine Realm’s leaders, the result stayed the same. The devils had entered their universe. And now they’d be allowed to stay.","Varok looked down at the council domain and smiled faintly. \"Good. Let this be the start of a more peaceful relationship between our races.\"","No one believed him.","The meeting had avoided immediate war. But deep down, everyone knew this wasn’t peace. It was only the first move of something far more dangerous.","Just as Varok’s faint smile appeared, Max stepped forward from among the ten geniuses. The movement wasn’t big, but in that suffocating council domain, it pulled countless gazes toward him at once.","The leaders of the Divine Realm looked over. The Four Sacred Clans narrowed their eyes. The devils behind Varok stared at him with cold amusement, while the other nine geniuses showed different reactions.","Orion’s eyes widened slightly, Damian turned serious, Ervin frowned like he’d guessed something coming, and Revona’s gaze sharpened with rare interest.","Max stopped beneath the floating star map and looked up at Varok.","\"Your agreement has a flaw,\" he said.","The council domain went silent.","Varok slowly lowered his gaze, his dark red eyes fixing on Max. A faint sneer crossed his face. \"And who are you supposed to be?\"","Max didn’t flinch. \"Someone who can see the hole in your words.\"","Several devils immediately let their killing intent loose. The pressure came down toward Max like a black tide, but before the Primarchs or any of the leaders could react, Max’s middle eye opened between his brows. A pure golden flame appeared inside it.","Primordial Flames.","The black killing intent closing in on him burned away silently before it ever touched his body. It didn’t scatter. It got refined into nothing with a calm purity that made several devils’ expressions shift.","Even Varok’s eyes narrowed.","The four Primarchs glanced at Max at the same time. Arvantos’s expression stayed calm, but a faint light passed through his eyes.","Max looked directly at Varok and continued, \"You said the devils under your banner in this universe will follow the agreement, but you also said you can’t control devils beyond this universe. That means any devil can act outside your so-called authority, attack our geniuses in neutral spaces, corrupt our people beyond the Wall of Eternity, and then claim they were never your responsibility.\"","Varok’s smile faded slightly.","Max’s voice turned colder. \"That’s not a loophole. That’s a prepared escape route.\"","The expressions of many leaders shifted. High Lord Astren Vale of the Nine Star Court looked at Max with a trace of approval. Grand Marshal Seraphis Kael crossed his arms, his cold eyes fixed on Varok. The Sword God Palace Master, Celian Voss, gave a faint nod, while Garron Aresvale of the War God Palace laughed under his breath.","Varok stared at Max and sneered. \"You talk boldly for someone standing behind his elders.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"You talk boldly for someone hiding behind his father’s name and a Primal Treasure.\"","The sky turned cold. The devils behind Varok nearly erupted on the spot.","Varok’s face went completely dark. \"Human, do you want to die?\"","Max immediately took a defensive stance. This time, the aura around him changed. Ten blue void rings appeared around his body, rotating from his wrists to his shoulders, each carrying a different kind of pressure.","One held a pale invisible sharpness that made emotions tremble. One flickered with seven-colored lightning. One burned with black devouring flames. One released the pure golden heat of Primordial Flames. The remaining rings carried folded space, light, ice, soul force, dragon aura, and deep Voidwalker sealing power.","Max couldn’t be sure when a devil would sneak attack him and so even though he was standing with leaders of the Divine Realm, he was still cautious.","For the first time, the devils looked at Max seriously.","Varok’s gaze locked onto the void rings. \"What are you?\"","Max answered calmly, \"The person who’ll kill your people if they cross the line.\""]},{"number":2009,"title":"Chapter 2009: Max’s One Condition!","paragraphs":["The council domain went deadly silent.","The four sacred ancestors looked at Max with complicated expressions. They’d seen him fight. They’d seen him awaken the fifth end. They’d seen him break through to the Law Manifestation Realm and shake the Five Sacred Clan domain.","But now, standing in front of Varok and speaking on behalf of the Divine Realm’s younger generation, Max no longer looked like a reckless genius who’d stumbled into ancient secrets.","He looked like someone stepping into his role.","Arvantos watched him for a moment, then spoke. \"Continue.\"","That single word shocked a lot of people. A Primarch had just given Max permission to speak at this meeting.","Varok’s eyes turned colder.","Max looked around at the gathered leaders, then turned back to Varok. \"The Divine Realm should add another condition. Any devil force established here must accept a blood-oath boundary. If a devil outside this universe harms a recognized genius, envoy, or protected representative of our universe under orders from Varok, Abaddon, or any devil faction connected to the force established here, the agreement will be considered broken.\"","Varok sneered. \"And how will you prove orders were given?\"","Max replied, \"Through soul traces, bloodline residue, contract marks, memory inspection, fate calculation, and testimony from neutral forces if the incident happens beyond the Wall of Eternity.\"","The Nine Star Court’s High Lord Astren Vale smiled faintly. \"That’s doable.\"","The Ravenhart ancestor narrowed her eyes. \"Difficult, but doable.\"","Lord Vael Noxis of the Grand Void Sanctum said from within the folded darkness, \"If the devil force established here leaves a registered authority mark on its members, connection traces can be tracked.\"","Hall Master Orin Caldus of Ascension Hall nodded. \"Ascension Hall can record the recognized geniuses and envoys. Anyone under official protection will have their status sealed into the agreement.\"","Varok’s face darkened further.","Max continued, \"There’s another condition too.\"","Arvantos looked at him with interest.","Varok’s voice turned icy. \"You’re adding a lot of conditions for someone still at the Law Manifestation Realm.\"","Max ignored the jab. \"The Divine Realm should form an enforcement team made up of the ten new Primordial geniuses and representatives from the top first-rate forces. If devils break the agreement in places where elders can’t act openly, this team will have the right to investigate, suppress, and kill the offenders.\"","The ten geniuses reacted at once. Orion’s eyes widened before a grin slowly spread across his face. Damian’s expression sharpened. Ervin looked surprised, then thoughtful. Morgana’s lips curled with interest.","Kaiden glanced at Revona, while Revona looked at Max like she was seeing him in a new light. Rosaline, Rakan, and Aurelian all turned serious.","The War God Palace Master laughed loudly. \"Good. Very good. Since the devils want to plant a force in our Divine Realm, our younger generation should have a blade pointed at their throats too.\"","Queen Selene Lunaris spoke gently. \"It would also stop the devils from blaming every conflict on overbearing elders.\"","Celian Voss said calmly, \"If their younger devils can move freely around the Divine Realm, our young geniuses should be able to respond in kind.\"","Varok’s eyes burned with anger. \"You want to build a hunting group for my people and call it enforcement?\"","Max looked at him calmly. \"You want to build a devil force in our universe and call it peace.\"","For a moment, no one spoke. Then Garron Aresvale laughed again, his battle intent shaking the air. \"I like this kid.\"","Arvantos looked toward the other three Primarchs.","Eryndor nodded. \"The proposal has merit.\"","Lysandra’s eyes moved across the devils. \"It also gives the younger generation real experience before the greater war arrives.\"","Veyrion said quietly, \"And it puts pressure on the devil force without forcing immediate conflict.\"","Arvantos turned back to Varok. \"This condition will be added. The ten new Primordial geniuses along with the geniuses from the Four Sacred Clan will form the core of a special enforcement group. They won’t attack devils without reason, but if your people violate the agreement, they’ll have the authority to act.\"","Varok’s expression turned ugly. The devils behind him glared at Max with undisguised killing intent.","Max didn’t look away. He knew this move would make him a target, but he didn’t care. The devils had already entered their universe. If they were allowed to move around freely while everyone politely waited for disaster to strike, the Divine Realm would only be giving them time to spread their roots.","Someone needed to watch them. Someone needed to act without getting held back by the older generation’s hesitation. And if there was one thing Max was good at, it was turning danger into growth.","Varok stared at him for a long time. Then his lips slowly curved again, though this time the smile carried real malice.","\"Fine,\" he said. \"Add your little enforcement group.\"","His gaze stayed locked on Max. \"But remember this, human. Once you take on a role like that, you’re no longer just a genius standing behind the Primordials. You become part of the game.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"I was already part of it the moment your people entered our universe.\"","Varok’s eyes flashed.","Arvantos raised his hand, and the newly added terms sealed themselves into the agreement through a massive golden law scroll that appeared above the council domain. One by one, the conditions lit up across its surface.","The devil force would be restricted to a designated star region. Their members would be registered. They were forbidden from entering the Mortal Realm. They couldn’t build hidden passages. They couldn’t enslave, corrupt, or slaughter people of the Divine Realm. They couldn’t secretly control local forces.","Any violation would allow retaliation. Any confirmed connection to attacks on official geniuses or envoys beyond the universe would also count as a breach.","And finally, the special enforcement group would be formed, with Max and the other nine new Primordial geniuses at its core.","The moment that final condition appeared, many gazes turned toward Max. The leaders of the Divine Realm now saw him differently.","The Four Sacred Clans looked at him with even more complicated emotions. The other geniuses realized their own role had shifted from future hope to active blade. And the devils committed his face to memory.","Varok finally looked away from Max and placed his palm against the golden law scroll. The Pearl of Abyss flickered faintly beneath his sleeve, letting out a dark pulse.","Arvantos placed his palm against the scroll too.","The agreement was sealed.","The devils had won the right to build a force inside the Divine Realm. But because of Max, they hadn’t gotten a free path to spread without consequences.","Then one of the devils standing beside Varok suddenly leaned in and whispered something into his ear.","\"I see,\" Varok sneered as he looked at Max again. \"No wonder you’re so confident talking to me. Turns out you’re the strongest young genius in this universe.\"","He added, \"But has the Primordial Universe fallen so far that its strongest genius is only at the 1st level of the Law Manifestation Realm? I haven’t heard anything this funny in a while.\""]},{"number":2010,"title":"Chapter 2010: Provocation for a battle?!","paragraphs":["Varok’s gaze moved across the young geniuses standing near the Primordial side.","His dark red eyes lingered on Damian, Ervin, Revona, Morgana, Kaiden, Orion, Rosaline, Rakan, Aurelian, and the rest. Most of them had already stepped into the 1st level of the Divine Lord Realm.","Their auras were young, fierce, and unstable in places from their recent Primordial Bloodline awakenings, but their realms were undeniable. They weren’t ordinary geniuses anymore. They’d turned into young monsters carrying the future of the Divine Realm on their shoulders.","Then Varok’s gaze finally landed back on Max. A faint sneer slowly crossed his face.","\"I’ll admit, the other young geniuses of your universe aren’t bad,\" Varok said, his voice carrying across the council domain. \"All of them sit at the 1st level of the Divine Lord Realm. At the very least, they look like people your universe might reasonably pin some hope on.\"","His smile turned colder.","\"But him?\"","Varok’s eyes fixed on Max with open mockery.","\"How can the so-called strongest young genius of your universe only be at the 1st level of the Law Manifestation Realm? Is this some kind of joke?\"","The moment those words fell, the atmosphere shifted. Several of the Divine Realm’s leaders frowned. The young geniuses turned cold too.","Orion’s grin disappeared. Damian’s eyes sharpened with faint killing intent. Ervin’s expression turned serious, while Morgana’s lips curled in displeasure. Even Revona, who’d stayed calm through most of the meeting, looked at Varok with a colder gaze.","They all knew Max’s realm sat lower than theirs. But none of them thought he was weak. He had defeated every single one of them at one entirely lower realm than them.","Max had only recently stepped into the Law Manifestation Realm, but you couldn’t judge his foundation by realm alone.","Before Max could say anything, a cold voice came from the War God Palace side.","Saint Reiner, who’d been sitting silently among the senior figures of the War God Palace, finally spoke.","\"You talk too much for someone hiding behind a few devils.\"","Many eyes turned toward him.","Saint Reiner rose slowly from his seat. He was an old man with long silver hair, a weathered face, and eyes that looked like they’d witnessed countless battlefields. His body wasn’t large, but the moment he stood, an ancient and terrifying war intent spread through the council domain.","It wasn’t the sharp, reckless aura of a young warrior. It was the heavy pressure of someone who’d survived endless wars and personally walked through mountains of corpses.","The armor covering his body was dark gold and crimson, marked with countless scars. Every mark carried the weight of a battle that had once shaken the heavens.","In the War God Palace, the title of Saint wasn’t handed to ordinary geniuses or promising juniors. It was a position reserved for beings who stood at the same level as the palace master, or possessed strength that could surpass that seat.","Saint Reiner was one of the oldest and most powerful figures in the War God Palace, a legendary presence who’d once fought beside Garron Aresvale and had even guided him during his early years.","To Max, Saint Reiner was more than just an ancient powerhouse. He was also a teacher to him. Max had personally inherited everything Saint Reiner knew about the Seven Divine Veins, so in a way, Max counted as his student.","Now Saint Reiner looked at Varok with undisguised contempt.","\"You’re looking down on a Primordial at the 1st level of the Law Manifestation Realm,\" Saint Reiner said, his voice calm but heavy, \"yet he’s more than enough to handle a few devils at the same realm.\"","His words instantly drew attention from both sides.","The War God Palace Master, Garron Aresvale, didn’t stop him. Instead, he leaned back with a fierce smile. He clearly understood what Saint Reiner was doing. The old saint wasn’t speaking out of arrogance. He was deliberately pushing the devils to reveal how far they were willing to go.","The War God Palace had never been the kind of force that stayed quiet when insulted. If the devils wanted to test the Divine Realm’s courage, the War God Palace would never be the first to back down.","Varok looked at Saint Reiner. For a moment, he said nothing. Then a cunning light flashed through his eyes. The mockery on his face deepened, but it no longer looked like simple arrogance.","\"Oh?\"","Varok’s gaze shifted from Saint Reiner to Max and back again.","\"So you actually believe this Primordial trash at the 1st level of the Law Manifestation Realm can handle devils at the same realm?\"","The word trash made the air turn colder at once.","Max’s expression didn’t change, though he had a feeling something interesting was about to happen.","Saint Reiner’s eyes narrowed. He’d immediately caught Varok’s trap. The devil was trying to twist his words and drag Max into the center of the confrontation. Saint Reiner hadn’t meant to push Max into a reckless fight. He’d only wanted to remind the devils that the Divine Realm wasn’t short on powerful warriors.","But Varok had seized the opening.","Varok smiled. \"Then how about this.\"","His voice grew louder, spreading across the entire council domain.","\"I’ll send one devil from my side at the 5th level of the Law Manifestation Realm. Let him fight this Primordial.\" He looked at Saint Reiner with a provocative smile. \"You said he’s more than enough to handle a few Law Manifestation Realm devils. Then surely a single devil at the 5th level won’t be too much, right?\"","Saint Reiner’s expression darkened. His gaze shifted to Max. For the first time, a trace of concern crossed his ancient eyes. He knew Max’s strength better than most people here, but he also knew how dangerous it was to fight a devil from a higher realm.","Max had only recently entered the Law Manifestation Realm, and even if his combat power outstripped his cultivation, the gap between the 1st and 5th levels was still huge.","The moment Varok mentioned the 5th level of the Law Manifestation Realm, plenty of people caught his intent. He wasn’t just trying to humiliate Max. He was trying to use Max’s lower realm as a weapon against the Divine Realm’s confidence.","If Max refused, Varok would mock him as an overhyped reputation manufactured by the Primordials and the top forces. If Max accepted and lost, the devils would use the win to crush the momentum of the Divine Realm’s younger generation before the agreement had even fully settled.","The timing was malicious. The method was crude, but it worked.","Varok turned toward the four Primarchs. \"What do you say? Since your side seems so confident, surely you wouldn’t object to a simple exchange between juniors.\"","The entire council domain went silent. The leaders of the top first-rate forces looked toward the four Primarchs.","Arvantos’s expression stayed calm. Eryndor’s molten-star eyes glowed faintly. Lysandra looked at Max as if she were measuring something inside him. Veyrion’s starfield-like gaze stayed unreadable.","For a moment, none of them spoke. Then Arvantos said, \"We have no objection.\"","Varok’s smile widened slightly.","Eryndor added in a deep voice, \"A fight between juniors won’t affect the agreement.\"","Lysandra’s eyes stayed on Max. \"Nor will it decide the future of the Divine Realm.\"","Veyrion spoke quietly. \"But if both sides agree, there’s no reason to stop it.\"","The four Primarchs had all given their answer. They didn’t object."]},{"number":2011,"title":"Chapter 2011: A Life and Death battle!","paragraphs":["That decision stirred up the atmosphere again. Some leaders looked thoughtful. Some frowned. Some looked worried, while others looked interested. The War God Palace Master’s smile widened, since he’d always preferred direct clashes over endless talk. The Sword God Palace Master stayed calm, but the sword intent around him sharpened slightly.","The Four Sacred Clans watched Max with complicated expressions. After everything that had happened in their domain, they knew well enough that Max’s realm couldn’t be measured normally.","On top of that, they’d personally watched Max beat one of their own geniuses at the 10th level of the Law Manifestation Realm, let alone a devil sitting at the 5th.","Saint Reiner, though, stayed silent, his eyes fixed on Max. He’d spoken to provoke the devils, but Varok had instantly turned his words into a challenge aimed straight at Max. Saint Reiner knew Max wouldn’t back down just because his opponent held a higher realm. He also knew Max’s pride wasn’t the kind that could be easily reined in.","Still, if the fight turned too dangerous, Saint Reiner was ready to step in. No agreement between the Divine Realm and the Devil Race mattered more than Max’s life.","Max still hadn’t said anything.","Varok looked down at him, his expression now dripping with open provocation.","\"So, Primordial?\" His voice slowed down, turning mocking. \"Are you ready to fight a devil at the 5th level of the Law Manifestation Realm?\"","The devils behind Varok grinned coldly. One of them stepped forward. He stood taller than Varok, his massive body covered in dark crimson tattoos. His horns curved backward like blades, and black fire flickered around his shoulders.","His aura clearly sat at the 5th level of the Law Manifestation Realm, but the pressure he gave off ran far stronger than an ordinary cultivator at that level. His body carried the brutal strength of the Devil Race, and his eyes gleamed with bloodthirsty excitement.","He looked at Max like he’d already found his prey.","\"A Primordial at the 1st level?\" the devil said with a deep laugh. \"Young master, you’re honoring him too much by sending me.\"","Varok chuckled. \"Don’t underestimate him too much. Apparently he’s the strongest young genius of this universe.\"","The devil’s laughter grew louder.","Several Divine Realm geniuses showed their anger openly.","Orion clenched his fists. \"This bastard.\"","Damian’s face turned colder. \"He’s trying to use Max to humiliate all of us.\"","Ervin sneered lightly. \"Let him try. Now that Max has reached the Law Manifestation Realm, I have a feeling he’s gotten even harder to gauge right now. We’re about to see a good show.\"","Only Revona looked at Max with a solemn expression. Nobody knew exactly what was going through her mind.","Max stood at the center of the temporary battlefield with Dragonheart in hand.","Across from him, Raghor, the devil chosen by Varok, grinned with savage confidence. His massive body was covered in dark crimson devil tattoos, and black flames flickered around his shoulders like a cloak of living malice.","He sat at the 5th level of the Law Manifestation Realm, four minor realms above Max, and as a member of the Devil Race, his true combat power naturally outpaced ordinary cultivators at the same level.","To most people, this should have been a hard fight. To Varok, it should have been a humiliation set up for the Divine Realm.","But Max looked calm. Too calm.","Raghor noticed that calm, and his grin slowly turned cruel. \"Still looking confident, huh. Good. I hate killing prey that trembles too early.\"","Max looked at him without much feeling.","\"I’ll accept this fight,\" Max said slowly. \"But it has to be a life-and-death battle. Otherwise, I’m not interested in entertaining a bunch of stupid devils.\"","The moment those words fell, the council domain went silent.","Varok was stunned for a brief moment. Then his eyes narrowed. He couldn’t tell whether the Primordial boy in front of him was a peerless genius or a complete idiot.","A 1st level Law Manifestation Realm cultivator was actually asking for a life-and-death battle against a devil at the 5th level of the same realm. Even among the Devil Race, that kind of arrogance would be considered absurd unless someone had absolute confidence behind it.","The leaders of the top first-rate forces were surprised too. They already knew Max wasn’t simple. They’d heard about his performance, his breakthrough, and the shocking events inside the Five Sacred Clan domain. Some had personally felt the strange pressure hidden in his body.","Even so, asking for a life-and-death battle under these circumstances still went beyond what they’d expected.","Saint Reiner’s eyes turned colder. He didn’t stop Max, but the war intent around him sharpened faintly.","Max didn’t look back. His gaze stayed on Varok. \"So, what’ll it be, Varok?\"","Varok stared at him for a second. Then he laughed.","\"Hahaha!\"","His laughter spread through the council domain, dripping with contempt and amusement.","\"I’ve seen arrogant fools before, but I’ve never seen an idiot quite like you. Since you’re so eager to die, I suppose I have no reason to refuse.\"","He turned to Raghor. \"Go ahead and kill him.\"","Raghor’s grin widened. \"My pleasure, young master.\"","The massive devil rolled his shoulders as he looked at Max with utter disdain. The devil tattoos across his body began to glow, and dark energy surged around him like smoke rising off a battlefield soaked in blood.","\"Dying in front of all these Primordials and leaders of your universe must be pretty embarrassing, don’t you think?\" Raghor said with a deep laugh.","His devil aura erupted. The battlefield beneath his feet trembled, and the black flames around him roared higher. His law manifestation started forming behind him, taking shape as a vast devil furnace filled with charred bones, screaming shadows, and burning crimson chains.","The pressure it released turned several weaker descendants of the Divine Realm pale.","Max smiled faintly at the sight.","\"What morons you devils are....\"","Before Raghor’s expression could even change, a blue void ring flashed out from Max’s body. It moved too fast. The ring didn’t travel like a normal attack. It folded through space, appeared in front of Raghor almost instantly, and wrapped around his body before his devil aura could fully erupt.","Raghor’s eyes went wide. \"What?\"","The void ring expanded. A blue transparent sphere formed around him in an instant. The devil furnace behind him froze. The black flames around his body froze. Even the crimson tattoos glowing across his skin dimmed, as if the connection between his body and the world around him had been cut off.","Raghor tried to move, but his limbs didn’t respond. He tried to circulate his devil power, but the energy inside him turned sluggish. He tried to roar, but even his voice got trapped in his throat.","He’d been sealed. Not restrained. Not slowed. Sealed. His entire body hung suspended in midair, frozen in a separate layer of space.","The expressions of the devils changed. Varok’s smile stiffened.","Before anyone could react, Max moved. His figure vanished from where he stood and reappeared directly in front of Raghor. His right hand transformed mid-motion, pale human fingers turning into terrifying dragon claws covered in black scales.","The claws carried the brutal strength of the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline, the sharpness of his Law Manifestation Realm foundation, and the condensed force of a body strengthened well beyond ordinary limits.","Raghor’s eyes trembled with horror. He still couldn’t move."]},{"number":2012,"title":"Chapter 2012: A Sneak Attack!","paragraphs":["The next instant, Max thrust his dragon claws forward.","Puchi!","His claws pierced through Raghor’s chest and came out through his back.","The battlefield fell silent. The devil’s eyes bulged. The law manifestation behind him shattered before it could fully take shape. The devil furnace collapsed into black sparks, the crimson chains dissolved into smoke, and the dark flames around his body died out like candles caught in a storm.","Raghor stared at Max in disbelief, as if he still couldn’t understand how the battle had ended before it had really begun.","Max pulled his claws out. Raghor’s body fell from the air and crashed onto the battlefield.","The blue void ring returned to Max’s side, rotating silently beside his shoulder.","The massive devil didn’t move again. He was dead.. A devil at the 5th level of the Law Manifestation Realm had been killed in a single exchange.","For a moment, no one spoke. The leaders of the Divine Realm stared at Max with different reactions. Some looked shocked. Some looked thoughtful. Some looked pleased. Garron Aresvale of the War God Palace laughed loudly, his voice full of fierce satisfaction.","Celian Voss of the Sword God Palace looked at the void ring with a rare trace of interest. High Lord Astren Vale’s nine stars rotated faster behind him, as if his calculations had just shifted. Even the Four Sacred Clans fell into a deep silence, their gazes fixed on Max with complicated emotions.","The nine geniuses reacted too. Orion’s eyes shone with excitement. Damian’s expression grew even more serious. Ervin let out a soft breath, while Morgana smiled like she’d just watched something extremely entertaining. Revona stared at Max without a word, but her eyes carried a depth that hadn’t been there before.","Saint Reiner slowly unclenched his fist. A faint smile crossed the old saint’s face.","\"Good,\" he muttered.","Max didn’t look at the fallen devil. He raised his head and looked at Varok.","\"Are you happy now?\"","His voice came out calm. There was no arrogance in it. That only made the humiliation worse.","Varok’s expression had gone completely dark. The mockery on his face was gone. The amusement was gone. Even the earlier arrogance that had filled his eyes had faded, replaced by something far colder and more dangerous. He stared at Raghor’s corpse, then slowly shifted his gaze back to Max.","A devil from his camp had been killed. And not after a long battle, but in an instant. The Divine Realm’s side hadn’t just defended its dignity. Max had crushed the trap Varok set and turned it right back on him, in front of every major force present.","But that wasn’t what truly disturbed Varok. What truly disturbed him was Max himself.","Varok’s eyes narrowed as he stared at the blue void ring floating beside Max.","’A 1st level Law Manifestation Realm cultivator sealed Raghor before he could even react. His body strength is abnormal. His bloodline aura runs layered. Dragon power, Primordial power, sealing power colder than ordinary law. This isn’t a normal genius.’","His expression stayed dark, but his thoughts raced.","’The Primordial Race has produced a rare monster.’","Varok’s gaze turned even more vicious.","’No. Not just rare. Dangerous.’","He’d seen plenty of geniuses in the Devil Universe. Some had terrifying bloodlines. Some had monstrous bodies. Some were blessed by Primal Treasures. Some could cross realms and slaughter enemies stronger than themselves.","But Max was different. His realm sat low, yet his foundation felt impossibly dense. His powers weren’t scattered like a kid collecting treasures. They were beginning to fuse into a real combat system, one that could threaten beings far above him.","If someone like Max was allowed to grow, he’d become a problem. Not just for Varok. For the entire Devil Race.","’If he reaches the Divine Lord Realm, ordinary young devils might not be able to touch him. If he reaches the Divine King Realm, he could become a real obstacle in the coming war. If he lives long enough to mature, he might turn into one of the blades that cuts straight into our invasion.’","A cold decision formed in Varok’s heart.","’He cannot be allowed to grow.’","The Pearl of Abyss shifted beneath his sleeve. It had stayed quiet until now, hidden under his aura and the pressure of the devils around him. But the moment Varok made his decision, a dark pulse flowed from the pearl into his palm.","Varok’s face stayed still. No one saw him raise his hand. No one heard him chant. The Pearl of Abyss didn’t need such obvious movements.","A thin black line appeared behind Max. It was almost invisible. It didn’t tear open space violently. It simply appeared, as if a piece of reality had quietly been erased. From that erased line, an abyssal spike emerged, silent and cold, carrying a power that didn’t belong to ordinary law.","The spike moved toward the back of Max’s head. Fast. Silent. Deadly.","Max’s eyes changed. At the last moment, a warning exploded inside his senses. His Dimensional Sovereign Body trembled. His Primordial Bloodline and Voidwalker bloodline pulsed violently.","’Danger.’","The attack was already behind him. Max didn’t try to block it. He knew instantly this wasn’t something he should take head-on. The aura carried by the abyssal spike felt too strange. It didn’t feel like a normal attack from Varok.","It felt deeper, colder, and far more ancient, like it had come from a darkness that existed before worlds were even separated.","Pearl of Abyss.","The realization flashed through Max’s mind.","Without hesitation, Max activated the entrance to the Dimension of Time. His figure blurred. The abyssal spike pierced forward, but just before it touched him, Max disappeared. The attack passed through the space where he’d stood and struck empty air.","For one breath, the council domain froze. Then the entire sky erupted.","\"Varok!\"","Arvantos’s voice thundered through the council domain.","The four Primarchs moved at the same time. Arvantos appeared above the battlefield, his golden primordial aura spreading across the sky like a vast divine curtain.","Eryndor stepped to his left, his bronze-gold body releasing crushing physical pressure that made the air collapse layer by layer. Lysandra appeared to his right, silver-gold runes flowing around her as she locked onto every trace of abyssal energy in the area. Veyrion appeared behind them, and the space around the battlefield folded into countless invisible barriers.","In an instant, the four Primarchs formed a defensive formation. They didn’t attack right away. They stayed wary. Not of Varok himself. Of the Pearl of Abyss.","A Primal Treasure couldn’t be treated casually. Even with their strength, they couldn’t assume suppressing Varok would come easy while he held one of the five Primal Treasures.","If the Pearl of Abyss erupted fully inside the Primordial Ancestral Domain, the consequences might go beyond even what they could predict.","The leaders of the top first-rate forces reacted too. Garron Aresvale’s battle aura exploded like a war sun. Celian Voss’s sword intent filled the sky. Astren Vale’s nine stars formed a calculation array behind him. Seraphis Kael raised one hand, and the Stellar Templar instantly locked into a battle formation.","Queen Selene Lunaris summoned a pale moon barrier. Lord Vael Noxis distorted the void near the devils. Hall Master Orin Caldus opened an ancient law scroll that released sealing light.","The Four Sacred Clans released their auras too. For a moment, the devils found themselves surrounded by the full pressure of the Divine Realm’s peak forces.","Varok stood at the center of that pressure. His face had gone pale. A thin line of dark blood slid from the corner of his mouth. The Pearl of Abyss hovered above his palm now, no longer fully hidden.","It looked like a small black pearl, smooth and bottomless, with faint rings of abyssal light rotating inside it. Looking at it felt like staring into a hole that led beneath reality itself.","Around the pearl, space didn’t crack. It sank. Light didn’t scatter. It disappeared. Laws didn’t break apart. They got swallowed into a depth that refused to reveal its limit.","This was the true terror of the Pearl of Abyss. It didn’t simply release destructive power. It opened a connection to the abyss itself. Any attack born from it could ignore many ordinary defenses, since it didn’t need to break through them the normal way.","It could erase a path through space, appear behind a target, bury itself inside their body, and drag their flesh, soul, bloodline, or laws into abyssal collapse. Used fully, it could open abyssal passages, hide traces from fate, devour surrounding energy, and blur the boundary between worlds.","It was a treasure capable of turning a single moment of carelessness into death.","But Varok wasn’t its true master. At least, not yet. His cultivation only sat at the Divine King Realm. That realm was already powerful by normal standards, but it wasn’t enough to freely control a Primal Treasure.","The Pearl of Abyss had answered him because of his bloodline, status, and preparation, but using it still came with a price. The moment the sneak attack failed, the backlash hit him.","Dark veins appeared along Varok’s wrist. The abyssal patterns crawled up his arm before slowly sinking back into his flesh. His aura turned unstable for a brief moment, and the devils behind him immediately stepped forward in alarm.","\"Young master!\"","Varok raised one hand, stopping them. His expression looked ugly. He’d paid the price, yet the attack had still failed. Max had escaped.","The spot where Max had stood now sat empty, but everyone knew he wasn’t dead. He’d vanished somewhere at the very last moment, dodging the Pearl of Abyss’s strike by a hair."]},{"number":2013,"title":"Chapter 2013: End of the Meeting!","paragraphs":["Lysandra’s eyes turned cold. \"You used a Primal Treasure to sneak attack a junior during an agreed battle.\"","Eryndor’s voice carried heavy killing intent. \"You truly want war.\"","Veyrion stared at the Pearl of Abyss. \"Careful. The treasure’s still active.\"","Arvantos looked at Varok, and for the first time since the meeting began, his calm expression showed a trace of terrifying anger.","\"Varok,\" he said slowly. \"Explain yourself.\"","Varok wiped the blood from the corner of his mouth. His expression stayed dark, but his eyes still carried stubborn arrogance.","\"That Primordial killed one of my people.\"","Garron Aresvale laughed coldly. \"In a life-and-death battle you agreed to.\"","Celian Voss’s voice came out quiet. \"And you answered by ambushing him with a Primal Treasure.\"","Saint Reiner’s face had gone colder than anyone else’s. His war intent had grown so dense that the space around him trembled. If not for the four Primarchs standing between both sides and the Pearl of Abyss still pulsing in Varok’s hand, he would have already crossed the battlefield.","\"That was my student,\" Saint Reiner said. His voice came out low, but everyone heard it. \"If he dies because of your sneak attack, no agreement will save you.\"","Varok’s eyes flickered. The pressure coming from all sides was terrifying. Even with the Pearl of Abyss, he knew he couldn’t act recklessly again. He’d already suffered backlash from one silent strike.","If he forced the pearl to erupt while surrounded by the four Primarchs and the strongest forces of the Divine Realm, the outcome might slip out of his control.","The pearl could protect him. It could threaten them. But it could also consume him if he tried to push power beyond what his realm could handle.","For the first time, Varok felt the danger of standing in another universe.","Then space trembled softly above the battlefield. A silver ripple opened. Max stepped out of it.","His expression stayed calm, but his eyes had gone much colder than before. The Dimension of Time had saved him, but the fact remained that he’d nearly been killed.","If his Dimensional Keeper Legacy had warned him even a fraction later, if his reaction had been slower, if the entrance to the Dimension of Time had failed to open in time, that abyssal spike would have gone straight through his head.","Max looked at the Pearl of Abyss in Varok’s hand. Then he looked at Varok.","\"One day I’ll return that a hundredfold.\"","Varok didn’t answer him. For a few breaths, he just stared. Seeing Max standing there alive and unharmed after dodging the Pearl of Abyss made Varok feel even worse than before.","Raghor had been killed in front of everyone, his sneak attack had failed, and the Primordial he wanted erased had returned with the same calm expression, as if even a Primal Treasure hadn’t been enough to truly scare him.","That silence stung worse than any insult. Varok’s hatred for Max climbed to a whole new level. Before this, Max had been a troublesome genius who might become an obstacle down the road. Now, in Varok’s eyes, he’d become someone who had to die.","A young Primordial with that kind of talent, that kind of reaction speed, that kind of strange escape method, and that kind of fearless attitude couldn’t be allowed to grow freely.","If Max survived a few more centuries, he might become one of the most dangerous enemies the Devil Race would ever face inside this universe.","But Varok couldn’t make another move now. The four Primarchs were already watching him with cold eyes. The leaders of the top first-rate forces had locked their auras onto him too.","Saint Reiner’s killing intent felt especially terrifying, and Varok could tell the old saint of the War God Palace was only waiting for one excuse to act.","Even with the Pearl of Abyss in his possession, Varok knew he couldn’t keep pushing the situation. He’d already suffered backlash from using the treasure once, and if he forced it again surrounded by this many peak experts, the outcome might not stay within his control.","The Pearl of Abyss was powerful. But it wasn’t something his current cultivation could use without a cost.","Varok slowly wiped the dark blood from the corner of his mouth. His expression settled back into calm, but that calm only made the hatred hiding beneath it feel more dangerous. He looked away from Max and turned to the four Primarchs.","\"We have our agreement,\" Varok said coldly. \"Now it’s time for us to leave.\"","The four primarchs became silent hearing him. They knew that if the devils wanted to leave they couldn’t stop them since they possessed the Pearl of Abyss. And so they didn’t even try to stop them.","Arvantos looked at him without any warmth. \"Remember the terms.\"","Primarch Eryndor’s voice followed like a heavy mountain pressing down from the heavens. \"If your devils break them, there will be no second negotiation.\"","Lysandra’s silver-gold eyes stayed fixed on the Pearl of Abyss. \"And if you use that treasure carelessly inside our universe again, don’t assume your father’s name will protect you.\"","Veyrion said nothing, but the space around the devils tightened faintly, as if reminding them their retreat was being allowed, not overlooked.","Varok’s fingers curled around the Pearl of Abyss. A dark, radiant light flashed from the pearl. For an instant, the sky above the grand council domain seemed to sink into a bottomless darkness. The devils behind Varok got swallowed by that abyssal glow one after another, their figures twisting like shadows reflected on deep water.","Varok’s gaze stayed on Max until the very last moment. The hatred in his eyes was unmistakable.","Max looked back at him calmly. Neither of them said anything.","Then the abyssal light surged. A moment later, Varok and the remaining devils vanished from the council domain.","The black mist in the sky slowly faded. The pressure left behind by the Pearl of Abyss lingered for a few breaths before the primordial light of the ancestral domain washed it away.","No one moved right away. The agreement had been made. The devils had retreated.","But everyone present understood this wasn’t the end of the conflict.","It was only the beginning."]},{"number":2014,"title":"Chapter 2014: A Path Beyond the Seven Divine Veins!","paragraphs":["After Varok and the devils disappeared, the meeting finally came to an end.","The outcome wasn’t a surprise. In truth, everyone present had already sensed the likely result before the meeting even started. The Divine Realm wasn’t in a position to launch a full war against the Devil Race right now.","The hole in the Wall of Eternity was still small, the devils inside their universe were limited in number, and the older generation needed time to prepare. Because of all that, flat-out rejecting Varok’s demands had never been the realistic option.","What actually mattered wasn’t whether the Divine Realm would agree to his conditions. What mattered was how many restrictions they could squeeze into the agreement. That was the whole reason for the meeting.","The Devil Race had gotten permission to set up a force in the Divine Realm, but that permission came with chains attached.","They’d be watched. Their movements would get recorded. They’d be forbidden from entering the Mortal Realm. They’d face punishment if they harmed, corrupted, enslaved, or secretly controlled the people of the Divine Realm.","The devils had won a foothold, but the Divine Realm had made sure that foothold wouldn’t turn into a free path to spread unchecked.","Even so, nobody looked relaxed.","The strongest first-rate forces started leaving one after another.","The War God Palace, Sword God Palace, Ascension Hall, Nine Star Court, Grand Void Sanctum, Stellar Templar, and Lunarian Kingdom all exchanged a few brief words with the four Primarchs before preparing to head out.","Their leaders didn’t speak loudly, but the solemn look on their faces made it clear each force had already started thinking about the future.","The years ahead wouldn’t be peaceful. Defense lines needed strengthening, disciples needed warning, hidden spies needed rooting out, and every major force had to prepare for a possible war that might arrive within five hundred years, or even sooner.","The Four Sacred Clans stayed quiet too. Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest had walked into this meeting carrying their own internal conflict, but after watching the devils and seeing Varok try to use the Pearl of Abyss on Max, even they understood the Divine Realm now faced a far bigger threat.","Whatever resentment and suspicion still lingered between them and the Voidwalker Clan couldn’t be allowed to weaken the whole universe.","Max stood silently near the Primordial side, watching the great forces leave. His fight with Raghor had ended quickly, but its impact hadn’t faded.","Plenty of gazes still drifted toward him before turning away. Some carried approval. Some carried curiosity. Some carried caution. Some carried the complicated mix of emotions from people who’d just realized this 1st level Law Manifestation Realm youth couldn’t be measured by normal rules.","Just then, Saint Reiner walked toward him from the War God Palace’s side.","The old saint’s aura had softened compared to when Varok attacked. He looked calmer now, though the deep battle intent around him hadn’t fully faded.","His long silver hair moved slightly as he approached, and the scars across his dark gold and crimson armor looked even more ancient under the fading light of the council domain.","He stopped in front of Max and looked at him for a moment. Then he laughed and patted him on the shoulder.","\"Haha, you did well, kid,\" Saint Reiner said. \"Those devils really thought they could do whatever they wanted inside our universe. How stupid.\"","Max smiled lightly. \"They were pretty stupid, yeah.\"","Saint Reiner’s laughter faded into a satisfied grin, but his eyes soon turned more serious. He looked Max over closely, as if examining the changes in his body with a gaze sharpened by countless years of body cultivation.","Then his expression shifted.","\"I can see it,\" Saint Reiner said. \"You’ve unlocked the fifth vein of the Seven Divine Veins.\"","Max’s eyes moved slightly.","Saint Reiner nodded with clear approval. \"The Vein of Resilience. Good boy. With this, you’ve officially surpassed every single person in the Divine Realm who’s ever opened the Seven Divine Veins.\"","His words carried real pride. Saint Reiner had always been strict with Max, and he wasn’t someone who handed out praise easily. His whole path revolved around war, body cultivation, and endless tempering. Getting approval like that from him meant Max had truly achieved something extraordinary.","Saint Reiner continued, \"I told you before that only the Primordials had ever managed to reach the fourth Divine Vein, and that wasn’t wrong. Among the Primordial Race, there’s one existence who opened the fourth vein with the help of a complete technique, a natural primordial body, and countless resources accumulated by the oldest force in the Divine Realm.\"","He paused for a moment. \"Even for that person, going beyond the fourth Divine Vein was impossible.\"","Max listened quietly.","Saint Reiner looked at him and smiled with rare pride. \"But you, Max, have done what nobody else in the Divine Realm has managed. Not the War God Palace. Not the Sword God Palace. Not the Four Sacred Clans. Not even the Primordial Race. You’ve opened the fifth Divine Vein and reached the Vein of Resilience. From this point on, when it comes to the Seven Divine Veins, you’ve officially surpassed everyone in this universe.\"","His hand tightened slightly on Max’s shoulder. \"You did well.\"","Max nodded lightly, but the curiosity in his eyes didn’t fade.","After a brief silence, he asked, \"In your inheritance, you mentioned that beyond the Seven Divine Veins, there’s an even higher body cultivation path. You also said the Seven Divine Veins are only the foundation needed to reach that higher path.\"","Saint Reiner’s smile slowly faded.","Max’s expression sharpened as he pressed on. \"Can you tell me more about that?\"","Saint Reiner sighed. For a moment, the old saint looked far older than before. His eyes, filled with pride just a breath ago, now carried the regret of a man who’d chased a path for countless years without ever finding its end.","\"The path beyond the Seven Divine Veins is the thing that’s eluded me the most,\" he said slowly. \"In all my research, all my battles, all my studies of ancient body cultivation methods, and all the ruins I explored, I found plenty of fragments pointing to its existence. But fragments are only fragments. I know that path exists for certain, but sadly, I don’t know much about it.\""]},{"number":2015,"title":"Chapter 2015: Library of the Primordials!","paragraphs":["Max frowned slightly.","Saint Reiner continued, \"When I first got my hands on the incomplete Seven Divine Veins method, it was broken beyond recognition. Most people would’ve written it off as some ancient body cultivation remnant with no real value. I spent centuries researching it, comparing it against lost techniques, studying old battle records, digging through forbidden ruins, and testing it on myself over and over. Only after all that did I manage to complete the Seven Divine Veins.\"","His voice grew heavier. \"But while completing it, I found something strange. The Seven Divine Veins didn’t feel like the end of a body cultivation path. They felt like preparation. Each vein strengthens one part of the body’s foundation, but together, they seem built to support something far greater.\"","Saint Reiner looked directly at Max. \"The Origin Vein strengthens the root of physical existence. The Vitality Vein strengthens recovery and life force. The Speed Vein strengthens movement and reaction. The Strength Vein strengthens raw physical force. The Resilience Vein strengthens endurance and resistance. The remaining veins, if you manage to open them, should round out the body’s balance. Once all seven exist together, I believe they form the true foundation needed to step into a higher body cultivation realm.\"","Max’s eyes sharpened. \"What’s that higher realm called?\"","Saint Reiner shook his head. \"I don’t know.\"","Max fell silent.","Saint Reiner’s expression carried regret, but his voice stayed steady. \"That’s the part I never found. I searched for names, records, techniques, and inheritance fragments, but everything beyond the Seven Divine Veins was either erased, hidden, or never properly passed down in this universe. All I can tell you is this. The Seven Divine Veins aren’t the final destination. They’re the gate.\"","\"I see,\" Max said softly, his frown deepening slightly.","If even Saint Reiner didn’t have a clear answer about the body cultivation path beyond the Seven Divine Veins, finding clues would be extremely hard. Saint Reiner wasn’t an ordinary elder.","He was one of the greatest body cultivation experts in the Divine Realm, and he’d spent centuries studying this exact path. If even he’d only turned up fragments, the truth behind the higher body cultivation path had to be buried incredibly deep.","Saint Reiner noticed Max’s expression and smiled again. \"Don’t look so discouraged.\"","Max looked at him.","\"I don’t have the answer,\" Saint Reiner said. \"But that doesn’t mean nobody does.\"","\"Who does?\" Max asked, curious.","\"The Primordial Race,\" Saint Reiner replied solemnly, his gaze shifting toward the ancient halls of the Primordial Ancestral Domain.","\"They’re the oldest force in the Divine Realm. Their history stretches back further than every palace, court, kingdom, sanctum, hall, and sacred clan gathered here today. If anyone in this universe has records about the body cultivation path beyond the Seven Divine Veins, it’d most likely be them.\"","Saint Reiner looked back at Max. \"You’re a Primordial now. Use that. Visit the library of the Primordial Race. Search through their ancient records. Look for anything tied to body cultivation, divine veins, primordial physique, origin body, or paths beyond the seven veins. If there’s even a small clue anywhere, it should be there.\"","Max nodded. \"I will.\"","Saint Reiner patted his shoulder again, this time with more weight behind it.","\"Take care of yourself, kid,\" he said. \"Things are about to get wild in our universe. The devils have gotten in, the Wall of Eternity’s been pierced, and forces that stayed silent for countless years might start moving again. You need to get stronger fast.\"","His old eyes sharpened once more. \"And the next time I see you, I’d better see you go beyond the Seven Divine Veins.\"","Max’s expression turned solemn. \"I’ll try my best.\"","Saint Reiner gave a satisfied nod. \"Good.\"","He turned and walked back toward the War God Palace delegation, who were already waiting for him near the edge of the council domain. Garron Aresvale glanced at Max with a fierce grin before leading the warriors of the War God Palace into a glowing spatial passage.","Saint Reiner went in last. Before disappearing, he looked back one more time.","Max met his gaze from a distance. No more words passed between them.","A moment later, the spatial passage closed, and the War God Palace vanished from the Primordial Ancestral Domain.","Max stood where he was, Saint Reiner’s words still echoing in his mind.","The path beyond the Seven Divine Veins. The library of the Primordial Race.","+++","The next day, Primarch Arvantos gathered the ten young Primordials once again.","This time, they weren’t in the grand council domain where the meeting with the devils had taken place. Instead, Arvantos brought them into a quieter hall inside the Primordial Ancestral Domain.","The hall was vast but not oppressive. Its walls were made of ancient bronze-gold stone, and countless faint runes flowed across them like silent rivers of light. A wide window opened on one side of the hall, showing off the magnificent scenery of the Primordial Ancestral Domain outside.","From where Max stood, he could see floating mountains drifting above golden clouds. Ancient palaces sat on distant peaks, primordial law rivers flowed through the sky, and enormous stone statues of forgotten experts watched over the domain like guardians from the earliest era of the universe.","The whole place carried a sense of age that couldn’t be found anywhere else in the Divine Realm.","Arvantos stood in front of the window with his hands behind his back. After a moment, he finally spoke.","\"Now that the meeting with the devils has wrapped up, it’s time to talk about the truly important matter.\"","His voice stayed calm, but every word carried weight. He kept looking through the window for a few more breaths before turning toward Max and the others.","\"The agreement with Varok only delayed the problem. It didn’t solve anything. The devils have gained a foothold in the Divine Realm, the Wall of Eternity has been pierced, and the Devil Race is still trying to widen the breach from the other side. If nothing changes, a true war is coming sooner or later.\"","The expressions of the ten geniuses turned serious."]},{"number":2016,"title":"Chapter 2016: Three Ways!","paragraphs":["Arvantos’s gaze swept across them. \"You’re all talented. Each of you stood at the peak of the Cosmic Ascension Conference, and each of you now carries a Primordial Bloodline. Some of you have already awakened bloodline abilities. Some have already stepped into the Divine Lord Realm. Some of you have inheritances, physiques, talents, and backgrounds ordinary cultivators could never dream of.\"","His eyes paused on Max for a brief moment before moving on.","\"But talent alone isn’t enough.\"","The hall grew even quieter.","Arvantos went on, \"Given the current situation, normal growth in the Divine Realm won’t be enough for any of you. If you cultivate naturally, even with your talent, most of you would need thousands of years, maybe longer, to reach the Holy King Realm or Divine Master Realm. Only after reaching those stages would you truly have the strength to influence the war between universes.\"","Orion frowned. \"Thousands of years?\"","Arvantos nodded. \"That’s already a generous estimate. You need to understand that the higher the cultivation realm, the slower progress gets. In the early stages, a genius can break through several minor realms in a short stretch of time. But once you pass the Divine Lord Realm, Divine King Realm, Holy Lord Realm, Holy King Realm, and Divine Master Realm, every step demands far more than just energy. You need comprehension, foundation, law refinement, bloodline stability, soul strength, and opportunities that suit your path.\"","His voice deepened. \"Plenty of geniuses who once shook the Divine Realm turned ordinary after reaching the higher realms because they lacked one of those things. Some had talent but no opportunity. Some had opportunity but no foundation. Some had foundation but lacked the courage to risk their lives. Some simply hit the limit of what their bloodline and comprehension could support.\"","Max listened silently. He understood this better than most. His own growth had been fast, but it had never come easy. Every major jump in strength had come from terrifying inheritances, dangerous trials, hidden dimensions, cosmic paths, bloodlines, and battles where death had never sat far away.","Arvantos continued, \"But we don’t have thousands of years.\" His gaze sharpened. \"I want all of you to reach that level of strength within five hundred years.\"","The ten geniuses fell silent. Even Damian’s cold expression shifted slightly.","Five hundred years. Reaching the Holy King Realm or even the Divine Master Realm in five hundred years was an outrageous goal.","For ordinary cultivators, even imagining something like that would sound laughable. But Arvantos wasn’t speaking like it was a joke. He spoke like it was the bare minimum.","\"You’re the future hope of this universe,\" Arvantos said. \"Old people like me will lead the war if it comes. The Primarchs, the ancient experts, the masters of the first-rate forces, and the hidden protectors of the Divine Realm will stand at the front. But wars between universes aren’t won by old strength alone. The older generation can defend. We can delay. We can hold the line. But the younger generation is the one that creates variables.\"","His eyes swept across them again. \"A young genius who rises fast enough can break the balance. A cultivator who reaches a realm earlier than expected can change a battlefield. A monster who survives where others die can become a blade no enemy saw coming. That’s why the devils are dangerous, and that’s exactly why all of you matter.\"","Max’s gaze deepened slightly.","Arvantos continued, \"If you stay protected inside the Divine Realm and grow slowly, you might become powerful one day, but that day might come too late. So we need to pick a faster path.\"","Orion’s eyes lit up slightly. \"What path?\"","Arvantos smiled faintly. \"There are only three real ways for all of you to get stronger quickly.\"","The moment he said it, the attention of the ten geniuses sharpened even further.","Orion immediately asked, \"What three ways?\"","Arvantos looked at him with a faint smile. \"The first and easiest way is the Primordial Race.\"","The answer surprised no one, but everyone listened closely.","Arvantos said, \"If you want, I can summon great experts from our race to personally guide each of you. We can give you cultivation grounds, bloodline pools, law towers, ancient scriptures, combat instructors, soul tempering formations, divine medicines, and resources even many first-rate forces can’t easily offer. With the foundation you already have, I can guarantee every one of you will at least reach the Holy Lord Realm within the five hundred years we have.\"","That statement shook a few of the geniuses’ hearts. Holy Lord Realm within five hundred years. A promise like that would drive countless cultivators mad with envy. For most forces, producing even one Holy Lord could change their entire status. Yet Arvantos was talking about the Primordial Race forcibly nurturing ten of them within five centuries. That alone showed just how terrifying the resources and background of the oldest race in the Divine Realm really were.","But Arvantos’s expression soon turned more serious.","\"That said, I don’t recommend this path unless there’s no other choice.\"","Damian’s eyes narrowed. \"Why?\"","\"Because a path built purely on protection and resources is fast, but it isn’t sharp,\" Arvantos replied. \"You’d grow stronger, sure, but your strength would come from cultivating under controlled pressure. Your foundations might look impressive, but they’d miss the tempering that comes from real danger. You’d learn techniques, improve your realms, refine your bloodlines, and strengthen your laws, but you wouldn’t go through the kind of desperate situations that force a genius to truly transform.\"","His voice carried a note of warning. \"The Primordial Race can raise your cultivation. But if we raise you too safely, we might also make you rusty. Worse, your foundations might turn unstable because too many resources got poured into you too fast. On the surface, you’d become Holy Lords. In reality, you might end up weaker than enemies who reached the same realm through blood, battle, and life-or-death opportunities.\"","Morgana smiled faintly. \"So it’s the comfortable path.\"","\"Yes,\" Arvantos said. \"And comfort is dangerous for people like you.\"","Damian looked at Arvantos. \"Then what are the other two methods?\"","His tone made it clear he had no interest in sitting inside the Primordial Race for five hundred years. Most of the others seemed to feel the same way. They were geniuses who’d fought their way to the peak of the Cosmic Ascension Conference. None of them wanted to be raised like treasures inside a protected cage."]},{"number":2017,"title":"Chapter 2017: Godslayer’s Pilgrimage!","paragraphs":["Arvantos smiled slightly. \"Have any of you heard of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage?\"","The ten geniuses looked at each other. No one answered. Even Revona, who seemed to know plenty of secrets, showed a trace of confusion. Orion blinked. Ervin frowned in thought. Damian stayed quiet, but his expression made it obvious the term was new to him.","Max finally asked, \"What is that?\"","Arvantos’s smile faded, and his expression turned solemn.","\"The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage is the highest-level opportunity available to the younger generation across all five universes.\"","Those words instantly changed the atmosphere in the hall.","Arvantos continued, \"If the Cosmic Ascension Conference gathers the strongest geniuses of the Divine Realm from our universe, then the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage gathers the strongest geniuses from all five universes. The Primordial Universe, the Devil Universe, the Spirit Universe, the Angel Universe, and the Dragon Universe all send their most terrifying young monsters there.\"","The expressions of the ten geniuses shifted. All five universes. That meant they wouldn’t only be facing geniuses from the Divine Realm. They’d be facing devils born in the Devil Universe, spirits naturally close to law and life essence, angels wielding terrifying holy power and divine order, and dragons whose bodies and bloodlines ranked among the strongest in existence.","Arvantos said, \"Don’t underestimate what that means. In our universe, all of you count as peak geniuses. But in the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, you’ll run into beings who carry the destiny of their own universes. Some were born from royal bloodlines. Some have been trained by supreme races since childhood. Some are descendants of old monsters who fought in the last universal war. Some hold treasures, physiques, eyes, souls, and laws even I wouldn’t casually dismiss.\"","Orion’s excitement turned more serious. Damian’s eyes sharpened. Max stayed calm, but his interest had clearly been stirred.","Arvantos looked at them and continued, \"The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage doesn’t sit inside any of the five universes. It exists in a strange region beyond the Wall of Eternity, beyond the reach of the five universes, in a place where their borders overlap without fully merging. Some call it the Forgotten Crossing. Some call it the Grave Road. Some call it the Battlefield Beneath the Gods. But its true name, at least in the oldest records, is the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"Why’s it called that?\"","Arvantos stayed silent for a moment. Then he said, \"Because according to ancient records, gods once fell there.\"","The hall went deathly quiet.","Arvantos continued slowly, \"Not Divine Masters. Not peak experts who got worshiped as gods by weaker worlds. I’m talking about beings closer to the true meaning of that word. Whether they were real True Gods, failed True Gods, or existences who’d touched the threshold above the Divine God Realm, no one can say for certain. Too much time has passed, and too many records have been lost. But what we do know is that countless divine remnants, broken weapons, blood-stained laws, shattered thrones, and sealed inheritances got left behind there.\"","His voice grew deeper. \"Every cycle, the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage opens up for the younger generation of the five universes. No single race controls it. And because of that, it became a battleground for geniuses from all five universes.\"","Ervin asked quietly, \"What kind of opportunities exist there?\"","Arvantos glanced at him. \"Almost every kind you can imagine, and plenty you can’t.\"","He raised one hand, and faint images appeared in the air in front of them. Max saw a vast road made of broken stars. He saw ruined temples floating inside storms of law. He saw a battlefield where enormous bones stretched across space like mountain ranges. He saw a river of golden blood flowing against time. He saw a shattered throne surrounded by countless weapon fragments. He saw a dark valley where laws moved like living beasts.","Arvantos said, \"There are inheritance grounds left behind by fallen supreme beings. There are law pools capable of pushing a cultivator’s comprehension forward by centuries. There are body tempering zones where flesh gets crushed, rebuilt, and transformed. There are soul-forging ruins where one mistake can erase the mind, but success can strengthen the soul beyond ordinary limits. There are bloodline altars that can purify, evolve, or mutate bloodlines. There are ancient weapons that choose their own owners. There are battlefields where killing enemies earns divine marks, and those marks can be traded for opportunities that don’t exist anywhere in the Divine Realm.\"","Several geniuses drew in a soft breath.","Arvantos continued, \"There are also trials tied to the five universes. Some test the body. Some test the soul. Some test law comprehension. Some test killing power. Some test will. Some test whether a cultivator can survive betrayal, illusion, despair, and temptation. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage doesn’t raise gentle flowers. It sharpens blades.\"","Max’s eyes deepened. That kind of place sounded dangerous. But it was also exactly the kind of place where he could grow the fastest.","Arvantos looked at them solemnly. \"Any opportunity you find there will be countless times stronger than anything you’d normally find in the Divine Realm. That’s why there’s never a shortage of geniuses willing to go in. Every race sends its monsters. Every universe sends its future pillars. Some go there to rise. Some go there to kill rivals before they mature. Some go there to seize inheritances that could shift the balance of their race.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed at that. ’This place probably isn’t simple.’","Arvantos looked at the ten of them and spoke again. \"The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage doesn’t stay open all the time. It follows cycles that none of the five universes fully control. The next opening is coming up soon. If you choose this path, you’ll be sent there.\"","Orion couldn’t hold back any longer. \"And the third path?\"","Arvantos turned toward him. \"The third path is tied to the Seven Monarchs.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, the atmosphere in the hall shifted again.","Damian’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"Monarchs?\"","His reaction wasn’t small. Even someone as cold and composed as Damian couldn’t stay indifferent hearing that title. The others grew more attentive too. Some looked surprised, some looked doubtful, and some seemed like they’d only heard the name in passing without ever really believing it was real.","\"Are they actually real?\" Damian asked in a low voice. \"I thought the Seven Monarchs were just legends, some wild rumor passed around the Divine Realm.\"","Before Arvantos could answer, Revona smiled faintly. \"Oh, they’re very real,\" she said.","Everyone turned toward her. Revona’s expression stayed calm, but there was a strange depth in her eyes, as if that title had stirred up memories buried far beyond this life.","\"In fact,\" she continued, \"I even fought one of the Monarchs in one of my past lives.\"","The hall fell silent again.","Max looked at Revona for a moment, then turned back to Arvantos with a slight frown. \"Monarchs?\"","This time, he was genuinely confused. It was the first time he’d heard of them.","Judging by Damian’s reaction, though, they clearly weren’t ordinary figures. If someone like Damian had only ever treated them as legends, then these so-called Monarchs had to be existences hidden so deeply that even top geniuses of the Divine Realm didn’t know the full truth."]},{"number":2018,"title":"Chapter 2018: Seven Monarchs!","paragraphs":["Arvantos looked at Max and spoke slowly. \"The Monarchs are real beings.\"","His voice stayed calm, but it carried a seriousness that made everyone listen without interrupting.","\"The Seven Monarchs might be the strongest seven beings in our entire universe. They rarely show themselves in the Divine Realm, and even a lot of first-rate forces only know fragmented rumors about them. Some believe they’re ancient cultivators who survived the last universal war. Some believe they’re living embodiments of certain cosmic paths. Some believe they’re existences who failed to step into the True God Realm but still surpassed the limits of ordinary Divine Masters. None of those rumors are entirely right, but none of them are completely wrong either.\"","Max’s eyes sharpened.","Arvantos continued, \"In a way, they’re the protectors of our universe.\"","Those words changed Max’s expression. Protectors of the universe. That title carried too much weight. The Primordial Race was already the oldest force in the Divine Realm. The four Primarchs stood among the highest beings Max had ever seen.","Yet Arvantos was saying the Seven Monarchs were the universe’s last protectors. That meant their standing didn’t sit below the Primordial Race. If anything, they occupied a place so special that even the Primordials had to acknowledge them.","Max couldn’t help but ask, \"Are the Seven Monarchs stronger than Primarchs like you?\"","The other geniuses looked toward Arvantos too. This was the question they all wanted answered.","Arvantos smiled lightly, but his answer wasn’t direct. \"It’s hard to say who’s stronger between the four Primarchs and the Seven Monarchs.\" He paused for a moment before continuing. \"Our powers are different. Our responsibilities are different. Our battlefields are different. The four Primarchs stand openly at the front of the Primordial Race, and we carry the weight of leading the oldest force in the Divine Realm. We guard the structure of this universe through authority, armies, ancient formations, and the foundation left behind by our ancestors.\"","His gaze moved past the window, toward the distant sky of the Primordial Ancestral Domain.","\"The Seven Monarchs work differently. They don’t rule forces in the ordinary sense. They don’t attend conferences. They don’t fight over territory. They don’t get involved in the disputes of forces, clans, kingdoms, or palaces unless the matter touches the survival of the universe itself. Most of the time, they exist outside the visible order of the Divine Realm.\"","His voice deepened. \"But when the universe reaches its final line of defense, they’re the ones who show up.\"","The hall went extremely quiet.","Arvantos looked back at them. \"That’s why they’re called Monarchs. Not because they sit on thrones ruling over people, but because each of them has mastered a path so completely that ordinary cultivators can’t even imagine the height they’ve reached. One Monarch might suppress a forbidden region alone. Another might guard a wound in the Wall of Eternity. Another might sleep inside a dead star realm, waiting for an ancient seal to break. Another might be watching the movements of the Angel Race, the Dragon Race, or the devils right now.\"","Max listened with growing interest. He’d already seen plenty of powerful beings, but the way Arvantos talked about the Seven Monarchs made them feel different.","The Primarchs were mighty pillars. The Monarchs sounded like hidden blades buried somewhere in the darkness beyond the known world.","Arvantos continued, \"The third path for all of you is to receive tutelage from one of the Seven Monarchs.\"","The expressions of the ten geniuses shifted again. Even Revona’s smile faded slightly.","Arvantos said, \"If the first path is safe cultivation under the Primordial Race, and the second path is the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, the third path means being personally guided by one of the beings closest to the peak of our universe. That doesn’t mean all of you would get accepted. The Monarchs don’t teach casually. They don’t care about your background, your reputation, or the rankings you earned in the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","His gaze swept across them. \"If a Monarch doesn’t find you suitable, even I can’t force them to take you in.\"","Orion frowned. \"Then how are we even supposed to choose that path?\"","\"You won’t choose them first,\" Arvantos replied. \"They’ll choose you.\"","That answer made the hall feel heavier.","Arvantos explained further, \"Each Monarch follows a different path. Some specialize in body cultivation. Some specialize in soul. Some specialize in space, fate, sword, battle, life, death, and other terrifying directions. If your foundation resonates with one of them, you might get summoned. If not, you’ll have to choose between the Primordial Race’s protected training and the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.\"","Max’s heart stirred slightly. Body cultivation. The path beyond the Seven Divine Veins immediately jumped into his mind. Saint Reiner had told him that if any force held records about the higher path beyond the Seven Divine Veins, it would be the Primordial Race.","But now Arvantos had mentioned that among the Seven Monarchs, there might be someone who specialized in body cultivation.","Maybe that wasn’t a coincidence. Maybe Saint Reiner’s clue and Arvantos’s third path pointed toward the same place.","Arvantos seemed to notice the shift in Max’s expression but didn’t comment on it. Instead, he continued, \"Still, don’t think this third path is easier than the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. Getting taught by a Monarch isn’t the same as being protected by a teacher. Their methods run extreme a lot of the time. Some might throw you into danger worse than anything you’d face in the Divine Realm. Some might test your will until your soul nearly breaks. Some might force you to confront your own path in a way that leaves no room to retreat.\"","His expression turned stern. \"A Monarch won’t waste time comforting you. If they accept you, it means they believe you have a real chance to carry part of the universe’s future. If you fail, they won’t lower the standard just for you.\"","No one spoke. The three paths now felt far heavier than before. The first path offered safety, resources, and steady growth, but risked dulling their edge. The second path offered terrifying opportunities in the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, but also dropped them among monsters from all five universes, where death could show up at any moment.","The third path offered guidance from the universe’s hidden protectors, but acceptance wasn’t guaranteed, and the training might turn out even harsher than stepping onto an ancient battlefield.","Arvantos looked at them calmly. \"You all have one day to decide.\"","His voice spread through the hall. \"The next opening of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage is in one week. During that time, the Monarchs will also be told about your existence. If any of them show interest, you’ll know before the pilgrimage begins.\"","He paused briefly. \"Decide how you want your path to unfold.\"","The ten geniuses stayed silent. Each of them carried different ambitions, different foundations, different fears, and different reasons for wanting strength. But after hearing Arvantos’s words, they all understood one thing clearly.","From this moment on, their choices would no longer affect only themselves.","Arvantos looked at them one last time. Then his figure faded from the hall and vanished without a sound.","The hall grew quiet. Outside the wide window, the Primordial Ancestral Domain remained majestic and ancient, but in Max’s eyes, even that sacred scenery now seemed to carry the weight of an approaching storm."]},{"number":2019,"title":"Chapter 2019: Talking Among Themselves!","paragraphs":["Only the ten geniuses remained inside the hall after Arvantos disappeared.","For a while, no one spoke. The words Arvantos had left behind still hung in the air. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, the Seven Monarchs, the Devil Race, the Wall of Eternity, and the coming war all pressed down on them like invisible mountains.","Before this, every one of them had counted as a peak genius of the Divine Realm. Each carried their own pride, their own background, their own ambitions, and their own path to the top. But now the stage had suddenly expanded far beyond the Divine Realm itself.","They were no longer only competing with each other. They’d have to face monsters from all five universes.","Orion was the first to break the silence. He looked around at everyone with a smile, though the excitement in his eyes ran more serious than usual. \"So, which path is everyone picking?\"","Kaiden answered without much hesitation. \"I’m willing to train under one of the Monarchs if I get chosen. Otherwise, I’ll go to the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.\"","His tone came out firm. He’d clearly already made up his mind.","Damian nodded from the side. \"Same.\"","He looked toward Ervin. \"What about you?\"","Ervin shrugged lightly, but his thoughtful expression showed he wasn’t treating this casually. \"I don’t know much about the Seven Monarchs, so I can’t say whether I want to be chosen by them or not. But the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage tempts me a lot.\"","Damian nodded again. He was clearly interested in that place too. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage sounded dangerous, but for geniuses like them, danger and opportunity often meant the same thing.","A place where the strongest young monsters from all five universes gathered was exactly the kind of battlefield that could either kill them or push them far past their current limits.","Revona looked at them calmly and said, \"Training under the Seven Monarchs isn’t something we can control.\"","Everyone turned toward her.","She continued, \"The Monarchs are extremely arrogant people. I can tell you that much. They don’t care about reputation, background, bloodline, or how many people sing your praises in the Divine Realm. Their choices are strange, and their standards are even stranger. If even one of us gets chosen by them, that would already count as a huge stroke of luck.\"","Max looked at her. \"You seem to know a lot about them.\"","Revona nodded slightly. \"I know them better than anyone else here.\"","There was no arrogance in how she said it. She stated it like a plain fact.","\"I remember fighting one of the Monarchs in one of my past lives,\" she said. \"I haven’t fully unlocked the memories from that lifetime, but I remember enough to say they’re not ordinary powerful beings. Their strength, their personalities, and even the way they look at the world all sit apart from normal experts.\"","A faint trace of memory crossed her eyes.","\"They’re the kind of people who won’t look twice at you unless something about you catches their interest.\"","Max thought for a moment, then asked, \"Does any of the Seven Monarchs cultivate the body?\"","Revona looked at him and shook her head. \"Not that I remember.\"","Max’s gaze shifted slightly.","Revona added, \"But I can’t say for sure. My memories from that lifetime are incomplete. There might be a Monarch who walks the body cultivation path, or one who understands it even if it’s not their main focus. I only remember fragments, so I can’t give you a definite answer.\"","\"I understand,\" Max said with a nod.","His thoughts drifted back to Saint Reiner’s words. The path beyond the Seven Divine Veins. If one of the Seven Monarchs really had knowledge about that path, getting chosen by them would be extremely valuable to him.","But like Revona had said, the Monarchs wouldn’t take on disciples or students just because someone wanted to learn from them. They’d choose based on their own mysterious standards.","Max quietly weighed his options. If one of the Seven Monarchs picked him, he could train under them for a while before heading to the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. If none of them showed interest, he’d go straight to the pilgrimage.","Either way, he had no intention of sitting inside the Primordial Race for five hundred years growing under protection. That kind of path might raise his cultivation quickly, but it didn’t suit him.","He’d gotten stronger through danger, battle, inheritance, risk, and the constant pressure of enemies. A protected path would only dull the edge he’d built up.","The group kept discussing their choices for a little longer. Orion clearly leaned toward the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. Damian also seemed set on going there if no Monarch picked him. Ervin stayed curious about the unknown opportunities beyond the Wall of Eternity.","Morgana looked entertained by the idea of meeting geniuses from the Devil, Spirit, Angel, and Dragon Universes. Revona stayed calm, but Max could tell she’d already made her decision internally.","After the discussion wound down, the ten geniuses gradually went their separate ways. Some headed back to their assigned rooms. Some went to ask the Primordial attendants questions. Some left to prepare their cultivation, weapons, or mental state for whatever came next.","Max didn’t head back to his room right away. There were still things he needed to sort out.","He walked through the ancient corridors of the Primordial Ancestral Domain, following an aura he’d sensed earlier. Compared to the council domain and the training chambers, this part of the ancestral domain felt quieter.","Golden mist drifted between the pillars, and ancient symbols flowed across the walls like slow-moving streams. The deeper Max walked, the more he felt the Primordial Bloodline inside his body respond to the surroundings.","After a while, he found Sarvion standing beside a stone terrace. The terrace overlooked a vast primordial valley below.","In the distance, law rivers flowed through the sky, and floating mountains drifted silently above the clouds. Sarvion stood with his hands behind his back, his expression calm, as if he’d already known Max would show up.","\"You have questions,\" Sarvion said without turning around.","Max wasn’t surprised. He walked forward and stopped beside him. \"I do.\"","Sarvion glanced at him. \"Ask.\""]},{"number":2020,"title":"Chapter 2020: Slow Awakening of Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline!","paragraphs":["Max didn’t waste time. \"It’s about my Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline.\"","Sarvion’s eyes moved slightly, but he stayed silent.","Max continued, \"I know it’s supposed to be the highest level of Primordial Bloodline. I can feel it bringing me closer to the laws, strengthening my elemental control, boosting the power of my Pseudo Cosmic Paths, and letting me use the ability I awakened through it. But somehow it still feels weaker than I expected.\"","He frowned slightly.","\"I don’t mean it’s weak. It’s not. But given how powerful the Primordial Race is supposed to be, and given that Tier 4 is the highest bloodline level, I feel like I’m only touching the surface. Other geniuses with lower-tier bloodlines seem to have awakened their abilities more fully, while mine still feels incomplete.\"","Sarvion listened quietly. Then he smiled faintly.","\"That’s because it is incomplete.\"","Max’s eyes sharpened. \"What do you mean?\"","Sarvion turned to face him fully. \"The others awakened low-tier Primordial Bloodlines. Their bloodlines carry real power, but the potential locked inside them is limited compared to yours. Because of that, the training facility could push their bloodline abilities to fully awaken in a short time.\"","He paused briefly.","\"Your case runs differently.\"","Max stayed silent, listening carefully.","Sarvion continued, \"You carry the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline. That’s the highest level of Primordial Bloodline our race knows of. It stands on the same level as the bloodline the four Primarchs carry. In terms of potential, your bloodline isn’t something that can fully awaken in a few days, a few months, or even a few years.\"","Max’s expression shifted slightly.","Sarvion looked off into the distance.","\"The Primordial Bloodline isn’t just a source of strength. It’s a foundation tied to law, body, soul, origin, and the deeper structure of existence itself. A low-tier bloodline might awaken one or two abilities and settle into a stable state quickly. A higher-tier bloodline holds far more layers. Each layer carries more power, more law resonance, and more transformation.\"","His voice turned more serious.","\"A Tier 4 bloodline sits in a different category. Its potential runs too vast. If its full power woke up inside your body all at once, your body would most likely get destroyed.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed. \"Destroyed?\"","Sarvion nodded. \"Exploded into nothing, burned from the inside, torn apart by law pressure, or crushed by origin force. The exact result would depend on how the awakening happened, but none of those outcomes would feel good.\"","Max fell silent. He’d already gone through bloodline combustion during the forced awakening inside the training chamber. Even with his powerful physique, his Dimensional Sovereign Body, his Divine Veins, and all his other foundations, that process had still hurt badly.","If what he’d awakened so far was only a small slice of his Tier 4 bloodline, he could only imagine how terrifying the full awakening would feel.","Sarvion continued, \"That’s why your awakening feels slow. It’s not because your bloodline is weak. It’s because it’s too strong to awaken carelessly. As your cultivation realm climbs, as your body grows stronger, as your soul stabilizes, and as your comprehension of the laws deepens, the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline will awaken bit by bit.\"","He looked at Max calmly.","\"Each stage will reveal more of its strength. The Primordial Flames are only one manifestation. Your closeness to the laws is another. The boost to your Pseudo Cosmic Paths is another. There will be more changes down the road, but your body has to grow strong enough to handle them first.\"","Max nodded slowly. Now it made sense. His Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline wasn’t weaker than he’d expected. He’d just expected it to behave like an ordinary bloodline ability.","The lower-tier bloodlines of the others had awakened faster because they carried less hidden depth. His bloodline stayed asleep in layers because its full potential was too much for his current body to hold.","\"That makes sense,\" Max said.","Sarvion smiled lightly. \"Good that you asked. A lot of young geniuses get this wrong. They feel let down when a supreme bloodline doesn’t immediately hand them overwhelming abilities. They don’t realize the strongest bloodlines are often the slowest to fully awaken. The deeper the bloodline, the more careful the awakening has to be.\"","Max looked thoughtful. That explanation matched his current path too. His body already stood stronger than most cultivators at his realm, but even so, the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline still had to awaken slowly.","That meant he needed to strengthen his body even further if he wanted to draw out its full potential.","That led him to his next question.","\"Sarvion,\" Max said, \"does the Primordial Race have any cultivation arts or techniques tied to the body cultivation path beyond the Seven Divine Veins?\"","Sarvion’s expression shifted slightly. This time, he didn’t answer right away. He looked at Max with a bit more seriousness. \"You’ve opened the Seven Divine Veins?\"","\"Five of them,\" Max replied. \"Origin, Vitality, Speed, Strength, and Resilience.\"","Sarvion’s eyes narrowed faintly. For the first time, Max saw real surprise cross his face.","\"The fifth vein,\" Sarvion said softly. \"So Saint Reiner’s inheritance actually reached that level in your hands.\"","Max nodded. \"He told me the Seven Divine Veins are only a foundation for a higher body cultivation path, but he doesn’t know much about what’s beyond them. He said the Primordial Race might have records.\"","Sarvion stayed quiet for a few breaths. Then he said, \"The Primordial Race does hold a complete Seven Divine Veins cultivation art.\"","Max’s eyes sharpened.","Sarvion continued, \"It’s one of the ancient body cultivation methods preserved in our records. Very few people cultivate it, because opening the veins demands an absurd foundation, extreme pain tolerance, rare resources, and a body capable of surviving repeated transformation. Even among Primordials, very few have ever gotten far with it.\"","He looked at Max again.","\"As for a technique beyond the Seven Divine Veins, I’m not sure.\"","Max frowned slightly.","Sarvion said, \"I know there are records mentioning higher body cultivation paths. I also know some ancient Primordial experts believed the Seven Divine Veins weren’t the end. But whether we actually hold a complete technique beyond them, I can’t say. Information at that level would be stored somewhere I don’t usually access casually.\"","\"Where?\" Max asked."]},{"number":2021,"title":"Chapter 2021: Codex Library!","paragraphs":["\"The Codex Library,\" Sarvion replied.","That name made Max’s eyes shift slightly.","Sarvion continued, \"The Codex Library is one of the oldest record halls of the Primordial Race. It holds ancient techniques, lost histories, war records, bloodline studies, cosmic path theories, forbidden cultivation methods, and fragments recovered from ruins older than many of the current forces in the Divine Realm. If there’s information about a body cultivation path beyond the Seven Divine Veins, it’ll most likely be there.\"","He paused before adding, \"But the Codex Library isn’t a place that just hands you answers. Some records stay sealed. Some require authority. Some respond only to bloodline level. Some only open if your path resonates with them. Since you carry the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline, you should get access to a lot of areas, but how much you actually find will come down to you.\"","Max nodded with understanding. \"Then I’ll go there.\"","Sarvion smiled faintly. \"That would be wise. Before you choose between the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage and the Seven Monarchs, you should understand your own foundation as much as you can. Your body, your bloodline, and your path are all unusual. If you find even a small clue about what comes after the Seven Divine Veins, it might change how you prepare for the future.\"","Max looked toward the distant law rivers flowing across the sky. The path ahead had grown clearer, but also much bigger. His Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline hadn’t fully awakened. The Seven Divine Veins weren’t the end.","The Codex Library might hold the next clue. And in one week, the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage would open.","Max turned back to Sarvion and gave a slight nod. \"Thank you.\"","Sarvion looked at Max calmly. \"Don’t thank me yet.\"","Max raised his brows slightly.","Sarvion turned away from the stone terrace and started walking toward the inner halls of the Primordial Ancestral Domain. \"Let me take you to the Codex Library.\"","Max followed without hesitation.","The two of them left the terrace behind and moved through a long corridor filled with quiet golden mist. Compared to the paths Max had walked before, this route felt even older. No attendants, no guards, no young Primordials moving around.","The walls on both sides were made of dark bronze stone, and countless ancient symbols were carved into them so deeply they looked less like inscriptions and more like wounds left by time.","As Max walked, he felt the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline inside him responding again. It wasn’t a powerful reaction, but it stayed constant. The bloodline pulsed once every few steps, almost like it recognized the direction they were heading.","The deeper they went, the more Max sensed that this part of the Primordial Ancestral Domain wasn’t built for display. It wasn’t meant to impress outsiders. It was a place where the Primordial Race kept things they didn’t casually show to others.","Sarvion didn’t talk much while leading the way. Max stayed quiet too.","After a while, they arrived at an ancient door that looked far smaller than Max expected. Compared to the enormous gate of the training facility, this door looked almost ordinary. It stood only twice the height of a normal person and was made of dull gray stone.","No golden dragons carved into it, no towering statues, no grand formation circles spreading across the floor. Only a single symbol sat engraved at its center.","It showed the image of an open book, with a rotating star inside it.","Max looked at the symbol for a moment. The longer he stared, the stranger it became. At first it looked like a simple carving. Then he realized the star inside the book was actually moving. Its light stayed faint, but it seemed to hold countless words flowing within it.","Sarvion stopped in front of the door. \"This is the entrance to the Codex Library,\" he said.","Max glanced at the small stone door and frowned slightly. \"This is the library?\"","Sarvion smiled faintly. \"Only the entrance.\"","He raised his hand and placed his palm against the open-book symbol. The symbol lit up. A soft golden light spread across the dull gray stone, and the door slowly opened without a sound. Beyond it, there was no corridor, no chamber, and no visible library hall.","There was only darkness. Not empty darkness, but a deep, layered darkness filled with countless faint lights, like stars hidden behind mist.","Sarvion stepped forward. Max followed him through the doorway.","The moment he crossed the threshold, the world changed. The corridor disappeared. The stone door disappeared. Even the sense of standing inside the Primordial Ancestral Domain disappeared.","Max found himself inside an enormous pocket dimension. His eyes widened slightly. The Codex Library wasn’t a building. It was a separate space, a vast, silent, impossible space built to preserve the knowledge of the Primordial Race.","There was no floor beneath him in any ordinary sense. Instead, he stood on a wide transparent path made of condensed light.","Beneath that path stretched an endless dark void filled with floating books, jade slips, crystal tablets, ancient scrolls, sealed boxes, stone slabs, research files, law fragments, inheritance orbs, memory crystals, and strange objects Max couldn’t immediately identify.","Above him, the same sight stretched endlessly upward. Everywhere he looked, knowledge floated in the air. Some books drifted slowly with their pages open, glowing words rising from them like mist. Some scrolls sat wrapped in chains of light.","Some jade slips rotated inside small transparent cubes. Some crystal tablets released faint images of ancient battles, body cultivation diagrams, bloodline structures, formation patterns, and cosmic path theories.","Some inheritance orbs gave off such heavy pressure that Max knew they held terrifying techniques or memories left behind by ancient experts.","At first glance, the whole place looked chaotic. It seemed like countless books, records, inheritances, and research files had been tossed into the air by some careless giant and left to drift wherever they landed.","There were shelves, but the shelves didn’t stand on the ground. They floated in layers across the pocket dimension. Some stood vertical. Some lay horizontal. Some turned slowly like wheels. Some spiraled around invisible pillars. Some arranged themselves in rings that rotated around larger inheritance crystals."]},{"number":2022,"title":"Chapter 2022: A Strange Library Indeed!","paragraphs":["It looked scattered. It looked disordered. It looked impossible to search.","But after Max stared for a few moments, his eyes slowly narrowed. That wasn’t the case. The Codex Library only looked chaotic on the surface. In truth, everything had its place. Every book, scroll, tablet, crystal, and inheritance object seemed to float according to a hidden order.","Their positions weren’t based on something as simple as size, shape, age, or type. Instead, deeper connections seemed to decide where they sat. Records related to bloodline resonance floated near body cultivation studies.","Ancient war reports drifted close to cosmic path theories. Sealing inheritances gathered around spatial research files. Some law diagrams sat beside battle records, as if the library itself understood which techniques had been born from which wars.","Max felt like he was looking at a living mind made of knowledge. The arrangement was strange, but not random. It only looked messy to someone who couldn’t see the logic behind it.","\"This place,\" Max muttered.","Sarvion glanced at him. \"Strange, isn’t it?\"","Max nodded. \"It looks like everything’s scattered everywhere, but that’s not really true. Every record here feels like it’s exactly where it should be.\"","Sarvion smiled slightly. \"Good observation.\"","He looked out across the vast pocket dimension, his expression carrying a rare trace of reverence.","\"The Codex Library is one of the oldest treasures of the Primordial Race. It doesn’t just store books. It stores knowledge, inheritance, memory, research, history, failures, warnings, and even incomplete ideas left behind by experts who died before finishing their paths.\"","His voice softened slightly.","\"Some of the records here were written by Primarchs. Some were left behind by ancient elders who no longer carry names in the outside world. Some got recovered from ruined star realms after the last war. Some came from forbidden zones. Some are fragments taken from enemies. Some aren’t even written in our language, but the library keeps them anyway because their meaning might turn useful one day.\"","Max looked around silently. He could feel it. This place was more than a library. It was the memory of the Primordial Race.","Sarvion continued, \"The order here isn’t something ordinary people can grasp at first glance. The Codex Library arranges knowledge based on resonance, origin, usage, danger, compatibility, and hidden relationships between different paths. That’s why it looks scattered. A body cultivation record might float beside a bloodline study because the person who created it discovered a certain bloodline could endure a certain body refinement method. A war record might sit near a sealing art because that sealing art got created to counter an enemy from that war. A failed technique might sit beside a successful inheritance because one explains the weakness of the other.\"","Max’s eyes deepened as he listened. That explained why the library felt so strange. Its structure wasn’t built for convenience. It was built for understanding. A normal library placed records where they were easy to find. The Codex Library placed records where their meanings connected.","Sarvion raised his hand. A small golden light appeared above his palm.","\"The Codex Library will respond to your authority, bloodline, and intent. Since you carry the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline, plenty of areas won’t reject you. That doesn’t mean every record will open for you, though. Some inheritances need specific compatibility. Some need contribution. Some stay sealed because they’re dangerous. Some can’t be read unless your soul can withstand what’s inside them.\"","Max looked at a distant black scroll wrapped in nine layers of golden chains. Even from far away, he could feel a faint pressure coming off it.","Sarvion followed his gaze and said, \"For example, that scroll holds a failed attempt to create an artificial cosmic path from devil corruption and primordial origin. The expert who wrote it died before finishing the theory. Three people tried studying it afterward. Two lost control of their laws, and one ended up half-corrupted before getting sealed. It stays here because even a failed path can teach future generations what not to do.\"","Max pulled his gaze away. \"I understand.\"","Sarvion nodded. \"Good. Curiosity helps here, but carelessness gets dangerous.\"","He pointed deeper into the pocket dimension. \"Records related to the Seven Divine Veins are stored across several layers. The complete Seven Divine Veins cultivation art shouldn’t be hard for you to access with your bloodline authority. But if you’re looking for something beyond the Seven Divine Veins, the library might not show it to you directly.\"","Max frowned slightly. \"Why not?\"","\"Because the Codex Library responds to intent, but it also responds to readiness,\" Sarvion replied. \"If a record about that path truly exists, it might only appear once your body, bloodline, and comprehension grow strong enough to reach it. You’ve opened five Divine Veins, so you might be close, but close doesn’t always mean enough.\"","Max looked out into the endless sea of floating knowledge. Books drifted like stars. Scrolls turned like sleeping dragons. Inheritance crystals pulsed in the distance like ancient hearts. Somewhere in this impossible place, there might be a clue to the path beyond the Seven Divine Veins.","His eyes settled into calm focus. \"Then I’ll search until I find something.\"","Sarvion looked at him for a moment. Then he smiled faintly. \"That’s the right attitude.\"","He raised his hand again, and a thin thread of golden light flew out from his palm. The light entered the vast library, passing through floating shelves, spinning scrolls, and rings of ancient tablets.","A few breaths later, several records responded from a distance. They glowed softly before drifting toward Max and Sarvion.","Books. Jade slips. Stone tablets. A crystal file holding anatomical diagrams. A sealed inheritance orb with seven faint lights rotating inside it.","One by one, they stopped in front of Max.","Sarvion said, \"Start with these. They’re the records most directly connected to the Seven Divine Veins. Read them carefully. Don’t only look for the final answer. Sometimes the path beyond a technique hides in why the technique got created in the first place.\"","Max nodded and reached toward the first ancient book. The moment his fingers touched its cover, the five Divine Veins inside his body pulsed at the same time.","Origin. Vitality. Speed. Strength. Resilience.","The book trembled faintly, as if it recognized him.","\"This book must hold the original complete Seven Divine Veins,\" Max muttered as he opened it and started reading.","Even though he already carried the complete version Saint Reiner had created, Max couldn’t help but wonder about the original, full version of the Seven Divine Veins."]},{"number":2023,"title":"Chapter 2023: A Reaction!","paragraphs":["As Max read through the original complete Seven Divine Veins technique, his expression slowly grew more thoughtful.","The technique was far more complex than the one Saint Reiner had created. At their core, both methods led to the same result. Both aimed to open the Seven Divine Veins inside the body.","Both strengthened the physical foundation through Origin, Vitality, Speed, Strength, Resilience, and the two remaining veins Max had yet to unlock. Both treated the body not as a simple vessel for energy, but as a divine structure that could be refined, expanded, and pushed past ordinary limits.","But the gap between them was enormous.","Saint Reiner’s version came out clean, direct, and terrifyingly practical. It explained the process clearly. It focused on what needed doing, what resources were required, what dangers would come up, and how the body should endure each transformation.","It was the kind of technique built by someone who’d spent centuries studying an incomplete path, cutting away unnecessary confusion, fixing flaws through countless attempts, and rebuilding the method so someone else could actually cultivate it.","The original complete Seven Divine Veins technique read completely differently. It felt like a divine scripture.","Every sentence seemed to carry several layers of meaning. Every diagram held hidden changes. Even the descriptions of the veins weren’t simple instructions, but profound explanations of how the physical body connected to law, origin, soul, vitality, and the deeper structure of existence.","Some parts sounded less like a cultivation method and more like the thoughts of an ancient being who’d already reached a height where ordinary language could no longer properly describe the body.","Max could follow it, but even he had to slow down to read it. If a normal body cultivator tried studying this technique, they’d probably spend years puzzling over a single Chapter and still miss its true meaning.","That didn’t mean Saint Reiner’s version had flaws. Actually, Max felt the opposite.","Saint Reiner’s version stood out precisely because it had taken something impossibly profound and turned it into a method someone could actually cultivate directly.","The original technique had likely come from an existence at the peak of body cultivation, maybe someone so powerful that opening the Seven Divine Veins was just a natural step on their path.","Saint Reiner, on the other hand, had used research, battle experience, ancient fragments, and centuries of study to rebuild the technique from an incomplete inheritance.","One was a scripture written from the height of a god-like expert. The other was a path carved open by a mortal genius who refused to quit. Both held value. Both carried real power. They were simply different.","After a long while, Max closed the ancient book in his hand.","\"But there’s still no mention of a body cultivation technique beyond the Seven Divine Veins,\" he muttered.","His brows furrowed slightly. He’d read the complete technique carefully from start to finish. He hadn’t skipped a single diagram, note, warning, or hidden annotation.","The text confirmed the Seven Divine Veins as an extraordinary body cultivation path, and it went deeper than Saint Reiner’s version in plenty of areas.","But it never clearly said what came after all seven veins opened. There were hints. There were vague phrases. There were lines talking about preparing the body for a higher transformation. But there was no name, no complete method, and no direct answer.","Max placed the book back into the air, and it slowly floated away, drifting back to its strange assigned spot inside the Codex Library.","He started searching more broadly. The Codex Library stretched out beyond imagination. Books, scrolls, jade slips, crystal tablets, stone slabs, research files, inheritance orbs, sealed diagrams, and fragments of ancient records floated through the pocket dimension in countless layers.","Some drifted past him like quiet birds. Some turned slowly in the distance like planets circling invisible suns. Some stayed wrapped in chains of light, refusing to open even as Max approached.","Max moved through the transparent pathways, scanning everything around him. He searched for records tied to body cultivation. He searched for anything related to divine veins, immortal physiques, primordial bodies, origin bones, bloodline vessels, law-forged flesh, and ancient body transformation.","Whenever a book or jade slip responded to his intent, he pulled it over and read through it.","Some records described rare body tempering methods. Some explained how Primordials strengthened their physiques through bloodline resonance. Some were research notes on why certain body cultivation paths collapsed after reaching the Divine King Realm. Some held battle reports about ancient experts whose bodies were strong enough to resist cosmic path attacks.","Valuable knowledge sat everywhere. Yet none of it gave him the answer he wanted.","Hours passed. Max didn’t grow impatient. He understood a place like the Codex Library wouldn’t simply hand him what he wanted just because he asked. Sarvion had already warned him.","Some knowledge here responded to authority. Some responded to bloodline. Some responded to readiness. Some stayed hidden not because no one could find them, but because finding them required the right person at the right moment.","Max kept moving deeper. The scenery around him grew stranger the farther he went. The floating shelves looked older. The light grew dimmer. The books and tablets here weren’t cleanly preserved anymore.","Plenty were damaged, cracked, burned, or incomplete. Some pages floated without covers. Some scrolls were torn in half. Some stone tablets had missing corners. Some jade slips looked so old their surfaces had lost their original color.","This part of the Codex Library felt different. It didn’t feel like a section for complete inheritances. It felt like a graveyard of forgotten knowledge.","Max slowed his pace. His five Divine Veins pulsed faintly inside his body. Origin. Vitality. Speed. Strength. Resilience. The reaction started weak, so faint that Max almost brushed it off. But after a few more steps, the pulse came again, slightly stronger than before.","Max stopped. His eyes narrowed.","The Codex Library stayed silent around him. Books floated through the air in their strange order. Ancient scrolls drifted in slow circles. Faded jade slips turned gently in the darkness. Everything looked scattered, yet everything still carried that hidden arrangement that made this place feel almost alive.","Then Max noticed something. At the far corner of this forgotten layer, near a spot where the light barely reached, a single withered page floated alone.","It looked insignificant. The page was old, yellowed, and torn at the edges. It had no cover, no protective seal, no glowing inscription, and no powerful aura. Next to the inheritance orbs, golden scrolls, and crystal tablets around it, the page looked like a useless remnant that should have turned to dust long ago.","But it kept drifting in place. It didn’t move with the other records. It floated in a small, quiet circle at the very edge of the library space, as if waiting for someone to notice it.","Max’s eyes fixed on it. The five Divine Veins inside his body trembled again. This time, the reaction came through clear.","Max moved toward the withered page. The closer he got, the stronger the response grew. His Origin Vein pulsed deep inside his body. His Vitality Vein stirred with warm life force. His Speed Vein sent a faint current through his limbs. His Strength Vein tightened his muscles slightly. His Resilience Vein turned firm, as if bracing his body for some unknown pressure.","Max reached out. The withered page drifted toward him on its own. The moment his fingers touched it, all five Divine Veins trembled at once.","Max’s expression changed. The reaction wasn’t violent, but it ran deep. It felt like the five veins had recognized something far above them, something they were connected to but hadn’t yet reached.","The sensation wasn’t like finding a technique of the same level. It felt like standing before a gate that had always existed beyond the Seven Divine Veins, hidden behind mist until this exact moment."]},{"number":2024,"title":"Chapter 2024: Eternal Body!","paragraphs":["Max slowly lowered his gaze to the page. Very few words remained written on it. Most of the text had faded away, leaving only broken marks and incomplete lines. But at the very top of the withered page, one name stayed clear.","Eternal Body.","The moment Max read those two words, his five Divine Veins shook again. This time, the tremor spread through his entire body. His blood slowed for an instant. His bones seemed to grow heavier. His flesh tightened, and his soul felt like it had just heard an ancient echo from a path buried beyond time.","Even his Dimensional Sovereign Body reacted faintly, not with rejection, but with a strange silence, as if it too were paying attention to the name written on the page.","Eternal Body.","Max stared at those words. Now he was certain. Whatever this page mentioned tied directly into the body cultivation path beyond the Seven Divine Veins. The complete Seven Divine Veins technique hadn’t given him the answer. Saint Reiner hadn’t known the answer.","Even Sarvion had only told him to search the Codex Library and see what turned up. Yet here, in a forgotten corner of this pocket dimension, a withered page had responded to the five Divine Veins inside him.","That couldn’t be a coincidence.","Max held the page carefully. The old paper felt fragile, but it didn’t crumble. Instead, a faint warmth spread from it into his palm, then flowed toward the five Divine Veins in his body.","His eyes deepened.","\"So this is it,\" Max muttered softly.","The path beyond the Seven Divine Veins. Or at least, the first clue to it.","He looked once more at the name written at the top of the page. Eternal Body. A faint excitement rose in his heart, but he quickly pushed it down. He knew this was only a fragment.","The page didn’t hold a complete technique. Most of its contents were missing, and even the remaining lines were barely readable. But for Max, a name alone was already enough to prove Saint Reiner had been right.","The Seven Divine Veins weren’t the end. They were only the foundation.","Max held the withered page carefully and left the Codex Library. The moment he stepped out of the pocket dimension, the endless sea of floating books, scrolls, jade slips, inheritance orbs, research files, and ancient fragments disappeared behind him.","The strange silence of that impossible library faded, and the familiar aura of the Primordial Ancestral Domain returned. The dull gray stone door closed behind him without a sound, and the symbol of the open book with a rotating star slowly dimmed until it looked like an ordinary carving again.","Sarvion was still waiting outside. He stood quietly in the corridor with his hands behind his back, as though he hadn’t moved at all since Max went in.","The golden mist around him flowed gently, and the ancient symbols on the walls flickered with soft light, but Sarvion’s expression stayed calm and unreadable.","When Max walked out, Sarvion turned his gaze toward him. \"How was it?\" he asked.","Max didn’t answer right away. He looked down at the withered page in his hand. Compared to the countless grand records inside the Codex Library, this page looked almost pitiful. It was old, fragile, yellowed by time, and torn along the edges.","Most of the writing had faded away, leaving only broken marks and incomplete traces. Yet the name at the top of the page still carried a strange weight Max couldn’t ignore.","Eternal Body.","Those two words had made all five Divine Veins inside him tremble. That alone proved this paper wasn’t ordinary.","After a brief silence, Max held out the page and handed it to Sarvion.","\"I found something,\" he said. \"Can you tell me where this paper came from?\"","Sarvion took the withered page. At first he only looked at it casually, but the moment his eyes landed on the name at the top, his expression shifted slightly. It wasn’t shock, but a clear trace of seriousness crossed his gaze now.","He didn’t explain right away. Instead, he held the page in the air between them and released a thin stream of primordial energy into it.","\"Let me check the records,\" Sarvion said.","The page floated by itself. A moment later, purple screens appeared around it. They weren’t ordinary formation projections. Each screen was made of condensed information runes, with lines of ancient text moving across them rapidly.","Some showed dates. Some showed names. Some showed storage locations. Some showed records of who had touched, studied, sealed, or transferred the page in the past.","The screens circled the withered paper like a group of searching eyes, scanning its origin from every possible trace left behind.","Max watched silently. The Codex Library was strange enough on its own, but now he realized even a single damaged page inside it carried its own recorded history.","The Primordial Race had preserved not just techniques and inheritances, but also the paths those things had traveled to end up in their possession. Every fragment had a source, every relic had a trail, and every broken record still counted as part of a much larger chain of knowledge.","Several breaths passed. The purple screens kept shifting. Then Sarvion’s eyes narrowed slightly.","\"I found it.\"","Max’s gaze sharpened.","Sarvion looked away from the floating screens and turned to him. \"This paper got brought back by a Primordial who entered the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage for tempering.\"","Max’s expression shifted. \"Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.\"","He repeated the name softly. For a moment, he looked at the withered page again. He wasn’t disappointed. If anything, this answer only made his resolve firmer. He’d entered the Codex Library searching for clues about the body cultivation path beyond the Seven Divine Veins, and he’d only found a single broken page.","That page didn’t contain a complete technique. It didn’t tell him how to cultivate the Eternal Body. It didn’t explain what came after opening all seven Divine Veins. It only gave him a name and a direction.","But sometimes a direction was enough.","The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. That was where this page had turned up. That meant the clue he needed didn’t sit fully within the Primordial Race, nor did it stay hidden in some ordinary ancient record of the Divine Realm.","It came from that mysterious place beyond the Wall of Eternity, the place where geniuses from all five universes gathered, the place where gods were said to have fallen, the place packed with opportunities, inheritances, dangers, and ancient remnants beyond anything found in the Divine Realm.","Max slowly closed his fingers around the page again after Sarvion handed it back. His eyes deepened. He’d already planned to enter the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage before this. Even without this clue, that place gave him the best path to grow stronger quickly.","The Divine Realm wasn’t enough for him anymore. Training safely under the Primordial Race didn’t suit him. If no Monarch chose him, the pilgrimage would naturally become his next stop.","But now his reason for going ran deeper. He wasn’t just entering to compete with the geniuses of the five universes anymore. He wasn’t just entering to grab opportunities and prepare for the coming war. He was going to search for the Eternal Body. He was going to search for the path beyond the Seven Divine Veins."]},{"number":2025,"title":"Chapter 2025: Back to Four Sacred Clans!","paragraphs":["Sarvion watched him quietly and seemed to catch what he was thinking.","\"The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage isn’t a place where answers come easy,\" Sarvion said. \"If this page came from there, the complete inheritance might be hidden in some dangerous region, sealed inside an ancient ruin, held by another race, or scattered across different trials. It’s also possible only this fragment survives.\"","Max looked at him. \"But it’s still a clue.\"","Sarvion nodded. \"Yes. And for someone walking a lost path, a clue is sometimes worth more than a complete technique that doesn’t even belong to them.\"","Max stared at the withered page for a long moment. The five Divine Veins inside his body sat quiet now, but he could still remember how they’d trembled when he first read the name Eternal Body. That reaction couldn’t be false.","After a while, Max carefully folded the page and stored it away. His decision was clear now. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage was no longer just one of his options. It was the place he had to go.","\"Sarvion,\" Max said calmly, \"I’ve decided.\"","Sarvion looked at him.","Max’s eyes stayed steady. \"I’m going to the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.\"","Sarvion didn’t look surprised. Instead, he gave a faint smile. \"I figured you would.\"","After talking with Sarvion a little longer, Max parted ways with him and headed straight back to the room assigned to him inside the Primordial Ancestral Domain.","For now, nothing urgent remained for him to do. Arvantos had already laid out the three possible paths. Sarvion had explained the truth behind his Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline.","The Codex Library had handed him a clue about the Eternal Body, and that clue pointed straight to the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. Unless one of the Seven Monarchs chose him, Max’s next destination was already set.","He only had to wait. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage would open in roughly six days. For most people, six days wasn’t much. For Max, six days gave him more than enough time to make real progress.","The moment he entered his room, Max activated the isolation formation and stepped into the Dimension of Time. The quiet space of his personal dimension unfolded around him, and the shift in time flow immediately gave him what the outside world couldn’t.","He didn’t waste a single moment. He started training with his Pseudo Cosmic Paths, refining his control over the Emotion Severing Path, Divine King Punishment, the Devouring Flames Domain, the Primordial Flame Path, the Ice Path, and the Light Path.","Time flowed differently inside the dimension. Max moved from one path to another with complete focus. He practiced the Ten Void Sealing Art until the ten void rings responded with even greater precision.","He compressed Primordial Flames in one ring and black flames in another, then compared how both powers behaved under the pressure of void sealing. He used Dragonheart to test how the Emotion Severing Path flowed through his sword strikes.","He refined his use of Divine King Punishment, making sure the seven-colored lightning didn’t just explode outward with brute force, but came down with judgment and purpose.","Three days passed like that.","On the fourth day, Arvantos summoned all ten geniuses again. They gathered in the same quiet hall inside the Primordial Ancestral Domain.","This time, the atmosphere felt different from before. Everyone already knew the Seven Monarchs would make their decision before the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage opened, and even though most of them stayed quiet, their eyes showed real anticipation.","Arvantos stood at the front of the hall with a solemn expression.","\"The Seven Monarchs have made their decision,\" he said.","The ten geniuses immediately went serious.","Arvantos looked at each of them before continuing, \"They’ve chosen three among you.\"","The hall went silent.","\"Orion. Kaiden. Morgana.\"","Those three names changed the expressions of everyone else.","Orion blinked, then pointed at himself. \"Me?\"","Kaiden’s expression stayed steady, but his eyes clearly moved. Morgana raised her brows slightly, then smiled with interest, like she’d just heard something amusing and dangerous at the same time.","The others looked surprised too.","Max glanced toward the three of them thoughtfully. He hadn’t expected the Monarchs to pick Orion, Kaiden, and Morgana out of everyone here, but after thinking back on what Revona had said, it didn’t seem too strange.","The Seven Monarchs didn’t choose by normal standards. Their eyes worked differently from ordinary experts, and what caught their interest might not be obvious to anyone else.","Revona smiled faintly from the side. \"Told you their choices were strange.\"","Orion recovered quickly and grinned. \"Strange or not, I’ll take it.\"","Damian folded his arms and looked at him. \"Try not to die under your Monarch’s training.\"","Orion’s grin stiffened slightly. \"That was unnecessary.\"","Morgana chuckled softly. \"No, I think that was very necessary.\"","Kaiden stayed calm, but his gaze had turned resolute. Whichever Monarch had chosen him, this was an opportunity countless geniuses in the Divine Realm would never get. He wasn’t going to waste it.","Soon, a Primordial expert entered the hall to take the three away. Before leaving, Orion looked back at Max and the others with a wide smile. \"Don’t fall too far behind while I’m gone.\"","Damian snorted. \"Worry about yourself.\"","Morgana gave everyone a casual wave, while Kaiden nodded once before following the Primordial expert out of the hall. A spatial passage opened in front of them, and the three chosen geniuses disappeared into it.","Only seven remained. Arvantos turned toward Max, Damian, Ervin, Revona, Rosaline, Rakan, Aurelian, and the others who hadn’t been chosen.","\"As for the rest of you,\" he said solemnly, \"I take it you’re planning to enter the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.\"","The seven geniuses nodded. None of them hesitated. The first path, staying with the Primordial Race and cultivating safely, didn’t suit them. The Monarch path was no longer in their hands. That left the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, the dangerous battlefield where the strongest young geniuses of all five universes would gather.","Arvantos looked at their faces and spoke in a heavier voice. \"In that case, you have one day to visit your loved ones and settle your personal matters.\"","The hall grew quieter.","\"There’s no telling what you’ll run into in the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. You might encounter geniuses from the Devil Race, Angel Race, Dragon Race, and Spirit Race. You might enter ruins that have killed people far stronger than you. You might find opportunities that change your whole future, but you might also run into dangers that don’t give you a second chance.\"","His gaze swept across them. \"The chance of death is very high.\"","No one looked away.","Arvantos continued, \"Use this one day well. Meet the people you want to meet. Say what you need to say. Prepare your weapons, steady your minds, and make sure you walk into that place without regret.\"","The seven geniuses nodded solemnly.","After saying this, Arvantos dismissed them and vanished from the hall.","Max and the others talked for a short while afterward. Nobody said much. The mood had turned heavier. Everyone had families, teachers, friends, clans, or people they wanted to see before heading off to a place where even their own survival wasn’t guaranteed.","One by one, they went their separate ways.","Max also left the Primordial Ancestral Domain and headed back to the Five Sacred Clan domain. This time, his arrival looked completely different. No one threatened him. No one blocked his path. No elder questioned his identity or tried to push him around with authority.","Instead, the guards and descendants of the Four Sacred Clans treated him with obvious restraint and respect. Some even lowered their heads as he passed. Their expressions stayed complicated, but none of them dared show open hostility."]},{"number":2026,"title":"Chapter 2026: Freya’s Concern!","paragraphs":["Max almost laughed. ’They flip their attitude pretty easily.’","Of course, he understood why. The truth about the Voidwalker Clan had already come out, and the devil crisis had pulled the whole Divine Realm’s attention elsewhere.","More importantly, Max’s strength and standing had shifted in everyone’s eyes. He’d awakened the Voidwalker inheritance, gotten a Primordial Bloodline, killed a devil at the 5th level of the Law Manifestation Realm in front of every major force, and survived a sneak attack from the Pearl of Abyss.","At this point, treating him like some ordinary outsider would just be foolish.","Max ignored the stares around him and headed straight for the Voidwalker Clan’s area. There he found Freya.","The moment he told her about his plans, her expression shifted several times.","\"Godslayer’s Pilgrimage,\" Freya said softly. Her face turned serious, but after a while, she nodded. \"That place actually suits you right now. There are plenty of opportunities there, and if you can survive them, your strength will grow way faster than it would inside the Divine Realm.\"","Max looked at her, a little surprised. The way Freya talked sounded too familiar. It didn’t sound like she’d just heard rumors about the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. It sounded like she knew the place from personal experience.","\"Have you been to the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage?\" Max asked.","Freya nodded. \"Yes.\"","Max’s eyes moved.","Freya smiled faintly. \"What do you think I’ve been doing since I ascended to the Divine Realm all these years?\"","She walked to the window and looked out at the distant Voidwalker grounds.","\"The moment I entered the Divine Realm and got my original strength back to its peak, I entered the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. That’s actually one of the reasons I couldn’t come find you sooner.\"","Her voice carried a trace of regret, but it quickly turned serious again.","\"And I’ll tell you this, Max, that place is insane. Geniuses from all five first races fight there over resources, inheritances, trials, ancient marks, and opportunities you won’t find anywhere else. The Devil Race, Spirit Race, Angel Race, Dragon Race, and our own universe all send their monsters there. Some of them are arrogant beyond belief. Some are terrifyingly strong. Some look harmless until they kill people without warning. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage really opened my eyes to how wide the world beyond our universe actually is.\"","Max listened quietly.","Freya turned back to him and smiled lightly. Then she stepped closer and patted his head.","\"But I know you’ll do just fine there.\"","Max immediately pulled her hand off his head. \"I’m not a kid anymore, Big Sis.\"","\"Is that so?\" Freya asked with a mischievous smile.","Max narrowed his eyes slightly. \"What’s with that look?\"","Freya’s smile widened. \"Where are Alice and Lenavira?\"","Max froze for a moment.","Freya looked at him with the expression of someone who already knew everything. \"I know you’ve been keeping them with you, but you should let them out now. You don’t know what you’ll run into in the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. That place is way too dangerous, and dragging them along would only put them at unnecessary risk. The safest place for them right now is right here, inside the Voidwalker Clan.\"","Max didn’t answer right away.","Freya’s expression softened a little. \"Back in Acaris, I treated Alice badly. I know that. I want to make it up to her properly.\"","Then she added with a faint smile, \"And I want to get to know Lenavira better too. After all, these two girls are going to be my brother’s future wives. As your elder sister, I should at least understand them, right?\"","Max’s face turned slightly red. \"Big Sis.\"","Freya ignored his embarrassment and kept going. \"With me here, I can guide them. The Voidwalker Clan has resources, inheritances, training grounds, and protection they can’t find anywhere else. By the time you get back, they should be able to reach at least the Law Manifestation Realm, maybe even higher if their progress goes well.\"","Max grew thoughtful. Freya’s teasing annoyed him, but the first part of what she said made sense. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage wasn’t a normal training ground. It was a place where the most dangerous geniuses of five universes gathered.","Alice and Lenavira were talented, but bringing them there right now wouldn’t help them. It would only expose them to dangers far beyond their current level.","Leaving them inside the Voidwalker Clan was the best choice.","After a moment, Max waved his hand. Space rippled beside him. Alice and Lenavira appeared out of nowhere.","Alice blinked in confusion and looked around. \"Max?\"","Her eyes moved across the unfamiliar surroundings. \"Where is this place?\"","Lenavira also looked around with wonder. The aura here felt far stronger than what she was used to, and even the space itself felt different. \"Is this the Four Sacred Clans you told us about?\"","Before Max could answer, Alice’s gaze landed on Freya. Her expression darkened immediately. She hadn’t forgotten what Freya had done to her back in Acaris. Even with the situation changed, even knowing Freya was Max’s sister, that memory wasn’t something she could just erase.","Freya noticed Alice’s expression and didn’t look away. For once, her smile turned gentler and quieter.","Max spoke before the atmosphere could get too stiff. \"Alice, Lenavira, this is indeed the Four Sacred Clans. More specifically, we’re inside the Voidwalker Clan.\"","Both women turned toward him.","Max then explained everything briefly. He told them about the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, the danger of that place, the geniuses from all five universes, and why he couldn’t bring them along this time.","He didn’t downplay how serious this was. Alice and Lenavira needed to understand this wasn’t some ordinary journey or a short training trip.","\"This place will be safer for both of you,\" Max said. \"Big Sis will help guide you, and the Voidwalker Clan has enough resources to support your cultivation.\"","Alice frowned. \"You’re leaving us here because it’s that dangerous?\"","Max nodded. \"Yes.\"","Lenavira’s expression turned worried. \"Then what about you?\"","Max smiled faintly. \"I’ll be fine.\"","Neither of them looked convinced.","Max added, \"But don’t worry about the others inside the Dimension of Genesis.\"","He walked toward a section of the wall and placed his palm against it. A faint silver light spread from his hand. Using Dimensional Anchor, Max created an anchor point connecting directly to the Dimension of Genesis.","The wall trembled slightly, and a circular portal slowly formed on its surface. The portal shimmered with layered spatial light, and beyond it, a faint trace of the Dimension of Genesis could be felt.","Alice and Lenavira looked at the portal in surprise.","\"This portal connects to the Dimension of Genesis,\" Max explained. \"You can go in and out through it. I’ve separated the Dimension of Genesis from myself and fixed it to this anchor for now, so even if something happens to me out there, the people inside won’t be affected.\"","The moment he said that, the worry in Alice and Lenavira’s eyes deepened. They might not fully grasp the scale of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, but they understood Max.","He’d never done something like this before. He’d never separated one of his dimensions from himself as a precaution. He’d never spoken like there was a real chance something might happen to him. The fact that he’d made these preparations told them more than his words ever could.","This journey was dangerous. Far more dangerous than anything he’d faced before.","Alice looked at him quietly. Lenavira lowered her gaze slightly. The room grew tense.","Seeing the heavy mood, Freya let out a small sigh and stepped toward the door.","\"You three should talk,\" she said. \"I’ll wait outside.\"","With that, she left the room and closed the door behind her, giving Max, Alice, and Lenavira the space they needed."]},{"number":2027,"title":"Chapter 2027: To Alice and Lenavira!","paragraphs":["No sooner had Freya left the room than Alice turned toward Max.","Her eyes were full of worry.","\"Do you really have to go if it’s this dangerous?\"","A heavy silence filled the room. The question sounded simple, but it carried a lot of weight. Alice wasn’t asking because she didn’t understand his ambition. She was asking because she understood him too well. Max had always walked toward danger whenever danger promised strength, and even though that strength had protected them plenty of times, it had also put him on a path where every step seemed sharper than the one before.","Lenavira stood beside Alice without a word, but her expression carried the same fear.","Max looked at both of them. For a moment, he didn’t answer. Then he took a deep breath and nodded lightly. \"I have to.\"","Alice’s fingers tightened slightly.","Max continued in a quiet voice, \"The situation’s already changed. The devils have gotten into our universe, the Wall of Eternity’s been pierced, and nobody knows how long this current peace will hold. If I stay here and cultivate normally, I might get strong someday, but that day might come too late.\"","He looked at Alice first, then at Lenavira.","\"I need strength. Not just for myself, but for both of you, for Big Sis, for the people inside the Dimension of Genesis, and for everything I want to protect.\"","His voice dropped lower.","\"And you both know about my parents. My mother and father are still trapped. I haven’t forgotten what happened to them. I haven’t forgotten who destroyed my childhood. If I want to rescue them, if I want revenge, if I want to stand in front of the people who took everything from me and make them answer for it, then I can’t afford to grow slowly.\"","Alice bit her lower lip. She wanted to tell him not to go. She wanted to tell him that revenge, strength, destiny, even the fate of the universe, didn’t matter more than his own life. But looking into his eyes, she knew those words wouldn’t stop him. Max wasn’t leaving because he wanted to abandon them. He was leaving because he believed this was the only way he could one day come back without fear.","Lenavira finally spoke. \"You always risk your life for strength,\" she said quietly. \"More strength, greater strength, then even more strength after that. When are you going to stop doing this and just live normally? When are you going to start caring about yourself? When are you going to look after yourself the way you look after everyone else?\"","Max’s heart tightened slightly. He didn’t know how to answer right away, because Lenavira wasn’t wrong. He’d thrown himself into danger again and again. He’d challenged enemies stronger than himself, accepted trials that could’ve killed him, hidden pain beneath calm smiles, and kept moving forward even as every new step brought a stronger enemy. He understood their fear. He understood why they were tired of watching him leave for places where death waited.","But he couldn’t stop. Not yet. Not while his parents stayed imprisoned. Not while the devils threatened the universe. Not while people like Varok looked at their home as a place to invade, corrupt, and control. Not while Max still lacked the power to fully decide his own fate.","He stepped closer and pulled both Alice and Lenavira into his arms. They didn’t resist. Alice leaned against his chest, her hands gripping his clothes tightly. Lenavira closed her eyes for a moment and rested her forehead against his shoulder. For a while, none of them spoke. The silence between them wasn’t empty anymore. It was filled with fear, affection, helplessness, and a warmth none of them wanted to let go of.","\"I promise you both,\" Max said softly. \"It won’t be long before I leave all this fighting behind and live peacefully with you. That’s what I’m working so hard for.\"","His arms tightened around them.","\"I don’t want endless war. I don’t want to spend my life chasing enemies from one battlefield to the next. I want to reunite with my family. I want to protect the people beside me. I want a life where I don’t have to worry about someone taking everything away from me again.\"","Alice’s eyes turned slightly red. \"Then come back,\" she whispered. \"Don’t just promise us a future and disappear before we get there.\"","Max lowered his gaze to her. \"I’ll come back.\"","Lenavira looked at him with trembling eyes. \"You always say that so calmly.\"","Max smiled faintly, but his voice stayed serious. \"Because I mean it.\"","The room went quiet again. This time, the silence felt softer. Alice slowly raised her hand and touched his face, as if trying to memorize him before he left. Lenavira moved closer too, her earlier worry slowly giving way to something warmer and more tender. Max looked at the two women in his arms, and for the first time that day, thoughts of the devils, the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, the Eternal Body, and the coming war faded from his mind.","For this moment, there was only them. Alice. Lenavira. The people he wanted to come back to. The people who made all his desperate effort feel like it meant something.","Max gently lowered his head and kissed Alice first. She didn’t pull away. Then Lenavira moved closer, and Max turned to her too, holding both of them with a care that slowly softened the fear in their hearts. What started as comfort soon turned into something deeper. Their words faded, their hesitation disappeared, and the emotions they’d been holding back for too long finally found a way to speak without needing to be explained.","That night, Max stayed with both Alice and Lenavira, and their closeness deepened into something more intimate.","It wasn’t driven by impulse alone. It was a quiet, intimate promise between three people who understood the road ahead might separate them for a long time. Beneath the gentle glow of the room’s formations, they gave each other warmth, trust, and a closeness that made the coming danger feel a little less cruel.","For that one night, Max didn’t train. He didn’t think about the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. He didn’t think about Varok, the Devil Race, the Seven Monarchs, or the path beyond the Seven Divine Veins. He stayed with Alice and Lenavira until the weight in their hearts slowly eased, until their fear didn’t feel so sharp anymore, and until the coming separation became something they could face together.","Outside the room, the Voidwalker Clan stayed quiet beneath the ancient sky of the Five Sacred Clan domain. Inside, Max held the two women close, letting the silence settle around them like a fragile peace.","For one night, before stepping into a battlefield where even geniuses from five universes could die, he let himself remember what he was fighting for.","When the night deepened, the room finally settled into a peaceful silence."]},{"number":2028,"title":"Chapter 2028: Michael!","paragraphs":["The next day, after spending some time with Freya, Max finally got ready to leave the Four Sacred Clans.","Freya didn’t try to stop him. She knew better than anyone that Max had already made his decision. Instead of trying to talk him out of it, she warned him about several things he needed to keep in mind inside the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.","She told him not to trust anyone too easily, not to underestimate geniuses from the other four universes, not to assume every trial followed fair rules, and not to reveal all his abilities unless he had no other choice.","She also reminded him that in a place like the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, opportunities often came with hidden prices, and sometimes the most beautiful inheritance grounds were the ones that swallowed the most corpses.","Max listened quietly. He didn’t treat her warnings as unnecessary worry. Freya had already been to the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, and if even she called that place insane, Max had no reason to take it lightly.","After saying goodbye, Max left the Four Sacred Clans and headed back to the Primordial Ancestral Domain. When he arrived, he found the other top geniuses already gathered.","Damian, Ervin, Revona, Rosaline, Rakan, Aurelian, and the others were there, but they weren’t alone. Besides the seven who’d decided to enter the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, there were also ten young geniuses from the Four Sacred Clans.","Max spotted the strongest descendants of Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest among them, and their expressions turned complicated the moment they noticed him.","They no longer looked at him with the same hostility as before. Some looked wary. Some looked curious. Some clearly still disliked him, but none of them dared provoke him openly.","Besides the Four Sacred Clan geniuses, unfamiliar faces stood scattered through the gathering area too. Some looked calm and detached. Some carried strange auras that didn’t belong to ordinary disciples. Some had eyes too old for their young faces, and some stood silently, as if the whole world around them had nothing to do with them.","The number of young geniuses present had crossed thirty. Max hadn’t expected this many people. But apart from the Four Sacred Clan geniuses, the unfamiliar youths all shared one thing in common.","They were all Primordials. Their bloodline aura felt different from the ten geniuses who’d recently awakened Primordial Bloodline. It ran deeper in some spots, more stable in others, clearly belonging to people who’d been raised with Primordial inheritance from birth. That realization made Max wonder if all of them would be entering the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage together.","\"Max, you finally made it.\"","Sarvion’s voice came from nearby. Max turned and saw Sarvion walking toward him with his usual calm expression.","\"Who are the other geniuses besides the ones from the Four Sacred Clans?\" Max asked as they started walking together.","Sarvion glanced at the unfamiliar youths and smiled faintly. \"They’re disciples of some great hidden experts.\"","\"Hidden experts?\" Max raised his brows slightly.","Sarvion nodded. \"Not every powerful being in the Divine Realm belongs openly to a palace, clan, court, kingdom, sanctum, hall, or Primordial faction. Some ancient experts prefer to stay outside the public order. They don’t interfere much, but when something as big as the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage opens up, they naturally send their disciples.\"","Max looked at the unfamiliar geniuses again. That explained their strange auras. They weren’t ordinary disciples from famous forces. They were heirs trained by old monsters living outside the usual structure of the Divine Realm.","Max didn’t dwell on it too much. Soon he met up with Damian, Rakan, Revona, and the others. Damian gave him a brief nod. Rakan looked more serious than usual, while Revona’s gaze lingered on Max for a moment, as if she could tell something about him had shifted again. Max had no plans to explain anything, so he just greeted them calmly.","Just as he was talking with them, a young voice sounded from behind him.","\"You must be Max.\"","Max turned around. A young man with dark blue hair and a sharp, handsome face stood in front of him. His eyes carried pride, and his aura wasn’t weak. A faint pressure surrounded him, marking him as no ordinary genius, but the arrogance on his face stood out even more than his strength.","\"And you are?\" Max asked.","The young man lifted his chin slightly. \"I’m Michael.\"","\"Good to meet you, Michael,\" Max said, holding out his hand politely.","But to his surprise, Michael slapped it away. The sound wasn’t loud, but it instantly drew the attention of Damian, Rakan, Revona, and several nearby geniuses.","Max looked at his hand for a brief moment. Then he looked back at Michael.","Michael’s expression stayed sharp. \"I’m not here to make friends with you.\"","Max stayed silent.","Michael continued, \"I came here to tell you that you don’t deserve the title of the strongest young genius of our universe. Someone stuck at the Law Manifestation Realm doesn’t deserve a title like that.\"","The atmosphere around them turned strange.","Damian frowned. Rakan’s expression darkened. Revona looked at Michael with mild interest, like she was trying to figure out if he was brave or just foolish.","Max sighed inwardly. ’Trouble really does find me wherever I go.’","He looked at Michael, then shrugged. \"You’re right, buddy.\"","After saying that, he turned away like the whole thing no longer interested him.","Michael froze. The reaction ran completely opposite of what he’d expected. He’d figured Max would get angry, argue back, release his aura, or challenge him. Instead, Max had just agreed and ignored him.","\"A-are you ignoring me?\" Michael shouted.","Max turned his head slightly and looked at him from the side. \"Did you not hear me? I said you’re right.\"","Michael stood there, not knowing what to say. His challenge had landed on absolutely nothing.","Before the awkward silence could stretch any further, an old man appeared before them.","\"My apologies, young man.\"","The voice sounded calm and aged, but the moment it came out, the whole area seemed to grow heavier.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly. The old man had a large rectangular face, a thick white beard covering most of his lower face, and a pair of bright eyes that looked surprisingly lively for his age. He wore golden armor that looked like a formal suit prepared for war, and every part of him gave off an aura that felt both dignified and dangerous.","The moment Max saw him, he understood this old man wasn’t simple. His aura matched the four Primarchs, the leaders of the strongest first-rate forces, and the ancestors of the Four Sacred Clans.","What surprised Max even more was that the old man was human. Not a Primordial. Not from the Four Sacred Clans. Just a normal human who’d somehow reached a level where his presence could stand beside the peak figures of the Divine Realm."]},{"number":2029,"title":"Chapter 2029: Sovereign Warlock!","paragraphs":["Just then, Arvantos appeared too.","\"Max, and all you young ones,\" Arvantos said, looking at Max and the other six geniuses before turning toward the bearded old man. \"Let me introduce him to you. This is Sovereign Warlock. I believe you’ve all heard of him.\"","Sovereign Warlock. The moment that title reached their ears, the expressions of Max and the others changed.","The title of Sovereign wasn’t something anyone could just claim. In the Divine Realm, only experts who’d reached the Divine God Realm were qualified to carry it. Those beings stood at a height most cultivators couldn’t even imagine, and each one represented the absolute peak of a path.","Max was already connected to one such figure. Dragonheart, the sword in his possession, had come from the Sword Sovereign. And now another Sovereign stood right in front of him.","Sovereign Warlock looked at their reactions and laughed lightly. \"Don’t look so shocked, kids. I’m just an old man.\"","Then his gaze shifted to Max. \"I apologize for my disciple’s behavior,\" he said. \"Michael’s a bit too arrogant for his own good.\"","Michael’s face changed immediately. \"Master!\" He looked both embarrassed and unwilling to accept it. After all, he’d just declared Max unworthy of the title of strongest genius, and now his own master was apologizing to Max in front of everyone.","Sovereign Warlock turned toward him and knocked him on the head with his fist.","\"What, kid?\" the old man said. \"Have you not gotten more and more arrogant lately? How many times have I told you not to be arrogant, to stay humble, and to never underestimate anyone?\"","Michael lowered his head and answered with a serious face. \"I understand, Master.\"","Sovereign Warlock sighed and shook his head. \"You always say you understand, but look at how many problems you keep causing me.\"","Michael didn’t dare say anything else.","Max watched the whole exchange quietly. The old man’s tone sounded casual, but Max could tell Sovereign Warlock had complete control over the situation. He’d shown up at exactly the right moment, apologized before the conflict could escalate, and scolded his disciple without stripping Michael of all his dignity. That kind of effortless control only came from someone with real strength and experience.","Arvantos smiled faintly. \"Michael will also be entering the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.\"","Max glanced at Michael. Michael looked back at him with a complicated expression. The hostility hadn’t disappeared, but after getting scolded by his master in front of everyone, he no longer dared act too recklessly.","Sovereign Warlock looked at Max with interest. \"I heard what happened during the meeting with the devils.\"","Max stayed calm. \"News travels fast.\"","\"At our level, important news travels before people even finish cleaning up the battlefield,\" Sovereign Warlock said with a light laugh. \"A 1st level Law Manifestation Realm cultivator killed a 5th level Law Manifestation Realm devil in one move, survived the Pearl of Abyss, and then still had the nerve to provoke Varok. How could I not be curious?\"","Several nearby geniuses looked toward Max again. Michael’s expression stiffened slightly. Clearly, he’d heard the title of strongest genius, but he hadn’t fully understood what Max had done to earn it.","Sovereign Warlock glanced at Michael from the corner of his eye. \"This is exactly why I told you not to judge people by realm alone.\"","Michael clenched his fists but didn’t argue back.","Max smiled lightly. \"It wasn’t as impressive as the rumors make it sound.\"","Sovereign Warlock laughed again. \"Modesty suits you better than arrogance, but fake modesty gets annoying too. You killed him because you were strong enough. That much’s clear.\"","Arvantos looked toward the gathered geniuses and spoke, pulling everyone’s attention back to the main matter. \"You’ve all gathered here because the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage will open soon. Some of you come from the Primordial Race. Some come from the Four Sacred Clans. Some are disciples of hidden experts. Some are among the ten who recently awakened Primordial Bloodline.\"","His voice turned solemn.","\"But once you enter the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, none of those identities will protect you. The geniuses of the Devil Universe, Spirit Universe, Angel Universe, and Dragon Universe won’t care about your background unless it gives them a reason to kill you faster.\"","The atmosphere turned serious again.","Arvantos continued, \"Once the gate opens, each of you walks your own path. Whether you find opportunity or death will come down to your strength, judgment, and luck. I won’t repeat this again. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage isn’t some protected trial arranged by your elders. It’s not a competition where someone steps in when you’re about to die. It’s a battlefield, a graveyard, a treasury, and a road left behind by existences far older than the current order of the five universes. Anyone who enters must accept that everything they own can be taken from them.\"","No one said a word. Even the arrogant young geniuses who’d come from hidden experts and ancient clans went quieter under those words. They were proud, but they weren’t foolish. If Arvantos was speaking this seriously, the danger of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage had to go far beyond ordinary imagination.","Arvantos raised his gaze toward the distant sky of the Primordial Ancestral Domain. \"The entrance to the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage doesn’t sit in any ordinary region of the Divine Realm. It lies at a forbidden point in space, far beyond the controlled star regions of most forces. Even Divine King Realm cultivators aren’t allowed to approach that place without permission, and ordinary Divine Lord Realm cultivators would die before they ever reached the outer boundary.\"","Several expressions changed. A forbidden point in space. Those words alone were enough to make the gathered geniuses understand that the journey itself wouldn’t be simple.","Arvantos continued, \"That place sits too close to the Wall of Eternity. The laws there run unstable, space stretches thin, time doesn’t always flow evenly, and the boundary pressure can crush weaker bodies into dust. There are no cities nearby. No forces, no clans, no trade routes, and no safe domains. It’s a place that exists outside the normal map of our universe.\"","His gaze returned to them. \"It’ll take us one day to get there.\""]},{"number":2030,"title":"Chapter 2030: Wall of Eternity!","paragraphs":["The moment he finished speaking, Arvantos waved his hand. The space above the gathering area trembled. A vast shadow slowly appeared in the sky. At first it looked like a golden cloud descending from the heavens, but as the light faded, everyone saw an enormous flying boat hovering above them.","The boat stretched hundreds of meters long, built from ancient bronze-gold metal and dark divine wood that seemed to have soaked up starlight for countless years. Its body was covered in Primordial runes, each one giving off a faint glow that made the surrounding space ripple gently.","The front of the boat was shaped like the head of an ancient beast, neither dragon nor phoenix, but something older and heavier. Its eyes were made of two rotating golden crystals, and its open mouth held a formation circle that looked capable of tearing through space.","Along the sides of the boat, layered defensive barriers flowed like transparent waves, giving off an aura that made even the more reckless geniuses instinctively hold themselves back.","Max looked at the flying boat with interest. He could sense spatial law, defensive law, speed formations, concealment patterns, and something deeper hidden beneath all of it. This wasn’t just a means of transportation. It was a war vessel, a moving fortress crafted by the Primordial Race.","Arvantos looked at everyone. \"Board.\"","No one hesitated. One by one, the young geniuses flew toward the boat and landed on its wide deck. Max stepped onto the vessel too, and the moment his feet touched the surface, he felt a steady power flowing beneath him. The entire boat felt alive, as if every plank, rune, and formation connected to one central will.","Damian stood near the edge of the deck with his arms folded. Revona looked toward the distant stars with a calm expression. Rakan stayed silent, while Michael stood some distance away with his master, Sovereign Warlock, who looked far more relaxed than anyone else present.","After everyone boarded, Arvantos appeared at the front of the flying boat. He didn’t give another long speech. He only raised his hand. The runes across the boat lit up all at once. A low hum spread through the air, and the entire vessel trembled lightly before rising higher into the sky.","The Primordial Ancestral Domain slowly shrank beneath them. Floating mountains, golden rivers, ancient palaces, and towering statues grew smaller and smaller until the entire sacred domain looked like a golden painting beneath the clouds.","Then the flying boat shot upward. The world below disappeared. The boat pierced through the sky and entered the starry void.","Countless stars appeared around them. The Divine Realm stretched vast beyond measure. Star regions spread in every direction, and distant continents, floating worlds, and law rivers glimmered in the endless darkness.","The flying boat moved with terrifying speed, yet the deck stayed steady. Its barriers blocked the pressure of space, the cold of the void, and the turbulent flow of laws outside.","Max stood near the railing and looked into the distance. This wasn’t his first time seeing the vastness of the universe, but the feeling hit different now. In a few days, he’d be entering a place connected not just to this universe, but to all five.","A full day passed as the flying boat traveled through the starry void. During that time, almost no one spoke much. Some geniuses sat cross-legged and settled their minds. Some stood silently staring into space. Some checked their weapons, pills, treasures, and protective talismans. Though they were all proud, none of them dared treat the upcoming pilgrimage lightly.","Max used the time to calm his mind too. This time, he didn’t enter the Dimension of Time. Instead, he quietly stood on the deck and watched the strange changes in space as the boat moved farther and farther from the familiar regions of the Divine Realm.","The laws around them gradually grew thinner, but at the same time heavier. Space no longer felt like a stable ocean. It felt like cracked glass stretched across endless darkness.","After one day, the flying boat finally slowed down. The stars around them had changed. This region of space looked unlike anywhere Max had seen before. No nearby worlds. No continents. No floating cities. No law rivers flowing through the void.","The entire area sat empty, but the emptiness itself felt wrong. Far ahead, the darkness seemed to curve inward, as if the universe had hit a point where it no longer wanted to continue.","The flying boat stopped in front of that strange region. Everyone on the deck stood up. Max looked forward, and his eyes narrowed. At first, he saw nothing. Then, as his perception spread outward, he felt it.","A wall. Not a wall made of stone, metal, or formation power, but a boundary so vast and profound his mind could barely hold onto it. It stretched beyond sight in every direction. It had no clear shape, yet it was undeniably there. Space ended at that point, and something older than space stood beyond it.","The Wall of Eternity.","Max had heard about it plenty of times by now, but hearing about it and standing in front of it were two entirely different things.","The boundary gave him the feeling that it wasn’t just separating lands or star regions. It was separating realities. It was the membrane keeping universes from crashing into each other, the line dividing different cosmic orders, different laws, different origins, and different destinies.","Even from the safety of the flying boat, Max felt a heavy pressure pressing against his body. His five Divine Veins stirred faintly. His Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline grew more active too.","Arvantos stood at the front of the vessel, looking toward the invisible boundary ahead.","\"This is the place,\" he said.","Everyone turned toward him.","Arvantos continued, \"This point in space is one of the forbidden edges of our universe. The Wall of Eternity sits right here.\"","His voice stayed calm, but everyone could hear the seriousness underneath it.","\"But this side of the Wall is different from the side the devils pierced. It’s not connected to the Devil Universe, the Spirit Universe, the Angel Universe, or the Dragon Universe.\"","Max’s gaze sharpened.","Arvantos raised his hand and pointed toward the distorted darkness ahead. \"This side connects to the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.\"","The deck fell completely silent. The young geniuses stared forward with solemn expressions.","Arvantos continued, \"The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage doesn’t belong to any single universe. It exists in a strange region where the boundaries of the five universes overlap without truly merging. To reach it, each universe has its own separate entrance point. This is ours.\"","The space ahead began to ripple faintly, as if responding to his words.","\"Remember this,\" Arvantos said. \"Once the entrance opens, you’ll no longer be standing under the protection of the Primordial Race, the Four Sacred Clans, your masters, your families, or me. You’ll be entering a place where ancient laws decide the rules, and where every race sends the ones they believe can survive.\"","He turned and looked at the gathered geniuses. \"This is your last moment to get ready.\"","No one stepped back. No one spoke of retreat.","The flying boat floated silently before the Wall of Eternity, and the strange darkness ahead slowly began to pulse, as if something ancient on the other side had just woken up."]},{"number":2031,"title":"Chapter 2031: Into the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage!","paragraphs":["Max and the other geniuses waited patiently for the entrance to the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage to open.","The flying boat stayed suspended before the forbidden edge of space, unmoving and silent. Around them, the starry void stretched in every direction, but this region didn’t feel like ordinary space. It was too still. Too cold. Too heavy.","There were no distant worlds, no drifting continents, no shining law rivers, and no signs of life anywhere nearby. Only the vast darkness ahead kept pulsing faintly, as if something hidden behind the Wall of Eternity was breathing.","No one spoke much. Even Michael, who’d been arrogant not long ago, stood quietly beside Sovereign Warlock with a serious expression. The young geniuses from the Primordial Race, the Four Sacred Clans, and the hidden experts all watched the distorted space ahead with different looks in their eyes.","Some looked excited. Some looked nervous. Some tried to stay calm, but their tightened fists and sharpened breathing gave away their real feelings.","Max stood near the front of the deck, his gaze fixed on the invisible boundary ahead. The pressure coming from the Wall of Eternity was hard to describe. It didn’t just press against the body. It pressed against perception, bloodline, soul, and law comprehension all at once. Max could feel his Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline stirring faintly.","A low sound suddenly spread through the void. It wasn’t thunder. It wasn’t the roar of a beast. It sounded more like an ancient door turning after countless years of silence.","Everyone on the flying boat went alert at once.","The darkness ahead began to twist. At first the change was faint. A thin silver-gold line appeared in the empty space before them, stretching vertically across the void.","Then the line widened slowly, and layers of ancient symbols surfaced around it. Some symbols glowed gold. Some glowed silver. Some looked black. Some carried colors Max had never seen before, colors that seemed to exist somewhere between law and light.","The Wall of Eternity trembled faintly. A crack opened in the boundary. Beyond that crack, Max saw a road.","It wasn’t a normal road. It looked like countless broken stars had fused together into a vast path stretching into endless mist. Ancient ruins floated in the distance. Rivers of light flowed backward through the sky.","Fragments of shattered palaces drifted like dead moons. Enormous bones stretched across the horizon, and somewhere far deeper, Max sensed a power so ancient that even his soul went quiet in front of it.","The entrance to the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage had opened.","A heavy aura rushed out from the crack and swept over the flying boat. Several young geniuses immediately changed expressions. Some took half a step back. Some released their bloodline aura on instinct. Some had to circulate their cultivation just to steady themselves.","This was only the aura leaking out from the entrance, yet it already carried the feel of an ancient battlefield soaked in countless eras of death, glory, and forgotten ambition.","Arvantos stood at the front of the flying boat, his robes unmoving despite the violent flow of power from the entrance. He turned around and looked at everyone.","\"This is the entrance to the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.\"","His voice stayed calm, but every word reached all the geniuses clearly.","\"Once you pass through it, you’ll no longer be under my protection. The Primordial Race won’t be able to watch over you. The Four Sacred Clans won’t be able to interfere. Your masters, elders, teachers, and families won’t be able to save you when danger comes.\"","The geniuses’ expressions turned more solemn.","Arvantos continued, \"Inside that place, your identity only matters if you have the strength to defend it. Don’t think your background will scare the geniuses of other universes. The Devil Race will kill you the moment they see weakness.\"","His gaze swept slowly across all of them. No one dared take his warning lightly.","Arvantos’s expression turned even more serious. \"The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage splits into countless regions, and not all of you will land in the same place after entering. Some of you might get separated immediately. Some of you might meet again after days, months, or even years, depending on how the internal space behaves. Time, distance, and direction aren’t always reliable there. If you find companions you can trust, value them. If you find enemies you can’t kill, survive first and settle the debt later.\"","Max’s eyes moved slightly. That meant they might not be able to rely on each other once they got in.","Arvantos continued, \"You’re all geniuses of our universe. Some of you carry the blood of Primordials. Some carry the inheritance of the Four Sacred Clans. Some were trained by hidden experts. Some have walked paths even I can’t fully see. But none of that matters if you die at the first step.\"","His voice dropped. \"So live.\"","Those two words came out simple, but they carried more weight than any grand speech.","\"Take what you can take. Fight when you have to fight. Retreat when you have to retreat. Learn, endure, and come back stronger than you are today. The war with the devils has already cast its shadow over our universe, and the future won’t wait for slow growth.\"","Arvantos looked at them one last time. \"When you come back from the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, I hope to see fewer children standing in front of me and more blades sharp enough to cut into the coming storm.\"","The flying boat fell into complete silence.","Then Sovereign Warlock laughed lightly, breaking the heaviness for a moment. \"You heard him, brats. Go in alive, come back alive, and try not to embarrass your masters too badly.\"","Some of the tension eased, just slightly.","Arvantos raised his hand. A bridge of golden light stretched out from the flying boat toward the opened entrance. It crossed the empty void and connected directly to the star-forged road beyond the crack in the Wall of Eternity.","The first group of Primordial geniuses stepped forward. Without hesitation, they walked across the bridge and entered the entrance. Their figures got swallowed by the silver-gold light and disappeared into the mist beyond.","After them, the disciples of the hidden experts started moving. Some looked calm. Some looked excited. Some carried silent killing intent in their eyes.","The geniuses of the Four Sacred Clans went next. Several of them glanced at Max before crossing the bridge, but none of them said anything."]},{"number":2032,"title":"Chapter 2032: A very different Place!","paragraphs":["Then it was Max and the others’ turn.","Damian walked forward first, his expression cold and steady. Revona followed with a faint smile, though her eyes carried the depth of someone stepping toward an old memory. Ervin took a deep breath and entered after her.","Rakan, Rosaline, Aurelian, and the others moved one by one, each carrying their own thoughts and ambitions.","Michael walked past Max and paused for a brief moment. He looked like he wanted to say something, but in the end he just snorted and stepped onto the bridge.","Max ignored him. His gaze stayed fixed on the entrance. Beyond that light waited the strongest young geniuses of five universes. Beyond that light waited danger, trials, ruins, enemies, inheritances, and maybe the path to the Eternal Body. It was a place where many geniuses would rise and many more would end up buried.","Max stepped forward. He didn’t look back. With calm eyes, he walked into the entrance of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.","The silver-gold light swallowed his figure. A moment later, the starry void outside the Wall of Eternity settled back into quiet.","On the other side of the entrance, Max found himself standing on pale yellow land. The moment his feet touched the ground, the silver-gold light behind him disappeared, and the strange pressure of the Wall of Eternity vanished as if it had never existed. Max didn’t move right away. He stood where he was and quietly took in his surroundings.","The land beneath him stretched wide and dry, glowing faintly with a dull yellow sheen. It didn’t look like ordinary soil. Every grain of dust seemed to carry a trace of ancient energy, and when the wind swept across the ground, the pale sand moved like thin waves across the surface of a silent sea.","No mountains stood nearby, no forests, no rivers, no buildings. As far as Max could see, the land stretched endlessly in every direction.","The sky above him looked unusually blue. It wasn’t the gentle blue of an ordinary world. It ran too deep, too clean, too vast, as if someone had washed away every trace of impurity from the heavens.","Even stranger, both a sun and a moon hung in that sky at the same time. The sun burned with a soft golden light, while the moon gave off a faint silver glow despite the brightness around it. Their light mixed together without either one drowning out the other, filling the world with a strange balance of warmth and cold.","Max took a slow breath. The natural energy here entered his body almost on its own. His expression shifted slightly.","\"What a refreshing feeling,\" he muttered.","It felt like he’d arrived in an entirely different kind of world. The energy here didn’t match the Divine Realm or the Primordial Ancestral Domain. It felt more ancient, more active, and more natural.","It didn’t feel neatly arranged by formations or controlled by powerful forces. Instead, it felt wild and pure, like energy that had flowed freely since the beginning of time.","His Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline stirred faintly. The five Divine Veins inside his body responded too.","Max stood there for a while, letting his senses spread outward. After looking around for some time, he confirmed one thing.","He was in the middle of nowhere. No obvious road, no city, no camp, and no sign of the other geniuses who’d entered with him. It seemed Arvantos had been right. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage didn’t send everyone to the same place. Each person had to begin their journey alone, at least for now.","\"I need to find civilization first,\" Max muttered to himself.","Both Freya and Arvantos had warned him about this before he entered. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage was vast, strange, and filled with places that could kill even geniuses if they wandered blindly.","Finding a civilization, a settlement, or at least a gathering point was the safest first move. There, he could learn about the region, understand the local rules, and gather information about trials, marks, danger zones, and opportunities.","Max looked around again. No obvious landmarks stood out.","After a short moment, he activated his Dimensional Sovereign Body. His perception shifted. The world around him changed. Space no longer felt like just empty distance. It became layered, folded, and filled with faint traces left behind by movement.","The wind, the ground, and even the path of energy through the air grew clearer in his senses. Soon he noticed something.","Footprints. They were faint and almost completely covered by pale dust, but they were there. Someone or something had passed through this area not too long ago. The traces moved in one direction, and although Max couldn’t immediately tell whether they belonged to humans, beasts, or another race, they were still the only clue he had.","He decided to follow them. Max moved forward calmly, his senses spread around him.","But he’d only taken a few steps when the ground ahead trembled. A low growl echoed across the pale yellow land.","Max stopped.","From the dust in front of him, a huge beast slowly walked out and blocked his path. It was a wolf-like creature, though calling it a wolf didn’t really do it justice. Its body was massive, nearly five times bigger than Max, and its fur was dark gray with streaks of crimson running through it like dried blood.","It had six powerful legs, each ending in claws sharp enough to tear through stone. Most terrifying of all, it had six heads, and each head stared at Max with a different expression of hunger, cruelty, madness, and animal instinct.","Its aura surged outward.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"3rd level Divine Lord Realm.\"","The beast wasn’t some hidden guardian, and it didn’t seem to be a rare creature protecting an inheritance. It was just a random beast he’d run into shortly after entering this place, yet it already carried the strength of the 3rd level Divine Lord Realm.","Max frowned. \"Even a random beast here sits at the 3rd level of the Divine Lord Realm. My cultivation really is too low for the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.\"","He wasn’t afraid. But he wasn’t careless either. In the Divine Realm, his strength already counted as terrifying for someone at the 1st level of the Law Manifestation Realm.","He could fight across realms, kill enemies above his level, and shock even top experts with his foundation. But the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage clearly worked differently. This was a place where the basic standard of danger sat much higher."]},{"number":2033,"title":"Chapter 2033: A Bronze Mark!","paragraphs":["The six-headed wolf didn’t give him more time to think. All six of its heads roared at once. The sound shook the air, and a violent wave of killing intent rushed toward Max. In the next instant, the beast lunged forward with terrifying speed.","Its six legs pushed against the ground at the same time, cracking the pale yellow land beneath it as its huge body turned into a gray-crimson blur.","Max’s eyes stayed calm. He activated his Voidwalker Bloodline. In an instant, ten blue void rings appeared around his two arms. The rings rotated once around his wrists and forearms before flying out together.","They crossed the space between Max and the beast in a flash, circling the six-headed wolf before it could reach him. The beast was still mid-leap when the rings locked into place around it.","Space folded inward. A spherical seal formed instantly.","The six-headed wolf froze in the air less than a few feet from Max’s face. Its claws were still stretched forward, its jaws were still open, and its killing intent was still surging, but its body could no longer move.","The ten void rings rotated around the spherical seal, releasing layers of blue light that pressed down on its body, aura, bloodline, and Divine Lord Realm power.","Max studied the seal carefully. His brows furrowed slightly.","\"I can feel the void rings straining to hold the seal.\"","The ten void rings were still holding, but the pressure showed. The six-headed wolf’s cultivation ran far above Max’s own realm, and although the Ten Void Sealing Art was powerful, the gap in cultivation couldn’t be completely ignored.","The beast’s Divine Lord Realm energy kept pushing against the seal from inside, causing faint ripples to appear across the blue sphere.","\"Is it because I’m sealing something far above my cultivation realm?\" Max muttered.","That seemed like the most likely reason. Against someone closer to his own level, the void rings could suppress almost effortlessly. But against a Divine Lord Realm beast, even a random one, the burden grew much heavier.","This was valuable information. It meant that inside the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, he couldn’t rely on the Ten Void Sealing Art as carelessly as before against enemies far above his realm.","Still, the seal held enough.","Max raised one hand. Black flames rose from his palm. The flames looked dark, heavy, and devouring. Unlike the Primordial Flames, which refined and purified, these black flames existed to consume, corrode, and destroy.","Max flicked his fingers, and a thin stream of black fire entered the spherical seal formed by the ten void rings.","The moment the flames touched the trapped beast, they spread across its body. The six-headed wolf roared violently. Its Divine Lord Realm energy erupted, and the blue sealing sphere trembled more intensely.","But the void rings held firm. The black flames burrowed into the beast’s flesh, devoured its blood, consumed its energy, and burned through its life force. Within a few breaths, the massive creature that had lunged at Max with such ferocity got reduced to nothing but ashes inside the sealed space.","The ten void rings slowly returned to Max’s arms. The ashes scattered into the wind.","Max stood in place and sensed the change inside his body. A small portion of energy had gotten absorbed through the devouring nature of his flames, but the increase wasn’t much. His body felt slightly strengthened, and his energy grew a bit denser, but it fell far short of causing any major change.","\"Only a small increase in strength,\" Max said with a wry smile. He shook his head. \"Even devouring a 3rd level Divine Lord Realm beast isn’t enough to make me break through.\"","He felt a little disappointed, but not surprised. His foundation ran too strong. His body, bloodline, soul, Pseudo Cosmic Paths, Divine Veins, and several inheritances had pushed his base far beyond ordinary cultivators.","Because of that, ordinary energy gains no longer moved him forward easily. If he wanted to break through, he’d need far greater resources, deeper opportunities, or battles that forced his foundation to transform.","Just then, Max felt an itch on his right wrist. He lowered his gaze.","A faint bronze glow appeared on his skin. The glow slowly gathered into a mark. It formed a circular shape, and inside the circle sat the image of a sword pointing downward.","The mark looked simple at first, but when Max focused on it, he could feel a strange law hidden inside it. It wasn’t just a symbol. It was a record, a recognition, and maybe even a form of currency within the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.","Max stared at the bronze mark for a moment. Then he smiled faintly.","\"Is this the mark Big Sis told me about?\"","Freya hadn’t explained the marks in much detail, but she’d told him one thing very clearly. Marks meant everything in the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. Arvantos had also hinted at their importance before sending them in.","Marks could decide access, status, opportunities, rankings, exchanges, and even survival in certain places. Some trials required them. Some cities recognized them. Some inheritances demanded them. Some enemies hunted others precisely because of them.","Max lifted his wrist and looked at the bronze circle with the sword inside it.","\"I need to know more about these marks,\" Max muttered as he kept staring at the bronze symbol on his wrist.","The mark didn’t feel ordinary. It wasn’t just something left behind after killing a beast. It had entered his skin without resistance, attached itself to his aura, and settled into his body as if the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage itself had acknowledged his kill.","The more Max sensed it, the more he realized the mark connected to some deeper rule of this place. It wasn’t an external reward handed out by a person, sect, or formation. It was part of the structure of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage itself.","That made him even more curious.","Both Freya and Arvantos had mentioned marks before he entered, but neither of them had explained the details clearly. Freya had only told him marks were extremely important, while Arvantos had merely hinted that opportunities, status, and survival could depend on them.","Neither of them had gone further, and Max didn’t believe that was because they’d forgotten or wanted him kept in the dark.","There had to be a reason."]},{"number":2034,"title":"Chapter 2034: Getting Robbed?","paragraphs":["\"Restrictions,\" Max murmured.","That was the only explanation that made sense. If even someone as powerful as Arvantos, one of the four Primarchs of the Primordial Race, couldn’t freely explain the internal rules of this place, then the restrictions around the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage ran far more terrifying than Max had first assumed.","These rules weren’t something the current five universes had created. They were ancient, hidden, and strong enough to bind even the peak figures standing at the top of the Divine Realm.","This thought made Max’s eyes deepen. \"This place really is special.\"","He lowered his wrist and kept following the faint traces he’d found earlier. The pale yellow land stretched endlessly around him. Dust moved with the wind, the blue sky stayed impossibly clear, and the sun and moon kept hanging together above the world like two silent watchers.","The deeper Max walked, the more he sensed that this land only looked empty on the surface. Beneath the silence, traces of danger sat everywhere.","The ground carried old blood aura in some places. The wind occasionally brought faint killing intent from far away. Somewhere beneath the pale soil, broken laws seemed to sleep in fragments.","Max kept walking for some time before his footsteps suddenly stopped. His gaze shifted slightly toward a cluster of large boulders ahead.","The boulders looked ordinary at first. They sat half-buried in the pale soil, weathered by wind, covered with dry cracks.","But Max’s perception ran far sharper than most cultivators at his realm. With the Dimensional Sovereign Body active, space itself revealed small irregularities to him. Behind one of those boulders, the flow of space was slightly distorted.","There were people hiding there.","Max’s expression stayed calm. \"You three can come out now,\" he said.","His voice wasn’t loud, but it carried clearly across the empty land.","Nothing happened. The wind kept blowing. The boulders stayed still.","Max waited for two breaths, then sneered faintly. Black flames rose from his palm. He flicked his fingers, and a ball of devouring fire shot toward the largest boulder.","Before the black flames could touch it, three figures stepped out from behind the rocks. They stood tall and muscular, with dark gray skin, crimson lines crawling across their bodies, and sharp horns growing from their foreheads.","Their eyes glowed deep red, and their smiles carried a cruel hunger Max had already seen too many times from devils. Each of them wore dark armor made from some unknown beast hide and black metal, and all three carried weapons stained with old blood.","Devils.","Max looked at them silently.","The three devils didn’t seem surprised they’d been discovered. If anything, they looked amused.","\"Hehe, this Primordial sensed us somehow,\" one of the devils said, glancing at the other two with a sneer.","Another devil laughed and licked his lips. \"Good. Saves us the trouble of waiting. We finally caught ourselves a Primordial newbie.\"","The third devil looked Max up and down, his gaze lingering on Max’s wrist. When he saw the bronze mark there, his smile widened. \"He’s already got a mark too. Not bad. Looks like this little Primordial killed something right after spawning.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly. Spawning. So this area really was a place where newcomers appeared after entering the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.","The first devil cracked his neck and stepped forward. \"You’re unlucky, kid. This is one of the better newbie landing zones, and we’ve been guarding this area for a while now. Every time the entrance opens, a few fresh geniuses show up around here. Some carry treasures. Some carry marks. Some carry storage rings packed with treasures from their clans.\"","The second devil laughed. \"Primordials are usually rich. Their bloodlines are useful too, even if they’re a pain to extract. Maybe this one’s worth more than the last angel brat we killed.\"","The third devil stared at Max with greed in his eyes. \"Hand over your storage ring, your weapons, your mark, and whatever treasures you’re carrying. Cooperate, and maybe we’ll let you die quickly.\"","The three of them laughed together.","Max didn’t laugh. He sensed their auras clearly. All three devils sat at the 2nd level of the Divine Lord Realm. Out in the Divine Realm, that cultivation would’ve been more than enough to crush most people at his level.","Even inside the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, they clearly weren’t weak among those who preyed on newly arrived geniuses. Their choice to hide near a landing zone was deliberate too. They weren’t here to explore trials or fight powerful enemies. They were here to ambush people who entered alone before they understood the rules of this place.","Max’s gaze turned colder. \"You guard this area to rob and kill newcomers?\"","The first devil grinned. \"You say that like it’s a bad thing.\"","The second devil added, \"In the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, the weak exist to feed the strong.\"","The third devil raised his weapon. \"And today, you’re the weak one.\"","Max sighed softly. \"I see.\"","The three devils were still smiling when Max moved. There was no warning. No exchange of threats. Max had no interest in listening to them talk any longer.","Dragonheart appeared in his hand, and in the same instant, the aura around him changed completely. The pale yellow land seemed to lose its warmth. The wind went silent. Even the killing intent of the three devils froze for a brief moment, as if something had cut the emotions right out of the air itself.","The Emotion Severing Path erupted. But this time, Max didn’t use just a trace of it. He used its full power. His eyes turned calm to the point of coldness.","The first devil’s smile vanished. \"What is this?\"","He tried to retreat, but it was already too late.","Max stepped forward and swung Dragonheart once. The sword light wasn’t dazzling. It didn’t explode with thunder, flames, or overwhelming radiance. It came out quiet, pale, and terrifyingly clean.","Wherever it passed, killing intent disappeared. Fear disappeared. Anger disappeared. Even the devil’s instinctive urge to resist seemed to vanish for a single instant.","That single instant decided life and death. The sword light crossed the first devil’s neck. His head flew into the air."]},{"number":2035,"title":"Chapter 2035: Five Types of Marks!","paragraphs":["Before the body even hit the ground, Max had already appeared beside the second devil. The second devil roared and tried to activate his devil bloodline. Crimson tattoos lit up across his skin, and dark energy surged from his body like burning smoke.","But the moment the Emotion Severing Path came down on him, his roar weakened. His rage faded. His battle intent got sliced apart before it could fully form.","Max’s sword pierced through his chest. The power of the Emotion Severing Path flowed through the blade and spread through the devil’s body. The second devil froze. His eyes widened. Then the light in them dimmed as his soul, emotions, and life force all got severed together.","Two devils died almost instantly.","The third devil stood frozen in place. His weapon was still half-raised, but his body no longer dared move. Everything had happened too fast. One moment, the three of them were laughing about robbing a newly arrived Primordial.","The next moment, two of them were dead, and the young man they’d called weak stood right in front of him with a sword in hand.","The third devil’s face turned pale. Only now did he truly understand. This Primordial wasn’t prey. He was a monster.","Max appeared in front of him and placed Dragonheart against his throat. The cold edge of the sword touched the devil’s skin, and the lingering power of the Emotion Severing Path made his entire body tremble.","It wasn’t ordinary fear. It felt like something deep inside him was slowly getting stripped away, as if his courage, arrogance, and will to resist were being peeled from his soul layer by layer.","Max looked at him calmly. \"Where’s the nearest city?\"","The devil’s throat moved slightly. He wanted to speak, but his voice didn’t come out right away.","Max pressed the blade a little closer. A thin line of blood appeared on the devil’s neck.","\"Answer,\" Max said. \"And think carefully before you do.\"","The third devil swallowed hard.","Max’s eyes stayed cold. \"If you lie to me, you won’t die like the other two.\"","The devil’s pupils contracted.","Max continued in the same calm voice, \"They died fast. You won’t.\"","The devil’s body trembled harder. The two corpses beside him were still falling apart under the lingering power of Max’s sword. One had lost his head before he could even understand what happened.","The other had been pierced through the chest, his life erased so cleanly that even his devil energy couldn’t erupt properly. Compared to them, the third devil suddenly felt like death might have been mercy.","\"I’ll talk,\" he said quickly, his voice hoarse. \"I’ll talk. Don’t kill me.\"","Max didn’t move the sword away. \"Nearest city.\"","The devil took a shaky breath and pointed toward the direction the faint footprints had been leading. \"Keep going that way. There’s a city called Bloodstone City. It’s the nearest gathering place in this region. If you move at full speed, you can reach it in half a day. If you walk normally, it’ll take longer.\"","Max stared at him.","The devil quickly added, \"I’m not lying. I swear I’m not lying. Everyone who spawns in this outer region tries to reach Bloodstone City first. It’s not safe, but it’s still better than wandering outside. There are traders there, information brokers, mark exchange halls, and people who know where the nearby trials are.\"","Max’s eyes moved slightly. Bloodstone City. Mark exchange halls. Information brokers. That was exactly the kind of place he needed.","He looked at the devil again. \"What are marks used for?\"","The devil hesitated for a brief moment. Max’s sword pressed slightly deeper. The hesitation vanished immediately.","\"Everything,\" the devil said hurriedly. \"Marks get used for everything. You need them to enter trials, buy information, exchange resources, rent cultivation rooms, enter some cities, and open certain inheritance grounds. They also decide your ranking and status in some places. Without marks, you’re nothing in the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.\"","Max’s gaze deepened. Freya had been right. Marks truly were everything here.","The devil continued, afraid that silence would anger Max. \"There are five types of marks in the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. The first is the Bronze Mark. Every newcomer gets one when they enter, which is why it’s also called the beginner’s mark. The second is the Gold Mark. Above that sits the Sacred Mark. The fourth is the Divine Mark, and the last one is the Godslayer Mark.\"","Max glanced at the bronze sword mark on his wrist. \"Only five?\" he asked.","The devil nodded quickly. \"Only five recognized grades. The gap between them is enormous. A Bronze Mark sits at the lowest, while a Godslayer Mark stands at the absolute peak. Most participants spend countless years struggling to advance even one grade. Plenty die before they can get a Gold Mark, and only a tiny number ever reach the Divine or Godslayer level.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"How does someone get the higher marks?\"","The devil’s expression turned solemn. \"You can’t get them directly. You have to build up enough marks of the lower grade first.\"","\"Explain.\"","\"To become eligible for a Gold Mark, you need to collect one thousand Bronze Marks,\" the devil said. \"Once you’ve gathered one thousand Bronze Marks, the rules of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage let you condense them into a single Gold Mark.\"","Max’s gaze sharpened. \"One thousand Bronze Marks for one Gold Mark?\"","\"Yes,\" the devil replied. \"And the same rule applies at every level. After collecting one thousand Gold Marks, you become eligible to condense them into a Sacred Mark. Then you need to collect one thousand Sacred Marks to become eligible for a Divine Mark. Finally, after collecting one thousand Divine Marks, you can condense them into the highest grade, the Godslayer Mark.\"","Max stayed silent. The numbers were staggering. One thousand Bronze Marks for one Gold Mark. One thousand Gold Marks for one Sacred Mark. One thousand Sacred Marks for one Divine Mark. And one thousand Divine Marks for a single Godslayer Mark. The progression wasn’t just difficult. It was practically monstrous."]},{"number":2036,"title":"Chapter 2036: Uses of Marks!","paragraphs":["The devil kept explaining, terrified Max might think he was hiding something. \"The marks don’t just disappear for no reason. When you meet the requirement, the Pilgrimage recognizes your accumulation and gives you the choice to advance. But once you condense the lower marks into a higher one, the lower marks get consumed. You can’t use the same marks twice.\"","\"What happens if someone collects enough but refuses to advance?\" Max asked.","\"They can keep accumulating,\" the devil answered. \"Some people wait because lower-grade marks can get used directly for certain exchanges and transactions. But the higher your mark grade, the greater your authority, and the more valuable your status becomes. A Gold Mark holder gets treated very differently from someone who only carries Bronze Marks.\"","Max looked down at his wrist again. The bronze symbol seemed to glow faintly beneath his skin.","\"So every newcomer starts with one Bronze Mark,\" he said.","\"Yes.\"","\"And killing beasts gives more Bronze Marks?\"","\"Usually,\" the devil replied. \"The number depends on the strength of the beast and the rules of the region. Some beasts give one Bronze Mark. Stronger ones might give several. Certain trials can reward dozens or even hundreds. Killing other participants can also give marks, but the amount depends on the victim’s accumulated marks and the rules governing the area.\"","Max’s eyes turned cold. \"So killing someone lets you take their marks?\"","The devil nodded nervously. \"Sometimes. Not every region allows it, but plenty do. That’s why people are so careful about revealing their mark count. A powerful participant carrying a large number of marks turns into a walking treasure vault.\"","Max understood immediately. The three devils hadn’t just wanted his storage ring and treasures. They’d also noticed he already carried a Bronze Mark. If he’d accumulated more, they would’ve tried to seize those too.","The devil continued, \"There are also missions, inheritances, ancient ruins, and special trials that reward marks. Some opportunities can grant more marks than months of killing beasts. But the more valuable the reward, the more dangerous the trial.\"","\"What about the Godslayer Mark?\" Max asked. \"Has anyone ever obtained one?\"","The devil’s face changed. Fear and reverence appeared in his eyes.","\"I don’t know,\" he admitted. \"There are rumors that a few ancient existences once obtained Godslayer Marks, but nobody knows if those stories are even true. In the current era, I’ve never heard of anyone openly holding one. Even Divine Mark holders are rare enough to become legends in most regions.\"","Max’s expression stayed calm, but his mind was already working. The mark system was clearly more than a simple reward mechanism. It was a hierarchy built into the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, one that measured achievement, authority, and maybe even destiny.","If the highest mark truly required one thousand Divine Marks, obtaining a Godslayer Mark would demand an unimaginable accumulation of lower-grade marks.","The devil looked at Max carefully. \"Do you understand now?\"","Max raised his eyes. \"Not completely.\"","The devil’s face went pale.","Max continued, \"You said marks can be used for exchanges and entry fees. If I spend a Bronze Mark, does that reduce the number I need for advancement?\"","\"Yes,\" the devil answered quickly. \"Any mark you spend gets removed from your total. If you want to condense one thousand Bronze Marks into a Gold Mark, you need to still hold one thousand Bronze Marks at that moment. Marks used for transactions can’t get counted again.\"","Max nodded slowly. That meant he’d need to choose carefully between immediate benefits and long-term advancement.","The devil added, \"But some cities and factions offer conversion services. They might let you exchange treasures for marks or marks for resources. The exchange rates usually run terrible, though. The stronger the mark, the more valuable it gets. A Gold Mark is worth far more than one thousand Bronze Marks in ordinary transactions, even though it takes one thousand Bronze Marks to condense one.\"","Max’s eyes flashed. \"So the system pushes people to advance, but also tempts them to spend their marks before they can.\"","\"That’s exactly how it works,\" the devil said bitterly. \"The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage hands out opportunities, but it also forces people to make choices. Those who spend everything just to survive might stay at the bottom forever. Those who save everything might die before they ever get to use it.\"","Max fell silent. The rules ran cruel, but they weren’t chaotic. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage had built a clear path. Bronze. Gold. Sacred. Divine. Godslayer. Each step required an accumulation of one thousand marks from the level before it. The higher one climbed, the harder the journey got, but the rewards and authority grew accordingly too.","Freya had said marks were extremely important. Now Max understood why. They weren’t just currency. They were proof of achievement, a key to opportunities, a symbol of status, and maybe the only way to reach the deepest secrets of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.","Max looked back at the devil. \"Is there anything else I should know about marks?\"","The devil hesitated. Max’s sword pressed slightly deeper. The hesitation disappeared immediately.","\"There’s one more thing,\" the devil said hurriedly. \"Marks are bound to the soul. They can’t normally get stolen through ordinary means. If someone kills a participant in a region where mark transfer is allowed, the rules of the Pilgrimage decide how many marks can transfer. But if the victim has hidden or sealed their marks, the killer might not get everything.\"","Max nodded. \"And the mark on my wrist?\"","\"That’s your personal mark,\" the devil replied. \"It records your current accumulation and grade. As you get more Bronze Marks, the symbol will gradually change. Once you reach one thousand Bronze Marks, it’ll transform into a Gold Mark if you choose to advance.\"","Max studied the bronze symbol again. A faint light moved across its surface. He could sense it connected to something vast and ancient, something existing beyond his understanding. It wasn’t simply counting his achievements. It was watching them.","Maybe the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage was watching every participant. Maybe it was judging them. Or maybe it was just waiting to see who could climb high enough to reach the end.","Max pulled his gaze away from the mark and looked at the devil. \"You’ve told me everything you know?\""]},{"number":2037,"title":"Chapter 2037: Outer, Inner and Core!","paragraphs":["The devil nodded rapidly. \"Yes. I swear. I’ve told you everything.\"","Max stared at him for a moment. Then he pulled Dragonheart back.","The devil’s expression loosened with relief.","But before that relief could fully settle in, Max’s left hand rose. A blue void ring flashed across the air and entered the devil’s chest.","The devil froze. His eyes widened in terror. \"You said...\"","\"I said you’d end up worse than them if you lied,\" Max replied calmly. \"I never said I’d let you go.\"","The void ring tightened. The devil’s body collapsed to the ground, his cultivation sealed and his devil energy locked inside him. Max didn’t kill him right away. Instead, black flames rose from his palm and slowly wrapped around the two dead devils first, devouring their bodies, bloodline energy, and remaining devil power.","Then he looked down at the sealed devil. \"I still need more information before reaching Bloodstone City.\"","The devil trembled on the ground.","Max’s expression stayed the same.","He looked down at the sealed devil beneath his feet and spoke in a calm voice. \"Talk properly while you lead me to Bloodstone City, and your death will come quick.\"","The devil’s body trembled. He knew those words weren’t a threat meant to scare him. They were a plain statement. After watching two of his companions die in an instant, he no longer had the nerve to test Max’s patience. He nodded quickly and forced himself to stand, though his legs still felt weak from fear.","\"Alright, alright,\" the devil said fast. \"I’ll lead the way. I’ll tell you everything I know.\"","Max pulled the seal back slightly, leaving just enough power inside the devil’s body to keep him from escaping or using his devil energy recklessly. The devil clearly sensed it too. His face went even paler, but he didn’t dare complain. He turned toward the direction he’d pointed earlier and started leading Max across the pale yellow land.","As they traveled, the devil talked without waiting for Max to ask too many questions. At first his voice shook. But once he realized Max genuinely wanted information and wasn’t planning to kill him right away, he started explaining more carefully.","What he shared turned out useful. Some of it matched what Freya and Arvantos had already hinted at, while some of it gave Max a clearer picture of the place he’d just entered.","According to the devil, the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage split into three major regions.","The first region was the outer layer. This was where most newcomers landed when they entered the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage for the first time. It stretched vast and chaotic, filled with danger, but compared to the deeper regions, it still counted as the safest part of the pilgrimage.","New participants from all five universes usually got scattered across different areas of the outer layer. Some appeared near cities. Some appeared near wilderness. Some appeared near beast territories, ruined lands, abandoned trial grounds, or places where hunters like the three devils waited for fresh prey.","The outer layer was a place of adaptation. Newcomers learned the rules there. They learned about marks, cities, trials, dangers, factions, and the cruelty of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. Those who adjusted quickly could gather marks and resources before pushing forward. Those who stayed naive usually turned into targets for beasts, traps, old participants, or geniuses from rival races.","The second region was the inner layer. The devil’s tone turned noticeably more serious when he brought it up.","The inner layer counted as the main region of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage and also the largest part of the entire place. Most famous trials, ancient ruins, inheritance grounds, bloodline pools, law comprehension zones, body tempering grounds, and mark exchange cities were said to sit there. Almost every genius who entered the pilgrimage dreamed of reaching the inner layer, since that’s where the real opportunities started showing up.","\"The outer layer has opportunities too,\" the devil explained as he walked. \"But most of them are small. Enough for weaker participants or newcomers, sure, but not enough for the real monsters. The inner layer’s different. That’s where the geniuses of the five races truly start competing.\"","Max listened quietly.","The devil continued, \"If someone wants to make a name for themselves in the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, they have to enter the inner layer. If they can’t even reach that place, then no matter how famous they were outside, people here just see them as ordinary.\"","The inner layer also drew the most attention from stronger participants because it was dangerous but still reachable. It wasn’t like the outer layer, where a lot of newcomers wandered around with no direction, and it wasn’t like the core layer, where only the most terrifying geniuses could even step inside.","The inner layer was the great battlefield of the pilgrimage, the place where most conflicts between the five races played out and where countless reputations got built or destroyed.","Then there was the third region. The core layer.","When the devil said those words, even his voice dropped instinctively.","The core layer was the most mysterious part of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. Legend claimed it was the true center of the entire place, the region holding the deepest secrets and most ancient inheritances.","But unlike the outer and inner layers, the core layer wasn’t a place people could enter just because they wanted to. Only the strongest of the strongest geniuses had any real chance of getting inside.","The devil glanced back at Max nervously and said, \"Legend says that since the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage first appeared, fewer than a hundred people have ever entered the core layer.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"Fewer than a hundred?\"","That number was shockingly low. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage had existed since time immemorial. Nobody knew who’d created it, when it first appeared, or what purpose it truly served. Every time its gates opened, geniuses from all five universes poured in. The Primordial Universe, Devil Universe, Spirit Universe, Angel Universe, and Dragon Universe all sent their strongest young talents inside.","The number of participants wasn’t small. Each opening pulled in a massive wave of geniuses, and over countless eras, the total number of people who’d entered the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage should have reached an unimaginable scale. Yet out of all of them, fewer than a hundred had ever reached the core layer.","That made the core layer terrifyingly rare. It also made it unimaginably mysterious."]},{"number":2038,"title":"Chapter 2038: Bloodstone City!","paragraphs":["Max’s interest deepened. \"What’s inside the core layer?\" he asked.","The devil hesitated for a moment, but when he felt the faint pressure of the seal inside his body tighten, he answered quickly.","\"I don’t know the details. People like me aren’t qualified to know much about that place. But according to the rumors, the core layer holds the main inheritance left behind by the owner of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.\"","Max’s gaze sharpened. The owner of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. That was the first time he’d heard this place might have an owner.","The devil continued, \"Some say the owner was a god. Some say he was a godslayer. Some say he killed gods and built this place out of their corpses, laws, weapons, blood, and broken worlds. Others say the pilgrimage itself is a test left behind to find someone worthy of inheriting his path.\"","The devil swallowed before going on. \"But nobody knows the truth. At least, nobody in the outer layer knows. Even in the inner layer, most people only know rumors.\"","Max’s eyes deepened.","A place beyond the Wall of Eternity. A pilgrimage connected to all five universes. A mark system even Primarchs couldn’t freely explain. An outer layer, an inner layer, and a core layer that fewer than a hundred people had entered since time immemorial. And now, a rumor that the core layer held the main inheritance of the mysterious owner of this entire place.","No matter how Max looked at it, the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage ran far more extraordinary than he’d first imagined.","The devil kept walking as he talked. \"The core layer’s also said to be the real testing ground for the geniuses of the five races. The outer layer tests whether you can survive. The inner layer tests whether you can compete. But the core layer tests whether you’re truly qualified to stand above the geniuses of all five universes.\"","Max stayed silent. Those words carried weight. The core layer wasn’t just the deepest region. It was the place where the strongest geniuses of every race got measured against each other.","Maybe that explained why fewer than a hundred had entered it. Getting into the core layer likely demanded more than strength alone. It might require marks, achievements, talent, comprehension, bloodline, and recognition from the rules of the pilgrimage itself.","The devil glanced back and saw Max’s calm expression. For some reason, that calm scared him more than anger would have.","He quickly continued, \"Bloodstone City’s only an outer layer city. It’s not one of the great cities, but it’s still a proper gathering point. You can buy information there, exchange marks, accept tasks, learn about nearby trials, and find out how to reach the stronger regions. Most newcomers who survive the first few days try to head there.\"","Max nodded slightly.","About an hour later, the silhouette of a city came into view. Seeing that, Max came to a stop, and so did the devil.","\"What’s wrong?\" the devil asked.","\"Wait a minute,\" Max said, waving his right hand.","The void ring inside the devil flew out of his body, freeing him again, but before the devil could feel relieved, a different void ring entered his body. This time he didn’t feel his energy getting sealed or anything like that, but a strange feeling told him Max had done something worse than before.","\"What did you do?\" the devil asked, fear in his voice.","\"I planted a slave seal on you,\" Max said calmly. \"You’re under my control now. If I want you dead, you’ll die. So watch what you say once we reach Bloodstone City, and follow my lead.\"","\"What?\" The devil looked shocked. He hadn’t expected Max to go this far.","\"Do you understand or not?\" Max asked in an authoritative tone.","\"I understand, I understand!\" The devil nodded his head fast.","\"Good.\" Max smiled. He hadn’t expected the many techniques and uses hidden inside the Voidwalker Inheritance’s void rings to come in handy like this, but he wasn’t complaining at all.","\"Now let’s head into the city,\" Max said, smiling. \"You go ahead and keep some distance from me. It’d look too suspicious if a devil and a Primordial showed up together.\"","He added, \"I’ll call you when I need you. And if you have anything to say to me, just talk to yourself and I will know. Now move.\"","The devil nodded and flew off toward Bloodstone City.","Max followed after him slowly.","The journey wasn’t long, but it wasn’t peaceful either. Along the way, Max saw traces of many battles scattered across the pale yellow land.","Claw marks were carved deep into the ground, broken weapons lay half-buried beneath the dust, dried blood stains hadn’t faded even under the strange sunlight, and faint remnants of laws still lingered in the air like invisible wounds.","In several spots, Max sensed the aura of beasts far stronger than the six-headed wolf he’d killed earlier, but those beasts kept their distance, probably because the path they were walking was one commonly used by people heading toward the city.","After a while, the outline of Bloodstone City finally appeared in the distance.","At first it looked like a dark red mountain rising from the pale yellow earth. But as they got closer, Max realized it wasn’t a mountain at all. It was a massive city built from crimson stone, black metal, and ancient bones.","Its walls stood tall and thick, and every stone seemed soaked in blood from countless years. Strange symbols were carved across the walls, and several large gates stood open beneath towering arches.","Above the gates, a blood-red crystal floated silently, casting a faint light that swept over everyone who entered.","The devil walking ahead of Max slowed his steps on instinct.","\"This is Bloodstone City,\" he said in a low voice. \"It’s one of the outer layer cities. Not the safest place, but open killing inside the city is forbidden unless both sides agree to a duel or the city rules allow it. That’s why a lot of newcomers try to reach this place first.\"","Max glanced at him. \"Forbidden by who?\"","The devil swallowed. \"By the city rules.\"","Max’s eyes moved slightly. \"And who enforces those rules?\"","The devil hesitated for a moment before answering. \"The city itself.\"","Max didn’t ask any further, but his interest deepened. A city that enforced its own rules. That alone told him Bloodstone City wasn’t just a settlement built by cultivators. It was part of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage system, or at least deeply tied to it."]},{"number":2039,"title":"Chapter 2039: People From All Races!","paragraphs":["They approached the gate. The blood-red crystal above the entrance released a beam of light that swept over Max. The bronze mark on his wrist warmed slightly, and then the pressure disappeared.","No one stopped him. No guard questioned him. No fee got demanded. The devil beside him passed through the gate too, though his face stayed pale since the seal Max had placed inside his body was still there.","The moment Max stepped into Bloodstone City, his gaze sharpened. The city turned out far livelier than he expected. Wide streets stretched in several directions, paved with dark red stone that gave off a faint heat.","Tall buildings rose on both sides, some shaped like towers, some like fortresses, some like ancient temples converted into shops, halls, or resting places.","Strange signs floated in the air, glowing in different colors. Some displayed words related to mark exchange. Some advertised information halls. Some belonged to weapon stores, beast material shops, cultivation chambers, healing pavilions, and trial registration halls.","The most striking thing wasn’t the city itself. It was the people. For the first time since entering the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, Max saw beings from all five races gathered in the same place.","Primordials walked through the streets with calm, proud expressions. Their auras came off stable, deep, and naturally close to the laws around them.","Some had faint golden patterns on their skin. Some carried ancient weapons on their backs. Some moved in groups, while others walked alone with the confidence of people who didn’t fear being challenged.","Devils were around too. Their dark skin, horns, crimson tattoos, and savage auras made them easy to spot. Some stood huge and muscular, while others looked lean and cruel.","Their eyes often carried violence, and plenty of them didn’t bother hiding their hostility toward members of the Primordial Universe. Still, despite their sneers and cold stares, none of them attacked openly.","Then Max saw the Spirit Race for the first time. They took humanoid form, but there was an otherworldly quality to how they looked. Their skin carried faint natural colors, like pale green, soft blue, moon-white, and light gold.","Some had hair that flowed like water, while others had hair resembling leaves, silver grass, or strands of soft light. Their eyes glowed clear and luminous, and their bodies seemed to breathe with the energy around them.","Unlike the devils, who gave off oppressive and brutal auras, the Spirit Race gave Max the feeling of living law and natural harmony. Some had small vines coiling around their wrists. Some had faint elemental halos behind them. Some walked barefoot across the stone streets, yet dust never seemed to touch their feet.","Max’s gaze paused on them for a moment. \"So those are true spirits in humanoid form,\" he muttered inwardly.","They were different from elves, different from humans, and different from Primordials. Their existence felt closer to nature itself, as if they’d been born from the breath of the world rather than from flesh alone.","Not far off, Max also spotted members of the Angel Race. Their appearances reminded him strongly of elves. Most stood tall, elegant, and almost impossibly beautiful. Their features looked refined, their skin fair, their hair coming in shades of silver, gold, white, and pale blue. Some had pointed ears, and their eyes carried a calm but distant pride.","Unlike ordinary elves, though, each of them had a golden halo floating above their head. Some halos were simple rings of light, while others were layered with runes, feathers, or sword-like patterns. Their auras came off pure, bright, and filled with a kind of holy order that made the surrounding space feel cleaner wherever they walked.","The sight sent Max’s thoughts drifting. He remembered Planet Orion. He remembered Kazreth. That mysterious being had carried an aura similar to the Angel Race, but far stronger and more oppressive.","Back then, Max had guessed Kazreth might be the leader of the Angel Race, or at least someone standing extremely high in their hierarchy. Now, after seeing these angels in Bloodstone City, that feeling only grew stronger.","The angels here carried real power. But compared to the memory of Kazreth, they felt like sparks before a sun.","Max pulled his gaze away and kept looking around. Soon he spotted members of the Dragon Race. They also took humanoid form, but they looked very different from Max’s own dragon transformation.","Max’s dragon power usually showed up when he activated his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline or transformed parts of his body. These Dragon Race members, though, carried dragon traits naturally even while holding humanoid shape.","Scales covered parts of their bodies like armor. Some had scales across their arms and shoulders. Some had scales running along their necks and faces. Some had long tails, sharp claws, or horns curving backward from their heads.","Their pupils looked narrow and beast-like, and their physical auras felt dense, heavy, and full of overwhelming vitality.","Some of them looked toward Max as he passed. Their gazes lingered on him for a moment, as if sensing the dragon aura hidden inside his body. But since Max didn’t openly reveal his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline, they only looked at him with mild curiosity before turning away.","Max quietly took it all in. He’d expected trouble the moment he entered Bloodstone City.","After all, outside the city, three devils had been guarding a newbie spawning area just to rob and kill fresh arrivals. He’d figured a city packed with geniuses from all five races would be even more chaotic. He’d expected sneers, provocations, challenges, and maybe even immediate attacks.","But to his surprise, Bloodstone City felt fairly peaceful. Not friendly. Not gentle. But peaceful in its own cold way.","Everyone seemed caught up in their own business. Some hurried toward mark exchange halls. Some gathered near information boards. Some entered weapon shops or healing pavilions. Some sat in open courtyards negotiating trades.","Some stood outside large halls, forming temporary teams for nearby trials. The air carried tension, but it was controlled tension, like blades kept inside sheaths. Everyone here might be dangerous, but nobody drew their weapon without a reason."]},{"number":2040,"title":"Chapter 2040: Being an Anomaly!","paragraphs":["The devil beside Max whispered, \"Open killing’s forbidden here. That’s why the city looks calm. Outside the walls, it’s different.\"","Max gave him a brief glance. \"I can tell.\"","As Max walked deeper into the street, plenty of people noticed him. The Primordials reacted first. Several of them looked at Max and immediately sensed his cultivation realm.","When they realized he was only at the 1st level of the Law Manifestation Realm, strange expressions crossed their faces. Some looked surprised. Some frowned slightly. Some seemed puzzled about how someone at his level had even entered the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.","But once they sensed the Primordial aura in his body, most of them didn’t show any contempt. Instead, they nodded to him. It wasn’t a warm greeting, but it counted as recognition. Maybe they assumed he had some unusual background.","Maybe they figured anyone who could enter this place despite such low cultivation couldn’t be completely ordinary. Or maybe it was simply because he carried Primordial Bloodline, and in a city where all five races gathered, people from the same universe naturally kept up at least a surface-level courtesy toward each other.","The devils reacted very differently. Plenty of them sneered when they saw Max.","\"A Law Manifestation Realm Primordial?\"","\"He came here to die?\"","\"Maybe some old monster threw him in for tempering. If he leaves the city, he won’t last long.\"","Their voices weren’t loud, but Max heard them clearly. He ignored them. If he reacted to every sneer, he’d waste too much time.","Besides, the three devils outside the city had sat at the 2nd level of the Divine Lord Realm, and two of them were already dead. If the devils here wanted to underestimate him because of his cultivation, that was their problem.","Max’s calm reaction made some of the nearby Primordials glance at him again. A few of them looked slightly impressed.","The devil leading Max grew more nervous the deeper they went into the city. He clearly didn’t want to be seen walking with a Primordial, especially with a hidden seal still controlling his body. But Max didn’t care about his discomfort.","\"Where’s the information hall?\" Max asked.","The devil discretely pointed toward a tall building ahead. \"That one. The black tower with the bronze mark symbol above the entrance. Most newcomers head there first to buy basic information about the outer layer, nearby trials, mark rules, and routes toward the inner layer.\"","Max followed his gaze. A tall black tower stood at the end of the street. Above its entrance floated a large bronze circle with a sword in the middle, the same shape as the mark on Max’s wrist. Plenty of participants were entering and leaving the tower, most of them wearing serious expressions.","However, before Max could enter the information hall, several Primordials stepped into his path.","They didn’t look hostile, but their movements came off firm. There were three of them, each carrying a stable Primordial aura that felt far more natural than the newly awakened bloodline aura Max had seen among the ten geniuses chosen from the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","Their expressions stayed calm, their gazes lingering on Max’s face, cultivation, and wrist mark for a brief moment before one of them spoke.","\"Follow us.\"","After saying that, the Primordial turned and walked toward a quieter street without waiting for Max’s reply.","Max frowned slightly. He didn’t like being ordered around, especially in a place like Bloodstone City, where every race had its own agenda and every friendly face might hide another motive. But these people were Primordials, and their behavior didn’t carry obvious malice.","Since he’d just arrived in the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage and still knew very little about this place, it seemed better to see what they wanted before making any judgment.","Max glanced at the sealed devil beside him. \"You go ahead and wait for me at the information hall.\"","The devil’s expression shifted slightly, but he quickly lowered his head. He didn’t dare ask whether this meant he could escape. The seal inside his body was still there, and Max could crush him the moment he tried anything foolish.","\"I understand,\" the devil said quickly.","Max then followed the Primordials.","They led him away from the busy main street and into another part of Bloodstone City. The surroundings changed gradually. The crowded shops, loud exchanges, and mixed auras of the five races grew less dense.","The streets here were wider and cleaner, and the buildings carried fewer chaotic signs. Instead, most of them were built with a solemn, ancient style, as if they belonged not to merchants or wandering participants, but to factions that had occupied this city for a long time.","Soon, Max arrived in front of a large mansion-like building. The mansion was built from pale gold stone and dark red crystal, standing out clearly against the blood-colored structures surrounding it in Bloodstone City.","Its entrance was guarded by two tall Primordials, and above the gate floated a circular emblem giving off a calm golden glow. The symbol wasn’t exactly the same as the bronze mark on Max’s wrist, but it carried the same ancient feeling of recognition and authority.","Many Primordials could be seen entering and leaving the mansion. To Max’s surprise, there were also humans among them. Some of those humans wore battle robes, some carried swords, and some had auras clearly not inferior to the Primordials walking beside them.","This immediately told Max the building wasn’t purely a base of the Primordial Race. It was more likely the headquarters of their universe in Bloodstone City, a place where participants from the Primordial Universe could gather, exchange information, and get basic protection.","Max’s eyes moved slightly. ’So every race has a base here.’","That made sense. Bloodstone City might stay peaceful under the city rules, but the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage itself was still a place where the five races competed fiercely. In a place like this, each race naturally needed a foothold, especially in the outer layer where newcomers kept showing up constantly."]},{"number":2041,"title":"Chapter 2041: Anna!","paragraphs":["The Primordials led him through the entrance. The moment Max entered the mansion, a female Primordial walked toward him with a polite smile.","She looked young, though Max knew age could be deceiving in a place like this. Her hair was pale gold, her eyes clear and bright, and faint primordial patterns flowed across her skin like thin streams of light.","Her aura felt gentle, but not weak. Compared to the cold tension outside, she gave off a steadier and more welcoming presence.","\"Hello,\" she said. \"You must be new to the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. My name is Anna.\"","Max nodded slightly. \"I am new. Arrived not long ago.\"","Anna looked at him carefully. \"And your name?\"","\"Max Voidwalker.\"","The moment he said his name, Anna’s brows moved slightly.","\"Max Voidwalker.\"","She seemed to find the surname strange, or maybe familiar in a way she couldn’t immediately place. But she didn’t ask about it. After only a brief pause, her gaze shifted to his cultivation, and her expression turned more concerned.","\"How were you allowed to enter the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage with this level of cultivation?\"","Max shrugged slightly. He truly didn’t know how to answer that.","Anna sighed and pressed her fingers against her forehead, like she’d suddenly gotten a headache. \"How did the elders, even the Primarchs, agree to send someone at the Law Manifestation Realm into this place?\"","Max stayed silent.","Anna looked at him for another moment, then shook her head. \"Anyway, since you’re already here, there are a few things you need to know.\"","Her tone turned more serious. \"Bloodstone City is only one of many cities in the outer layer. Every major outer-layer city has bases belonging to the five races, so you’ll find people from the Primordial Universe, Devil Universe, Spirit Universe, Angel Universe, and Dragon Universe scattered throughout the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. Some cities are more balanced. Some are dominated by one race. Some are technically neutral, but everyone knows which faction actually holds the most influence there.\"","Max listened quietly.","Anna pointed toward his wrist. \"I’m guessing you already know something about the marks?\"","Max glanced at the bronze symbol on his skin. \"I’ve heard some information.\"","\"That’s good,\" Anna said. \"At least you’re not completely blind.\"","Then her expression turned stern. \"But do you understand how dangerous this place is for someone like you?\"","Max looked at her without answering.","Anna continued, \"You’re at the Law Manifestation Realm. Out in the wider world, that might already be enough to make countless cultivators admire you, especially with high talent. But in the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, this cultivation is dangerously low. The outer layer is packed with Divine Lord Realm geniuses. A lot of them have been here for years, and some have survived countless battles, trials, ambushes, and beast territories.\"","Her voice grew heavier. \"The inner layer is even worse. That place is full of Divine King Realm geniuses. The strongest among them are monsters who can fight across realms, crush ordinary Divine Kings, and compete for opportunities people in the outer layer can only dream about.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Anna looked at him directly. \"With your current cultivation, almost everyone who sees you will assume you’re easy prey. Devils will target you. Dragon Race members might challenge you. Angel Race cultivators might dismiss you outright. Even people from our own universe might wonder if you’re carrying some special treasure that let you in despite being so weak in cultivation.\"","She sighed again. \"Honestly, I’m surprised you made it from the spawning area to Bloodstone City in one piece.\"","Max ignored that last part, but Anna’s words gave him a much clearer picture of the overall power level in the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.","The outer layer was dominated by Divine Lord Realm geniuses. The inner layer was dominated by Divine King Realm geniuses. And he was only at the 1st level of the Law Manifestation Realm.","No wonder so many people had looked at him strangely when he entered Bloodstone City. From their perspective, his presence here was abnormal. Even among top geniuses, entering this place at his realm had to be extremely rare.","After a moment, Max asked, \"How long have you been here?\"","Anna smiled faintly. \"Around three years, I think.\"","\"Three years?\" Max’s eyes showed a trace of surprise. \"And you still haven’t entered the inner layer?\"","Anna stared at him for a moment. Then she laughed softly, not mockingly, but like his question was something only a true newcomer would ask.","\"You really think entering the inner layer is that easy?\"","Max didn’t answer.","Anna shook her head and said, \"I won’t get into every detail right now, but you should understand one thing. Out of every thousand participants in the outer layer, maybe only ten have a real shot at entering the inner layer.\"","Max’s expression finally changed. \"Only ten out of a thousand?\"","Anna nodded. \"That’s already a generous estimate. Plenty of people spend years here and still fail to meet the conditions. Some die trying. Some give up and stay in the outer layer, using their marks just for survival and cultivation resources. Some keep taking on trials until their foundations collapse or their luck runs out.\"","Max’s gaze deepened. Only around one percent had a real chance. That number reshaped his understanding of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage all over again. He’d already known the inner layer wouldn’t be easy to enter, but he hadn’t expected the gap to run this severe.","The outer layer wasn’t simply a beginner region everyone eventually moved past. It was a filtering ground. It swallowed the weak, trapped the ordinary, and let only a tiny number of truly capable geniuses pass through.","Anna looked at him seriously. \"That’s why I said you need to be careful. Surviving the outer layer’s already hard. Leaving it is much harder.\"","Max stayed silent for a moment. Then he looked toward the deeper part of the mansion. \"I understand.\"","His voice came out calm, but his eyes had sharpened.","The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage was far more dangerous than he’d expected.","Max thought for a moment before asking, \"Has anyone else from my batch arrived in this city?\"","Anna looked at him. \"You mean the new Primordials who entered with you?\"","Max nodded. \"Yes.\"","\"There are two,\" Anna replied. \"One’s from the Sword God Palace. His name’s Damian. The other’s Miss Revona.\"","Max’s eyes moved slightly. Damian and Revona had also landed near Bloodstone City.","\"As for the rest,\" Anna continued, \"they must’ve shown up near other cities in the outer layer. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage doesn’t send everyone to the same place. Even people who enter through the same entrance can end up scattered across different regions.\""]},{"number":2042,"title":"Chapter 2042: Anna’s Plan!","paragraphs":["Max nodded with understanding. That matched what he’d already guessed. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage was too vast, and the entry process seemed to follow its own rules. It was already lucky that Damian and Revona had ended up in the same city as him.","He glanced around the mansion and asked, \"So this place is the base for Primordials and humans from our universe?\"","Anna nodded. \"Yes. More precisely, this is the Bloodstone City base for participants from the Primordial Universe. Primordials, humans, and a few other races connected to our side can come here for help. If you need information, temporary lodging, basic supplies, introductions, or guidance, you can come here. As long as the request isn’t too outrageous, most people here will be willing to help.\"","\"I see,\" Max said.","At least now he had a proper foothold in Bloodstone City. That beat wandering around blindly and relying on a terrified devil for every scrap of information.","After thinking it over, Max turned toward the entrance. \"Then I’ll go to the information hall of Bloodstone City now.\"","He’d barely taken a step when Anna suddenly reached out from behind, grabbed his collar, and pulled him back.","Max nearly stumbled.","\"Where the hell are you going?\" Anna asked, her earlier polite smile gone in an instant.","Max turned his head and looked at her with a wry smile. \"To the information hall.\"","\"I heard you the first time,\" Anna said, her expression turning solemn. \"But do you understand what’ll happen if you go there openly?\"","Max didn’t answer right away.","Anna pointed at him and continued, \"You’re only at the 1st level of the Law Manifestation Realm. The moment you step into the information hall, plenty of people will notice you. That place isn’t like this base. Participants from all five races go there. Information brokers, scouts, hunters, faction members, and people looking for easy prey all keep their eyes on newcomers. Once word gets out that a Law Manifestation Realm Primordial has entered Bloodstone City, your existence will spread fast.\"","Her tone grew heavier. \"And when that happens, you’ll be as good as dead.\"","Max looked at her calmly. \"I have to go there, Anna.\"","Anna frowned. \"Why?\"","\"I’m new here,\" Max replied. \"I need to understand the situation in Bloodstone City, the outer layer, the nearby trials, the mark system, and the route toward the inner layer. I heard the information hall’s the best place for newcomers to learn the basics.\"","\"That’s true,\" Anna admitted.","She let go of his collar, but her expression stayed tense. She looked at Max for a moment, then fell into thought. Her brows furrowed slightly, and her fingers tapped against her arm, as if she were quickly weighing a few options. A few breaths later, her eyes lit up.","Then she clapped her hands once. \"I think I’ve got a plan.\"","Max raised a brow. \"A plan?\"","Anna pointed at him with a serious face. \"You. Stay here.\"","Max blinked.","\"Don’t move,\" Anna continued. \"Don’t wander outside. Don’t go to the information hall on your own. Don’t let some devil, dragon, angel, spirit, or even a bored Primordial drag you into trouble. I’ll be right back.\"","Max raised both hands slightly. \"I’m not going anywhere.\"","\"Good,\" Anna said.","Without another word, she turned and vanished deeper into the mansion.","Max watched her leave, then shook his head with a faint smile. ’Wonder what kind of plan she’s got.’","Since Anna had clearly told him to wait, Max didn’t try to leave. Instead, he started wandering slowly through the main hall of the mansion.","The interior turned out much bigger than it looked from outside. The hall stretched wide and bright, with pillars made of pale gold stone supporting a high ceiling engraved with faint primordial runes.","Several counters lined the sides, where participants talked with attendants about missions, marks, injuries, lodging, and information. A few groups sat around stone tables, quietly going over maps and routes. Others stood near floating screens displaying notices about nearby trials, dangerous zones, recent deaths, and faction movements.","Max took it all in carefully. Most of the people inside were Primordials, but there were also quite a few humans. Unlike the nervous newcomers outside, the participants here looked more experienced.","Their auras stayed stable, and their eyes carried the caution of people who’d survived the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage long enough to understand its cruelty.","Max silently checked their cultivation levels. The result wasn’t surprising, but it still gave him something to think about.","Most of the participants here sat at the 8th, 9th, or 10th level of the Divine Lord Realm. A smaller number sat at the middle levels of the Divine Lord Realm. As for those at the early levels, Max only spotted a few.","Law Manifestation Realm cultivators were almost nonexistent.","That alone explained Anna’s reaction. In this place, his cultivation realm wasn’t merely low. It was abnormal.","Even Anna herself had reached the 10th level of the Divine Lord Realm. Her aura had felt gentle when she greeted him, but thinking it over now, she was actually one of the stronger participants in this base. If she’d still stayed in the outer layer after three years at that cultivation, entering the inner layer clearly ran far harder than he’d imagined.","’Looks like all of them have spent a good number of years in the outer layer,’ Max thought.","That was the only reasonable explanation. These people hadn’t entered the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage yesterday. They’d survived, fought, cultivated, gathered marks, and slowly pushed themselves toward the peak of the Divine Lord Realm. Yet even then, most of them hadn’t made it into the inner layer.","The outer layer wasn’t a beginner area in any simple sense. It was a cruel filter. Only those strong enough, cautious enough, and lucky enough could even dream of moving forward.","As Max kept observing the hall, several Primordials and humans noticed him too. Their reactions all played out nearly the same way. First, they sensed the Primordial aura on him. Then they sensed his cultivation.","After that, their expressions turned strange. Some looked confused. Some frowned. Some whispered to their companions. A few nodded politely once they realized he belonged to their side, but even they couldn’t hide the doubt in their eyes. Clearly, they were all wondering the same thing.","How had someone at the Law Manifestation Realm gotten into the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage?","Max ignored their stares. He’d already gotten used to this kind of reaction. In the Divine Realm, people had underestimated him because of his age, background, realm, or lack of reputation.","Here, they’d underestimate him because his cultivation sat far below the common standard of the outer layer. That was fine. Sometimes being underestimated worked out better than being feared.","Still, Anna was right about one thing. If too many people learned about him too fast, trouble would come."]},{"number":2043,"title":"Chapter 2043: Daniel!","paragraphs":["As Max kept observing the mansion, Anna finally returned. This time, she wasn’t alone. Two familiar figures walked beside her.","Damian and Revona.","The moment Damian saw Max, a faint smile crossed his face. \"Max, you’re here too.\"","His expression made it clear he’d thought only he and Revona had made it to Bloodstone City. Seeing Max here was a pleasant surprise.","Max smiled lightly too. \"Damian, Revona. Looks like the three of us are the only ones from our batch who landed near Bloodstone City.\"","Revona nodded. \"That’s probably the case. Bloodstone City isn’t far from one of the nearby spawning points. Anyone who appeared around that region should’ve reached the city by now, if they survived the journey. Since we haven’t heard anything about the others, they most likely landed near different cities in the outer layer.\"","Damian nodded along. \"That makes sense. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage is way too big to gather everyone in one place.\"","Max wasn’t surprised by any of this. Arvantos had already warned them they might get separated after entering, but running into two familiar faces this soon still felt reassuring. In a place like this, even a familiar rival beat complete strangers.","Anna clapped her hands lightly, pulling their attention back to her. \"Now, let’s head to the Information Hall.\"","She looked at Max with a half-serious, half-helpless expression. \"Since you insist on going, you should at least go with people you know. Damian and Miss Revona haven’t visited the Information Hall either, so the three of you can go together.\"","Max had no objection. \"Then let’s go,\" he said.","Anna nodded, but instead of leaving right away, she looked around the mansion like she was searching for someone. \"We’re still missing one more person. Let’s wait for him.\"","Max raised a brow. \"Who?\"","Damian and Revona looked curious too.","\"Daniel,\" Anna said lightly.","Max stayed calm, since the name meant nothing to him. But Damian and Revona reacted differently. Their eyes moved slightly, and they exchanged faint looks of surprise. Max had just arrived in Bloodstone City and knew almost nothing about the important figures here, but Damian and Revona had already spent some time deeper inside the mansion. Because of that, they’d already heard a fair bit about Daniel.","Daniel counted as one of the three strongest Primordials currently stationed in Bloodstone City. He’d defeated many geniuses from the other four races and built up a powerful reputation in the outer layer.","There was even a rumor that he’d once fought two top geniuses from the Angel Race and Dragon Race at the same time without losing. Whether that rumor was fully true or not, the fact that people still talked about it said a lot about how formidable he was.","But what really made Daniel famous was his spot on the Bloodstone City Rankings. He sat at seventh. That meant he counted as one of the strongest young experts in the entire city, not just among Primordials but across all five races gathered here.","Damian and Revona couldn’t quite figure out how Anna had managed to call someone like him over just to walk three newcomers to the Information Hall.","Just as they were wondering about it, another Primordial walked toward them. He stood tall, around six feet, with a lean but powerful build. His hair was dark red, and his eyes carried a relaxed confidence that didn’t feel forced. Unlike a lot of geniuses who deliberately let their aura show to prove strength, Daniel’s presence stayed restrained.","That restraint made him feel even more dangerous, like the power inside him had been tempered through years of real battles.","\"Hey, Anna,\" Daniel said casually. His gaze moved across Max, Damian, and Revona. \"These the three newbies?\"","Anna nodded with a smile. \"Yeah. I’m taking them to the Information Hall, so I figured I’d bring you along.\"","Daniel stared at her for a moment. For a rare instant, his expression went speechless. \"No need for me to tag along if you’re the one taking them there,\" he said helplessly.","Anna pointed at Max without hesitation. \"Look at him.\"","Daniel followed her finger and looked at Max.","Anna continued seriously, \"He’s only at the 1st level of the Law Manifestation Realm, and yet he walked into Bloodstone City openly. Now he wants to walk into the Information Hall, where people from all five races gather to buy and sell news. If some arrogant fools from the other races notice him, they might start something just to test him.\"","Max looked at Anna with a faintly helpless expression.","She ignored him and kept going. \"That’s why I want you with us. You’ll act as a deterrent.\"","Daniel smiled wryly. Others might not know it, but he knew Anna wasn’t weak either. With her around, ordinary troublemakers would already think twice. Still, he understood her concern.","A Law Manifestation Realm newcomer walking into the Information Hall would definitely draw attention. Even with open killing forbidden inside the city, provocation, schemes, challenges, and targeted information leaks were still very much on the table.","Since he wasn’t busy, Daniel didn’t refuse. \"Fine,\" he said with a light smile. \"Let’s go.\"","Anna nodded, satisfied.","With that, the group left the mansion and headed toward the Information Hall. As they walked, Anna introduced Daniel to the three of them and introduced Max, Damian, and Revona to Daniel in return.","Daniel didn’t act arrogant despite his ranking. He greeted Damian and Revona politely, and when his gaze landed on Max, curiosity showed in his eyes, but no contempt.","\"So you’re the Law Manifestation Realm newcomer everyone’s about to start talking about,\" Daniel said with a faint smile.","Max glanced at him. \"That doesn’t sound like a good thing.\"","\"It’s not,\" Daniel replied honestly. \"But it’s not necessarily bad either. In the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, attention can bring danger, but it can also bring opportunities. The real question is whether you’ve got the strength to control what kind of attention sticks around you.\"","Max nodded slightly. That answer felt practical.","The group soon reached the black tower Max had spotted earlier. The Information Hall stood at the end of the wide street, taller than most surrounding buildings and far more crowded. Its walls were made of dark stone that seemed to soak up light, and countless glowing inscriptions moved across its surface like living words.","Above the entrance floated a large bronze symbol shaped like a circle with a sword at its center, almost identical to the mark on Max’s wrist. Around that symbol, smaller lights flickered constantly, each one carrying fragments of information, announcements, rankings, warnings, and transaction notices."]},{"number":2044,"title":"Chapter 2044: Infor for Newbies!","paragraphs":["Participants from all five races moved in and out of the hall. Primordials walked in with calm expressions. Devils strode out sneering at something they’d just heard. Spirit Race members gathered near the entrance, quietly exchanging information through glowing leaves of energy.","Angels stood in small groups, their golden halos casting gentle light over their elegant figures. Dragon Race geniuses leaned against the stone pillars outside, their scaled arms folded across their chests as they watched the crowd with beast-like patience.","The moment Max approached with Anna, Daniel, Damian, and Revona, several gazes turned toward them. Some recognized Anna. More recognized Daniel. Because Daniel stood there, the gazes landing on Max didn’t linger too recklessly.","A few devils noticed his cultivation and flashed mocking smiles, but after spotting Daniel walking beside him, they quickly looked away. Even the curious ones didn’t step forward to provoke him.","Anna glanced at Max. \"See? This is why I brought him.\"","Max smiled faintly and said nothing.","They entered the Information Hall together. The moment they stepped inside, Max felt like he’d entered a completely different world.","The interior stretched vast, far larger than the tower looked from outside. It had clearly been expanded through spatial formations.","Floors rose in layers above them, connected by floating stairways and circular platforms drifting through the air. Countless information screens hovered everywhere, displaying maps, city notices, mark exchange rates, trial locations, beast warnings, faction disputes, recent deaths, ranking changes, and basic guides for newcomers.","The hall was noisy but organized. Voices filled the air from every direction. Some people were buying maps. Some were arguing with information brokers. Some were checking the rankings. Some were digging through trial records.","Some gathered around large floating boards discussing newly discovered ruins and dangerous zones. Despite the crowd, the atmosphere stayed controlled, like the rules of Bloodstone City reached deep into this place too.","Max looked around carefully. This was exactly what he needed.","Anna noticed his expression and started explaining. \"The Information Hall’s one of the most important places for newcomers. Almost every proper city in the outer layer has one. Some run bigger than this, some smaller, and some get controlled more heavily by certain races, but their function stays mostly the same.\"","She pointed toward the floating screens. \"Here, you can learn the basic rules of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. You can buy maps of nearby regions, gather information about trial grounds, learn which beast territories to avoid, check mark-related rules, see rankings, purchase news about the inner layer, and even hire guides or join temporary teams.\"","Damian looked toward one of the screens showing a map of the surrounding region. \"So this place holds everything a newcomer needs to avoid dying blindly.\"","Anna nodded. \"Exactly. Though the free information only covers the basics. Anything valuable requires marks.\"","Revona smiled faintly. \"Naturally.\"","Anna continued, \"Information’s one of the most expensive things in the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage. Good information can save your life, lead you to an opportunity, or help you dodge a trap. Bad information can kill you faster than an enemy’s blade.\"","Max’s gaze moved across the hall. He spotted one counter marked Basic Newcomer Knowledge. Another was marked Outer Layer Maps. Farther off, a larger platform displayed Bloodstone City Rankings.","A separate area seemed to sell information about nearby ruins, while another section was surrounded by participants scanning team recruitment notices.","Anna said, \"Since all three of you are new, you should grab the basic information package first. It covers the outer layer, city rules, mark usage, common dangers, and how to dodge the most obvious traps. After that, you can decide what specific information you want to buy.\"","Daniel added calmly, \"Don’t spend your marks carelessly. Newcomers usually waste their first marks on stuff that sounds impressive but ends up useless. Buy what helps you survive first. Opportunities come later.\"","Max glanced at him and nodded.","The devil he’d captured had already told him a lot, but compared to the scale of information inside this hall, that devil’s knowledge was clearly limited.","If Max wanted to properly understand the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, especially the path to the inner layer, the core layer, and anything tied to the Eternal Body, he needed more reliable sources.","As they moved deeper into the Information Hall, more gazes fell on Max. This time, he could feel the curiosity more clearly. A Law Manifestation Realm cultivator entering the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage was just too unusual.","Even with Daniel beside him, people couldn’t help but stare. Some Primordials frowned in confusion. Several devils sneered from a distance. A few angels glanced at him with cold indifference, while one or two Dragon Race geniuses looked like they were trying to sense whether his weak realm hid something unusual underneath.","Max ignored all of it, keeping his eyes calm as he looked toward the information counters ahead.","Most of the basic information displayed inside the Information Hall had already been explained to Max by the devil he’d captured earlier. Even so, Max didn’t skip over it.","The devil had been terrified while speaking, and fear usually made people more honest, but Max wasn’t careless enough to take everything at face value without checking. This was the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, a place where information could mean the difference between life and death.","If the devil had hidden something, twisted something, or deliberately left out an important detail, Max needed to know before it caused him trouble later.","So he carefully read through the newcomer information package. The outer layer. The inner layer. The core layer. The five grades of marks. Bloodstone City’s basic rules. The common dangers outside the city. The role of Information Halls, exchange halls, trial grounds, and race bases.","After a few minutes, Max confirmed that most of what the devil had told him checked out. No obvious lies, at least not in what he’d already shared. Bloodstone City really was one of the outer layer cities.","Open killing inside the city really was restricted by the city’s own rules. Marks really did serve as the main currency, status symbol, and proof of achievement in the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.","The outer layer really was filled mostly with Divine Lord Realm participants, while the inner layer really was dominated by Divine King Realm geniuses."]},{"number":2045,"title":"Chapter 2045: Ascension Seals!","paragraphs":["Max’s expression stayed calm as he kept reading. Then his eyes suddenly stopped. One title caught his attention.","Ascension Seals.","Max narrowed his eyes slightly. This was the first time he’d seen that term since entering the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.","The devil had explained marks in great detail, and had talked about Bloodstone City, the outer layer, the inner layer, and the core layer, but he’d never once mentioned Ascension Seals. Whether that came from ignorance or a deliberate dodge, Max couldn’t say yet.","Curious, Max opened the information entry and started reading. A few minutes later, he finally understood why entering the inner layer was so hard.","To enter the inner layer, a participant needed something called an Ascension Seal. Only one Ascension Seal was required. At first glance, that sounded simple. But the real difficulty lay in getting one.","Ascension Seals ranked among the rarest things in the outer layer. Unlike marks, you couldn’t earn them by killing beasts, completing ordinary tasks, robbing other participants, or exchanging resources in cities.","They never showed up randomly in shops, and no one could buy them through normal mark transactions. Even powerful factions in the outer layer couldn’t produce them on demand.","There was only one known way to get an Ascension Seal.","The Ascension Trial.","Every few years, the Ascension Trial would descend somewhere in the outer layer. Its location was never fixed, and once it appeared, word of it would spread through the cities like wildfire.","Nearly every powerful genius in the outer layer would rush toward it, because the Ascension Trial was the only recognized path to obtain an Ascension Seal and earn the right to step into the inner layer.","Max kept reading, and his expression finally shifted slightly. Every time the Ascension Trial descended, it carried only ten Ascension Seals.","Ten. That number sounded almost absurdly small.","Max slowly leaned back and looked at the glowing information screen in front of him. The outer layer stretched enormous. It held many cities like Bloodstone City, countless wilderness regions, beast territories, ruins, trial grounds, and race bases.","Every time the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage opened, geniuses from all five universes poured in. Some stayed for years. Some stayed for decades. Some never managed to leave the outer layer at all.","If Max’s math was right, the number of participants in the outer layer could easily surpass one or two million. Yet every few years, only ten Ascension Seals showed up.","No wonder Anna had said that out of every thousand people, maybe only ten had a real shot at entering the inner layer. Honestly, even that estimate might have been generous.","The Ascension Trial wasn’t merely a trial. It was a bloodbath. When only ten seals appeared in front of countless geniuses who’d spent years struggling in the outer layer, the competition couldn’t stay peaceful.","Every genius who wanted to advance would fight for them. Every race would send its strongest outer layer participants. Every hidden expert’s disciple, every Primordial, every devil, every angel, every dragon, and every spirit confident enough would gather around the trial.","Those ten seals weren’t opportunities handed out to the talented. They were prizes that had to be ripped away from a battlefield.","Max’s gaze deepened. Now he understood why so many participants stayed stuck in the outer layer despite already reaching the 8th, 9th, or even 10th level of the Divine Lord Realm.","Their cultivation might be strong enough to survive here, but survival alone wasn’t enough to enter the inner layer. They needed an Ascension Seal, and getting one meant beating countless opponents who were just as desperate, just as prepared, and often far more experienced.","The difficulty was terrifying.","For most participants, the outer layer wasn’t a temporary stop before the real pilgrimage began. It was a cage. A massive cage filled with marks, trials, beasts, cities, and endless competition, where only a tiny number of people could ever break through the ceiling and move forward.","To Max, the outer layer was starting to feel less like a simple starting region and more like an enormous filter. It was a place built to throw countless geniuses from all five universes into danger, pressure, competition, and uncertainty.","Those who lacked strength would die. Those who lacked caution would get hunted down. Those who lacked persistence would stay trapped here for years. Only a very small number, those strong enough to seize Ascension Seals away from countless rivals, would ever get to step into the inner layer.","The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage wasn’t guiding geniuses forward gently. It was forcing them to prove they deserved to move forward at all.","After reading about the Ascension Seals, Max shifted his attention to another section of the information screen.","Bloodstone City Rankings.","The ranking only recorded the top one hundred geniuses in Bloodstone City. Beside each name sat the race or faction they belonged to, which made the list more than just a measure of individual strength. It also revealed the balance of power within the city.","Max’s gaze moved down the names slowly. Soon he spotted Daniel’s. Daniel sat at seventh, and beside his name was written one word.","Primordial.","Max wasn’t surprised. Damian and Revona had already reacted strongly when Anna mentioned Daniel, and now Max understood why.","Ranking seventh in a city where geniuses from all five universes gathered was no small feat. It meant Daniel wasn’t just strong among Primordials. He was one of the strongest figures in Bloodstone City overall.","Max kept reading.","First place belonged to Greyon of the Dragon Race. Second place belonged to Hemilin of the Angel Race. Third place belonged to Raymond of the Primordial Race. Fourth place belonged to Drevor of the Devil Race. Fifth place belonged to Shreya of the Spirit Race.","Looking at the top five, Max got a clearer picture of the power structure in Bloodstone City. Each of the five great races had at least one terrifying genius near the peak of the rankings.","The Dragon Race held first, the Angel Race held second, the Primordial Race held third, the Devil Race held fourth, and the Spirit Race held fifth. Just from that lineup alone, it was clear no single race completely dominated Bloodstone City.","The balance here ran delicate. Every race had powerful representatives. Every race carried enough strength to keep the others cautious.","Max’s eyes moved further down the list. As expected, the five great races took up many of the higher spots. Primordials, devils, angels, dragons, and spirits kept appearing throughout the ranking, proving they were the main powers of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage.","Their bloodlines, inheritances, bodies, souls, and foundations gave them an edge most other races couldn’t easily match.","But they weren’t the only ones on the list. Max also spotted humans. He saw elves. He saw demons. He saw names belonging to other lesser races he’d never even heard of before. Some ranked low, but a few had climbed surprisingly high. That made Max’s eyes sharpen slightly.","The five great races dominated, sure, but the so-called lesser races weren’t without their own monsters. Any genius who could force their way onto the Bloodstone City Rankings while competing against the five great races couldn’t be ordinary.","That realization made Max take the list a lot more seriously. The Bloodstone City Rankings weren’t just some display of fame.","They were a warning. Every name on that list belonged to someone who’d survived the outer layer, built up enough strength, beaten enough opponents, and earned enough recognition to be feared or respected in Bloodstone City.","Some of them were enemies. Some might turn into temporary allies. Some would stay neutral unless there was something in it for them. But none of them deserved to be underestimated."]},{"number":2046,"title":"Chapter 2046: Battle Space!","paragraphs":["\"Did you understand everything?\"","Anna’s voice came from behind just as Max finished looking through the Bloodstone City Rankings.","Max turned around and saw her walking toward him with Daniel, Damian, and Revona nearby. He nodded calmly. \"Almost.\"","Anna grinned, like she’d already expected that answer. \"So do you get now why I said entering the inner layer is so hard?\"","Max glanced back at the information screen for a moment before nodding. \"I knew it wouldn’t be easy, but I honestly didn’t expect the difficulty to run this high. Guess I underestimated the outer layer.\"","\"You’re not the first newcomer to think that way,\" Anna said. \"Most people assume the outer layer’s just a starting region, but after they stick around for a while, they realize this place alone is enough to trap countless geniuses.\"","\"You two talking about Ascension Seals?\" Damian asked as he walked over.","Anna nodded. \"Yeah.\"","Damian’s expression turned solemn. \"I read about them too.\" He looked at Max and continued in a heavier tone. \"From the looks of it, we might end up stuck in the outer layer for a couple of years.\"","Max nodded lightly, though his thoughts ran differently. He had no intention of settling down here like most people. The Godslayer’s Pilgrimage was dangerous, and the outer layer clearly held plenty of opportunities, but wasting years here wasn’t something he could accept.","They only had five hundred years before the final war with the devils, and next to a threat that size, even five hundred years didn’t stretch far. If he wanted the Eternal Body, if he wanted to uncover the deeper secrets of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, and if he wanted to grow strong enough to shape the coming battlefield, he needed to reach the inner layer as fast as possible.","After that, he needed to get into the core layer too.","Staying in the outer layer for years just because everyone else considered it normal would be foolish.","A moment later, Revona came back too. Unlike Damian, she wore a bright smile, a faint excitement showing in her eyes. Before anyone could ask where she’d gone, she raised her wrist toward Max and Damian.","\"Look what I got.\"","The bronze mark on her wrist glowed faintly. Inside the glow, a number showed clearly.","Three hundred and twenty-five.","Damian’s eyes shifted slightly. \"Did you get those from the Battle Space?\"","Revona nodded, clearly satisfied. \"Yeah. Didn’t expect the Battle Space to allow mark betting, but it does. Fought a few matches, and the other side underestimated me badly.\"","Anna smiled hearing that. \"The Battle Space is one of the most popular spots in every outer layer city. It’s also the only area inside the cities where people can fight freely without breaking city rules.\"","Max looked at her.","Anna explained patiently, \"The Battle Space gets built through extremely powerful virtual runes and spatial formations. When someone enters, their real body stays safe, while their consciousness and battle projection show up inside the arena. Because of that, even if you kill your opponent inside the Battle Space, or your opponent kills you, neither side actually dies.\"","Damian’s interest sharpened. \"So it lets people fight without holding back.\"","\"Exactly,\" Anna said. \"That’s why so many geniuses use it to test their strength, drill their techniques, and challenge opponents from other races. Outside the city, one mistake can cost you your life. Inside the Battle Space, a mistake only costs you the marks you wagered.\"","Revona smiled. \"That’s what makes it useful.\"","Anna nodded. \"There’s another important point too. The Battle Spaces across all the outer layer cities are connected. If you enter the Battle Space in Bloodstone City, you might run into someone from a completely different city. You’re not limited to opponents in this city alone.\"","Max’s eyes moved slightly. \"So the Battle Space connects the whole outer layer?\"","\"Only the outer layer,\" Anna corrected. \"The inner layer runs its own system, and the outer layer Battle Space can’t connect to it. But among outer layer cities, yeah, the Battle Spaces link up. That’s part of why rankings and reputations spread so fast. If someone performs too well inside the Battle Space, people from a bunch of cities might hear about it.\"","Max nodded slowly. He’d already read a brief description of the Battle Space in the information package, but he hadn’t paid it much attention at first. He’d seen plenty of illusion worlds, virtual arenas, and projection spaces before, so the concept itself didn’t surprise him. What genuinely interested him was the mark betting.","In the Battle Space, people couldn’t fight casually with nothing on the line. They had to bet marks. That single rule made every battle mean something. Win, and you gained marks without risking your life.","Lose, and you paid the price. For ordinary participants, that made the Battle Space a place of both opportunity and danger. For Max, it might turn out even more useful than he’d first thought.","His cultivation realm sat only at the 1st level of the Law Manifestation Realm. To almost everyone in the outer layer, that realm made him look weak. Honestly, it made him look like the easiest prey in the city.","Max could already picture what would happen if he walked into the Battle Space openly. Devils, dragons, angels, spirits, and maybe even some Primordials would come forward to challenge him.","To them, Max would look like free marks. But to Max, they’d be the same thing.","’It’s a good way to earn marks,’ Max thought calmly. A faint light passed through his eyes.","The Battle Space could turn into a perfect hunting ground for him. His true strength couldn’t be measured by his cultivation realm alone, and that made him extremely dangerous in a place where opponents judged people purely by numbers.","If others wanted to underestimate him, he’d let them. If they wanted to challenge him, he’d accept. If they wanted to hand him marks with their own hands, he had no reason to say no.","Anna noticed the look in his eyes and immediately narrowed her own. \"Max, why do I suddenly get the feeling you’re thinking of something troublesome?\""]},{"number":2047,"title":"Chapter 2047: Bregor","paragraphs":["Max looked at her with an innocent expression. \"I’m just thinking the Battle Space sounds useful.\"","Daniel, who’d been listening quietly nearby, suddenly smiled. \"It is useful. But only if you know what you’re doing.\"","Anna’s expression turned serious again. \"Don’t rush into it blindly. The Battle Space might not kill you, but it can expose you. If you show too much of your strength there, people outside will start paying attention.\"","Max understood exactly what she meant. The Battle Space protected life, but it didn’t protect secrets. Every technique he used, every power he revealed, every victory he earned could turn into information other people would buy, sell, and study.","In a place like the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, showing strength carelessly could get just as dangerous as showing weakness.","Still, the opportunity was real.","Just then, Daniel walked back toward them, his gaze moving across Max, Damian, Revona, and Anna before he spoke. \"They done?\"","Anna nodded. \"I think they’ve got the basics now.\"","\"Good,\" Daniel said. \"Then it’s time to move.\"","\"Move?\"","A cold sneer suddenly came from behind them.","Max and the others turned around at the same time.","A group of Dragon Race geniuses had shown up, blocking the path leading out of the Information Hall. There were several of them, all in humanoid form, though their dragon traits were impossible to miss. Scales covered their arms, necks, and parts of their faces like natural armor.","Some had curved horns rising from their heads, while others had long tails swaying behind them with a slow, dangerous rhythm. Their eyes were sharp and vertical, carrying the natural arrogance of ancient beasts who believed their bodies alone could suppress most opponents.","The one standing at the front gave off a particularly oppressive presence. His body stood tall and broad, dark bronze scales covering one side of his neck before spreading down toward his shoulder. His pupils were golden, his arms crossed over his chest, and his expression carried a lazy arrogance that made it obvious he wasn’t here for friendly conversation.","\"Daniel,\" the Dragon Race genius said, his gaze sweeping across Max, Damian, and Revona. \"These the three Primordial newcomers who came in this time?\"","Daniel’s expression stayed calm. \"What about them, Bregor?\"","’Bregor?’ Max’s eyes narrowed slightly at the name. He’d seen that name not long ago on the Bloodstone City Rankings. Bregor sat ranked eighth. Only one spot below Daniel.","That meant the dragon standing in front of them was one of the strongest figures in Bloodstone City. No wonder he’d dared to block Daniel’s group inside the Information Hall so openly. Even without attacking directly, his presence alone was enough to draw a crowd.","Some nearby participants slowed their steps. A few devils stopped watching the information screens and turned around with amused expressions.","Several angels glanced over with faint interest, while some Spirit Race members quietly stepped aside, clearly unwilling to get involved but curious enough to watch. In a place like Bloodstone City, a confrontation between the seventh and eighth ranked geniuses was enough to draw attention even without a fight breaking out.","Bregor smiled, showing sharp teeth. \"Nothing much. Was just thinking that since both our races got newcomers this time, why not make things a little interesting?\"","Daniel looked at him silently.","Bregor gestured toward the four Dragon Race newcomers behind him. \"How about we bet some marks on whose newcomers are better? Just your Primordial Race and my Dragon Race. Newcomers against newcomers. Should be fair enough.\"","Daniel didn’t answer right away. His gaze moved toward the four Dragon Race newcomers. All four sat at the 1st level of the Divine Lord Realm. Their cultivation clearly ran much higher than Max’s, and their dragon bloodline gave them naturally powerful bodies.","Against ordinary geniuses, any one of them would be extremely hard to deal with. But Damian and Revona weren’t ordinary either, and Max was an even stranger case.","After a moment, Daniel nodded. \"Sure.\"","Anna looked at him, a little surprised.","Daniel continued calmly, \"But our Primordial side only has three newcomers here, so we don’t need four battles. We’ll do three matches. Whichever side wins two takes the bet.\"","Bregor’s smile widened. \"Daniel, no wonder even some members of the Dragon Race respect you. You really do have nerve.\"","Daniel’s expression didn’t change. \"Bregor, we both know a small number of marks won’t help or hurt either of us much. If I win, it’s a bit of extra gain. If I lose, it won’t touch me.\"","\"You really are strange,\" Bregor said, shaking his head with a grin. \"Most people would at least pretend to care.\"","\"I only care when the amount’s actually worth caring about,\" Daniel replied.","Bregor laughed. \"Fine. Since you’re so relaxed about it, let’s make it three hundred Gold Marks.\"","The moment those words landed, several people nearby reacted. Three hundred Gold Marks wasn’t a small amount. Even for top-ranked geniuses, that wasn’t something most people would toss around casually for entertainment.","It was enough to buy valuable information, powerful resources, high-grade cultivation rooms, and access to plenty of special places in the outer layer. For newcomers, the value felt even more terrifying.","Anna’s brows furrowed slightly. Damian and Revona turned serious too.","Daniel, though, just looked at Bregor calmly.","Bregor continued, \"If my Dragon Race newcomers win two out of three matches, I get three hundred Gold Marks from you. If your Primordial newcomers win two out of three, you get three hundred Gold Marks from me.\"","\"Fine by me,\" Daniel said with a faint smile.","Bregor’s eyes flashed with satisfaction.","Daniel then turned to Anna, Max, Damian, and Revona. His gaze stayed calm, but a faint hint of interest showed through. \"So, how about it? You three willing to take the challenge?\"","Before Damian or Revona could speak, Max smiled. \"Sure,\" Max said calmly. \"It’ll be an easy win on my side.\"","For a moment, the air around them seemed to go quiet.","Anna stared at him.","Daniel looked at him in silence too.","Even Damian’s lips twitched slightly, while Revona blinked, like she was wondering if Max had actually just said that in front of Bregor and the Dragon Race newcomers."]},{"number":2048,"title":"Chapter 2048: Anna’s Advice!","paragraphs":["Anna finally snapped out of it and turned to Max with a stern look. \"What do you mean, easy win?\"","Max looked at her innocently. \"Exactly what I said.\"","Anna’s expression turned even more helpless. \"All four of them sit at the 1st level of the Divine Lord Realm, and you’re only at the 1st level of the Law Manifestation Realm. Where’s this confidence even coming from?\"","Max didn’t answer.","Anna pointed at Damian and Revona. \"Only Damian and Revona fight first. Let’s hope they win their matches so you don’t even have to fight.\"","Max smiled wryly. \"As you say.\"","Damian couldn’t help but smile seeing Max’s expression. He wasn’t sure whether Anna genuinely didn’t know Max’s real strength or was just too worried because of the realm gap, but Damian knew well enough that Max couldn’t be judged by cultivation alone.","Still, he didn’t explain anything. In a place like the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, the fewer people who understood Max’s true ability, the better.","Bregor looked at Max with clear amusement in his eyes.","\"A Law Manifestation Realm newcomer calling a battle against the Dragon Race an easy win,\" he said with a low laugh. \"Interesting. I knew Primordials were arrogant, but I didn’t know they’d gotten this entertaining.\"","The Dragon Race newcomers behind him laughed too.","One of them looked at Max with contempt. \"If he’s allowed to fight, I want him.\"","Another dragon grinned. \"No, let me take him. I’ve never crushed a Law Manifestation Realm participant in the Battle Space before.\"","The third dragon shook his head and said mockingly, \"Calling it a fight would be generous. It’ll be over before he even understands what happened.\"","Max listened quietly. His expression didn’t change.","Daniel glanced at him from the corner of his eye, and for some reason, that calmness on Max’s face left him a bit curious.","Most Law Manifestation Realm cultivators would’ve felt humiliated, scared, or angry under that kind of ridicule, especially facing Divine Lord Realm dragons. Max just stood there like he’d overheard a couple of kids arguing over a toy.","That calmness wasn’t simple.","Anna noticed it too, but she still sighed in frustration. \"Just don’t cause trouble before we even reach the Battle Space,\" she said.","Max nodded. \"I’ll try.\"","Anna narrowed her eyes. \"That answer doesn’t reassure me at all.\"","Revona covered a small smile, while Damian looked toward the Dragon Race newcomers with a sharper gaze. Since the challenge had already been accepted, there was no point dodging it now.","They were all new to the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage, but if they backed down right after entering Bloodstone City, their reputations would take a hit before they even got a chance to build one.","Daniel looked back at Bregor. \"Bet’s settled. Let’s head to the Battle Space.\"","Bregor smiled widely. \"Good. Hope your newcomers are as confident as that Law Manifestation Realm brat.\"","Daniel didn’t respond to the jab. He just turned and started walking.","Anna followed beside Max, still wearing the look of someone bracing for a headache. Damian and Revona walked behind them, both more serious than before. Bregor and the Dragon Race group followed with relaxed confidence, their mocking glances occasionally landing on Max, like they’d already decided he was the weak point of the Primordial side.","As they left the Information Hall, more and more people started noticing the movement. A bet between Daniel and Bregor wasn’t a small deal in Bloodstone City. Both of them sat in the top ten of the Bloodstone City Rankings, and their names carried real weight among the geniuses of the outer layer.","Daniel represented the Primordial side, while Bregor stood as one of the strongest Dragon Race figures stationed in the city. If ordinary participants placed a wager in the Battle Space, only a handful of curious people would bother watching.","But when two top-ranked geniuses decided to gamble three hundred Gold Marks on a battle between newcomers, the news spread through Bloodstone City almost instantly.","At first, only the people inside the Information Hall heard about it. Then the news hit the nearby streets. After that, it spread to the mark exchange halls, cultivation chambers, race bases, inns, weapon shops, and trial recruitment areas.","Before long, plenty of people knew Daniel and Bregor had made a bet, and that the Primordial newcomers would fight the Dragon Race newcomers in the Battle Space.","The amount involved made people even more interested. Three hundred Gold Marks wasn’t something ordinary participants could shrug off. Even for high-level Divine Lord Realm geniuses, it counted as a serious sum.","For newcomers, it felt almost unimaginable. A lot of people quickly realized this wasn’t just a casual contest between young participants. This was a public test between two races, and the result would shape how the newest batch of Primordial and Dragon Race geniuses got viewed in Bloodstone City.","By the time Daniel, Anna, Max, Damian, and Revona reached the Battle Space with Bregor and the Dragon Race newcomers, the area was already packed.","The Battle Space building stood enormous, shaped like a circular fortress at the center of a wide plaza, its walls built from black stone and carved with countless silver runes. Those runes pulsed with light, creating a faint barrier that wrapped around the entire structure.","Above the entrance, a massive projection floated in the air, showing ongoing battles between participants from different cities across the outer layer. Every strike, every movement, every win, and every loss showed up clearly for the crowd outside to watch.","People from all five races had gathered. Primordials stood in groups near one side of the plaza, their expressions calm but attentive. Devils watched with cold smiles, clearly hoping to see one side get humiliated.","Spirit Race members floated or stood quietly near the edges, their luminous eyes filled with curiosity. Angels gathered in elegant silence, golden halos glowing above their heads as they watched the arriving groups with unreadable expressions.","Dragon Race participants stood with their arms folded, scales gleaming under the strange light of the city as they looked toward Bregor’s group with open confidence."]},{"number":2049,"title":"Chapter 2049: Arrival of Shreya!","paragraphs":["Humans, elves, demons, and several lesser races mixed into the crowd too. Some had come purely for entertainment. Some had come to size up the newcomers’ strength. Some had come because Daniel and Bregor’s names were involved.","And some had come because they understood that information gathered from watching a battle like this could turn useful later.","Max’s gaze swept across the plaza, and he immediately noticed the crowd wasn’t made up only of ordinary participants. Several powerful auras hid among them, restrained but impossible to overlook.","These weren’t newcomers, and they weren’t simple spectators either. Their presence felt stable, deep, and dangerous.","Some stood quietly on balconies overlooking the Battle Space. Some sat in private viewing areas behind translucent formation screens. Some watched from the upper floors of nearby buildings, their eyes fixed on Daniel, Bregor, and the six newcomers about to fight.","Anna noticed Max looking around and lowered her voice. \"This bet drew more attention than I expected.\"","Daniel glanced toward one of the upper balconies and smiled faintly. \"Not surprising. Bregor and I both sit in the top ten. Even if we’re not fighting ourselves, people still want to see what kind of newcomers our sides pulled in this time.\"","Damian’s expression turned more serious. \"Those people up there aren’t ordinary.\"","\"They’re not,\" Daniel said calmly. \"Some are high-level figures from the race bases. Some are information brokers. Some are connected to the Bloodstone City Rankings. A few might even represent the stronger factions in the outer layer.\"","Just as Daniel finished speaking, a soft commotion suddenly spread from the far side of the plaza. The noise wasn’t loud at first, but it moved through the crowd fast, like a ripple crossing still water.","Several Spirit Race members standing near the edge of the Battle Space turned at the same time. The devils who’d been sneering went quieter. Even some Dragon Race geniuses shifted their gazes, and the angels standing beneath their golden halos looked toward the same direction with visible interest.","A woman from the Spirit Race walked into the plaza.","She stood in humanoid form, but her presence instantly set her apart from the ordinary spirits around her. Her long emerald hair flowed behind her like strands of living silk, and faint golden-green light moved across her skin in patterns resembling vines, leaves, and ancient runes.","Her eyes were clear and deep, carrying the calm of an old forest and the sharpness of a blade hidden beneath flowers. Every step she took landed light, yet the natural energy around her seemed to bend toward her willingly, as if the world itself recognized her.","Someone in the crowd drew in a sharp breath.","\"Shreya.\"","\"The fifth-ranked genius on the Bloodstone City Rankings actually showed up.\"","\"She rarely watches newcomer battles. Why’s she here?\"","The name spread through the plaza almost instantly.","Shreya. Ranked fifth on the Bloodstone City Rankings. A top genius of the Spirit Race. Her arrival shocked a lot of people, since someone at her level wouldn’t usually bother with a small battle between newcomers.","Even with Daniel and Bregor involved, this was still just a wager between their younger members. Yet Shreya had shown up in person, and that alone shifted the mood. The crowd stopped treating the event as simple entertainment. If the fifth-ranked genius had come to watch, this match clearly carried more weight than most people had first assumed.","Bregor’s eyes narrowed slightly when he saw her, but his smile didn’t fade.","Daniel looked toward Shreya too and gave a small nod from a distance.","Shreya returned the nod calmly, then moved to one of the raised viewing platforms beside the Battle Space. She didn’t speak, and she didn’t explain why she’d come. She just stood there, her gaze passing over Daniel, Bregor, Damian, Revona, and finally Max.","For a brief moment, her eyes paused on Max.","Max felt it clearly. Her gaze wasn’t mocking like the devils, and it wasn’t arrogant like the dragons. It came across quiet and searching, like she’d sensed something strange but hadn’t yet figured out what.","Then she looked away.","Anna’s expression turned even more serious. \"Even Shreya came. This is getting troublesome.\"","Max glanced toward the Spirit Race woman. \"She’s ranked fifth, right?\"","\"Yeah,\" Daniel answered calmly. \"Shreya of the Spirit Race. She’s stronger than Bregor and me.\"","Max’s eyes moved slightly. That one sentence said enough. If Daniel admitted it so openly, Shreya’s strength wasn’t just a matter of ranking. She genuinely stood above both him and Bregor in Bloodstone City.","The crowd grew louder after her arrival. More people stopped to watch. More messages went out. More powerful figures turned their attention toward the Battle Space. What had started as a provocation inside the Information Hall had now turned into one of the most watched events in Bloodstone City that day.","Bregor walked to the front of the Battle Space entrance and looked back at Daniel with a wide grin. \"Looks like everyone’s interested. Even Shreya decided to show up. Good. A bigger audience makes the bet more fun.\"","Daniel’s expression stayed relaxed. \"It also makes losing more embarrassing.\"","Bregor laughed. \"Then I hope your newcomers are ready.\"","\"They are,\" Daniel said.","Above the Battle Space, the floating projection shifted, and a new notice appeared in bright golden letters.","[Primordial Universe Newcomers vs Dragon Race Newcomers.]","[Three battles.]","[Best of three.]","[Wager: Three hundred Gold Marks.]","The moment the notice appeared, the entire plaza stirred again.","Max looked up at the glowing words. A faint smile touched his lips.","To others, this was a dangerous public stage. To him, it was his first real chance to see how the Battle Space worked, earn some marks, and measure the strength of Dragon Race newcomers without risking his life.","If the Dragon Race wanted to use this battle to test the Primordial newcomers, he had no reason to refuse. Let them test. He wanted to know how far the so-called geniuses of the Godslayer’s Pilgrimage could actually go, too."]},{"number":2050,"title":"Chapter 2050: Virgil’s Bet!","paragraphs":["As the excitement around the Battle Space kept rising, Daniel and Bregor walked to the registration platform and submitted the names of their three contestants.","The process was simple but solemn. Both of them placed their palms on the dark stone platform, and the bronze marks on their wrists lit up at the same time.","A moment later, several lines of light appeared in the air above the platform, recording the names of the participants, the races they represented, the number of battles, and the wager between the two sides.","Once registration wrapped up, the notice above the Battle Space glowed even brighter, and the crowd outside stirred again.","Daniel returned to Max, Damian, and Revona. His expression stayed calm as he looked at the three of them.","\"Revona, you’re up first. Damian, you go second. Max, you fight last.\"","The three of them nodded.","Max didn’t object, though he quietly figured he might not even need to fight if Revona and Damian did well.","Both of them were geniuses chosen by the Primordial Race, and their strength wasn’t ordinary. If they won the first two battles, the third wouldn’t even matter.","Still, Max didn’t underestimate the Dragon Race. ’The Dragon Race isn’t something anyone should take lightly,’ Max thought.","He knew this better than most. After all, he himself carried the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline, and because of that, he understood how terrifying a true dragon body could be.","Even in humanoid form, Dragon Race members had monstrous vitality, overwhelming defenses, explosive strength, and instincts far sharper than ordinary cultivators. If Damian and Revona judged them only by cultivation level, they might take a loss before they even realized what happened.","Anna seemed to share the same worry. She stepped closer to the three of them and lowered her voice. \"Listen carefully. Dragon Race members aren’t like ordinary opponents. Their bodies are their biggest advantage. Their scales can block attacks that would injure anyone else, their bloodline gives them powerful recovery, and their physical strength alone can suppress enemies before a technique even gets used.\"","Revona listened with a serious expression.","Damian focused on her words too.","Anna continued, \"Don’t clash with them carelessly in close combat unless you’re confident in your own body. Their defense runs extremely strong, but that doesn’t mean they have no weaknesses. Their movements hit hard but land heavy when they lean on brute force, and a lot of dragons get arrogant because of their natural strength. Make them overextend. Go for the joints, eyes, throat, and anywhere their scales run thinner. If they push their transformation further, don’t just stand there and try to endure it. Keep moving.\"","Daniel added from the side, \"Also keep in mind this is the Battle Space. You won’t actually die inside it, but the pain, pressure, and exhaustion will still feel real. Don’t relax just because it’s virtual. A lot of newcomers lose because they treat it like a game.\"","Revona smiled faintly. \"Understood.\"","Damian nodded. \"I’ll keep that in mind.\"","Max stayed silent, but his gaze drifted toward the Dragon Race side.","At that moment, one of the Dragon Race newcomers stepped forward. He stood tall and muscular, with dark green scales covering both arms and spreading up the side of his neck.","Two short horns curved from his forehead, and his golden vertical pupils carried a fierce confidence. His aura sat firmly at the 1st level of the Divine Lord Realm, and even among the four Dragon Race newcomers, his presence didn’t come off weak.","He looked toward the Primordial side and spoke loud enough for the crowd around him to hear. \"I’m Virgil. I’ll fight first. Who’s my opponent?\"","Revona stepped forward with a light smile. Her silver hair moved gently behind her, and her expression stayed composed even under the crowd’s pressure.","\"That’d be me,\" she said. \"I’m Revona.\"","Virgil studied her for a moment before nodding. \"Revona, huh? Good.\"","Then a grin crossed his face. \"Since we’re already fighting, how about we make it more interesting?\"","Revona raised a brow. \"What do you mean?\"","\"Let’s put a personal bet on our battle,\" Virgil said.","The crowd around them perked up immediately.","Revona didn’t refuse right away. \"How much are you thinking?\"","Virgil lifted his wrist, and the bronze mark on it glowed faintly. \"Two hundred Bronze Marks.\"","Revona’s eyes widened slightly. Two hundred Bronze Marks wasn’t a small amount for a newcomer. Even though she’d just earned three hundred and twenty-five Bronze Marks from the Battle Space, risking two hundred of them on a single fight still counted as a bold move.","Damian showed a trace of surprise too, and even Max looked at Virgil with a bit more interest.","This dragon carried real confidence. Or maybe he was just arrogant.","Revona looked at him for a few breaths. Then she smiled.","\"Fine,\" she said. \"Don’t regret it later.\"","Virgil’s grin widened. \"That should be my line.\"","The registration platform responded to their agreement right away. Two beams of bronze light dropped from the air and connected to the marks on their wrists. The numbers on both marks flickered briefly before the Battle Space itself recorded the wager.","A new line appeared on the floating notice above the arena.","[First Battle: Revona of the Primordial Universe against Virgil of the Dragon Race.]","[Personal Wager: Two hundred Bronze Marks.]","The crowd grew even louder. Some Primordials looked at Revona with hope. The Dragon Race members wore confident expressions, clearly believing Virgil’s win was already locked in. Devils sneered, ready to enjoy the show, while angels and spirits watched with quiet interest.","On the raised platform, Shreya’s luminous eyes shifted toward Revona and Virgil too, like she wanted to see if these newcomers were worth remembering.","Then the runes around the Battle Space began to shine. A circular formation opened beneath Revona’s feet. At almost the same moment, another formation appeared beneath Virgil.","Revona turned her head slightly and glanced once at Max and Damian, her smile still calm. \"I’ll be back after I win.\"","Damian nodded. \"Be careful.\"","Max looked at her and said, \"Don’t underestimate his body.\"","\"I know,\" Revona replied.","Virgil laughed from the other side. \"You’ve still got time to worry about yourself.\""]}]);
